Khmer Civilization Expert: What does the Royal Ceremony for the Release of Ghosts Mean?
(Phnom Penh): Khmer civilization expert, Mr. Rath Sandab, said that during the Pchum Ben festival, there is a ceremony for the King to release ghosts or loosen ghosts, because in his opinion, it is better to have a normal earth. Because if you die without karma and ascend to heaven, no matter, because the situation has improved, or at least normalized.
If this is the case for the King, the release of the ghost or the release of the ghost is in the right view, lest the ghost is not yet normal to be normal according to the dharma path. It means, "For the King to release the ghost or to loosen the ghost, this is a good idea to think or seek to normalize things so that everything follows the path of Dharma."
According to Buddhism, death is not the end of man, if it is understood that death is the end, then there is no need for a funeral. This means that death occurs automatically, and the survivors have to work hard to orient the body to the path of death.
It is believed that after death their souls will be taken to hell for 15 days, with four angels, the king's messengers, the kings of hell, judging the good and the bad. The dead.
