Factory worker wins 100 million Riel from Carabao energy drink
(Phnom Penh): A woman who is working as a garment factory worker in Phnom Penh is lucky to win 100 million Riel from Carabao energy drink.
The lucky woman, Mak Srim, 35, is currently working as a garment factory worker and living in a rented room in Trapeang Thleung village, Choam Chao commune, Por Senchey district, Phnom Penh, and has two dependent children.
Speaking to the team that handed over 100 million Riel to her house, Ms. Mak Srim confirmed that she was born in Kampong Thom province, Baray district, but due to the difficult living conditions of her family, she came to live in Phnom Penh to serve Work as garment workers, both husband and wife.
She said that although the couple had a job, but still have some difficulties in the family, especially some private debt. Last week, when she took a break from work at the factory, she bought a can of Carabao drink from a vendor who worked with her at the factory, just to eat when she was tired. .
When it was dug up, there was a prize in the earring. Suddenly, she was so excited that she called everyone around her to help look and inform the company through the existing phone number and earring.
She added that the 100 million riel is very important for the family, that after receiving the prize money, she will use it to build debt and leave some to build a house in her hometown and buy farmland. Grow crops to sustain future livelihoods.
* Please note: For real prizes, only on the cans with Khmer letters as a mark. Drugs destroy you and your family! Nationwide anti-drug campaign on September 26: 7 cases cracked, 12 arrested
