UN human rights ombudsman against Sam Rainsy on plot to overthrow government
(Phnom Penh): The United Nations Special Rapporteur on Human Rights, Rona Smith, has spoken out against Sam Rainsy over his plan to mobilize people and the armed forces to overthrow the government of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Rona Smith's opposition took place at the 42nd session of the UN Human Rights Council in Geneva, Switzerland, on September 25.
During the meeting, Ms. Rona Smith stated that "Mr. Sam Rainsy, co-founder of the Cambodia National Rescue Party, who has been living in exile since 2015, has continued to use hostile language against Prime Minister Hun Sen and others, including calling on the people "Cambodia is overthrowing the government, which I certainly do not support."
Sam Rainsy, a convicted prisoner, recently announced that he would return to Cambodia on November 9, 2019. With the announcement of his return to prison, the prisoner acted to call for the people's armed forces to rise up and overthrow the Royal Government of Cambodia. The convict's announcement was considered a legitimate coup d'etat by the government, which was against Cambodian law.
This act led to strong reactions and opposition from the Cambodian people because it was seen as an act leading to war in Cambodia. However, the Royal Government of Cambodia and law enforcement police officers have already announced to enforce the law on this prisoner if he really returns to Cambodia.
