Former oil tycoon Venezuela has plunged into a deep political and economic crisis, with more than 3.6 million people fleeing the country since 2016 to rebuild their lives and escape. Violence and famine. International Analysis: Will Donald Trump be the first president in US history to be ousted?
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - Democrat lawmakers have launched a formal investigation into the impeachment or ousting of Donald Trump, accusing him of seeking support. Overseas to defeat his rival Joe Biden before the 2020 US presidential election.
* What is the investigation to prosecute the President?
The investigation is the first step in the process of prosecuting or ousting the president. In this regard, US lawmakers need to investigate whether Trump actually committed any serious crimes that do not qualify him to continue as president.
* How does this investigation work?
Who can accuse the President of the United States?
Those who have the power to accuse the president are both houses of the US Congress (Senate and House of Representatives). In particular, the current Democrat-controlled House of Representatives can vote to accuse a president of committing a serious crime. But this is not easy, because the Republicans will not vote against each other.
Traditionally, Republican senators have never voted against each other, and it can be expected that they will not vote against Donald Trump for fear of tarnishing the party's image as a whole. On Monday, most of the Republicans had already come forward to defend Tram. Today, the US Senate is controlled by the Republican Party.
Can Donald Trump run in the 2020 election despite formal charges?
If Donald Trump is formally charged or ousted by the House of Representatives, he will still be able to run in the election. But for example, if he is ousted, it is very difficult to say because it never happened, so he can only rely on the US Constitution.
