During the visit, a delegation from the two countries' Ministries of Justice discussed a draft treaty on "transfer of prisoners" and signed a draft treaty on "legal aid in the field of criminal justice" between the two countries. Cambodia and Russia as well.
Kim Santepheap, a spokesman for the Ministry of Justice, said the results of the signing of the agreement came from nearly two years of hard work.
In the past, Cambodia and Russia have already had contacts in the field of justice, but only as an exchange of delegations to visit each other. In addition, both sides also have some technical assistance. Technical assistance is the implementation of cooperation in the field of justice.
According to Kim Santepheap, through this agreement, the cooperation in the field of criminal justice between Cambodia and Russia will be closer and smoother in helping each other. Cambodia has only signed such an agreement with Vietnam, while Russia is the second country.
