Asian Development Bank: Cambodia's economy will continue to achieve strong growth this year
"With the uncertainty of the growing global business environment and its impact on services such as tourism, Cambodia urgently needs a diversification strategy that focuses on what is appropriate for itself and focuses on what is right for it," she said. "Higher value-added products and services."
The ADB Country Director for Cambodia said that this would reduce the risks posed by lending to the growing real estate sector, developing a more skilled and productive workforce to maintain balance. With rising wages and attracting high quality capital investment, all of which also requires good governance and strong institutions.
The report identifies risks to production that could be affected by climate change, the ADB said in a statement. Drought, which occurred during the first half of the year, slowed down agricultural and fisheries production, reducing economic growth in agriculture by 1.1 percent for the year.
Growth in the industrial sector was strong due to the rapid growth of garment, footwear, especially travel goods, which led the ADB to raise its forecast from April 10 to 10.6 percent for the sector. This.
Growth in imports was faster than expected, despite strong exports of goods and tourist arrivals. Therefore, the current account deficit (excluding grants) is expected to widen in the forecast period.
The deficit is financed by inflows of foreign direct investment, which will continue to accumulate about $ 12.3 billion in international reserves by the end of this year, covering six months' import costs.
Due to lower fuel prices and a slight increase in food prices, inflation was as low as 1.4 percent at the end of June compared to the same period in 2018 and is expected to average 2.2 percent for the year. 2019.
The ADB is committed to bringing environmental, resilient and sustainable prosperity to the Asia-Pacific region and, at the same time, continuing to sustain its efforts to eradicate poverty.
