(Phnom Penh): A spokesman for the National Gendarmerie on September 26, 2019 issued a press release clarifying and clarifying the allegations of five days of detention for torture and arrest. Imprisoned in Banteay Meanchey province. This is according to an explanation received by Fresh News this morning.
A spokesman for the Royal Gendarmerie confirmed that after seeing this information, General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, ordered Brigadier General Ung Depot, Deputy Commissioner for Crime Investigation and Suppression. The National Gendarmerie immediately inspected the implementation of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie procedures to find out the truth.
As a result of the investigation, it was found that the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie Judicial Police officers did not follow the wrong procedure in the case of aggravated theft (burglary, burglary) which took place on the night of April 5. In 2019, Thong Ratha's house is located at Kilometer 4 Village, Sangkat Phsar Kandal, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
The arrest of the suspect, Tem Veasna, was carried out in accordance with the procedures set out in Article 96 "Detention" and Article 97 "Record of Detention". This implementation is under the authority of the arrest warrant issued by Mr. Meas Chanpiseth, Prosecutor of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Prosecutor's Office No. 07, dated 26 June 2019.
Regarding the detention of the suspects at the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie Command, due to the fact that the prosecution and the investigating judge continued the interrogation procedure until the provisional detention order was issued, the experts sent the accused to the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Prison.
According to the answers of the suspects during the judicial police officers, the prosecution and the defendants during the interrogation by the investigating judge with lawyer In Yoeun accompanied and signed the transcript, no charges were filed against the police officers. Justice does not torture or misrepresent the procedure for detention or annulment.
