Find out: What do you know about the Iranian regime facing major problems with the United States?
The current president of Iran is Hassan Rouhani. Hassan Rouhani was first elected in 2013 with 51 percent of the vote, and was re-elected in 2017.
Sura Council (National Assembly) This council is a legislative and oversight council with 290 seats and a term of 4 years. The council has the right to make laws within the framework of the constitution and to summon and question ministers as well as the president.
At the same time, the Sura Council has the right to grant or withdraw the trust of the government and ratify international treaties or agreements, but is under the control of the Guardian Council.
Judicial power The President of the judiciary is directly appointed by the Supreme Leader of Iran for a five-year term. And the President of the Court appoints the members of the Supreme Court, the highest authority in the country.
8. The Supreme National Security Council, in accordance with Article 176 of the Iranian Constitution, states that the Council has the mission of defending the Islamic Revolution, the territorial integrity and sovereignty of the country.
The council is made up of the president, the speaker of parliament, the president of the judiciary and the commander of the armed forces, the minister of foreign affairs, the interior minister, the director of intelligence, as well as the commander of the Iranian Revolutionary Guards.
9. Armed Forces The Iranian Armed Forces are divided into two categories. One is the regular army (Republic of Iran) under the command of the Ministry of Defense and the other is the Iranian Revolutionary Guards. The latter category is under the direct command of Iran's supreme leader.
According to the Iranian Constitution, the Armed Forces of the Republic of Iran is responsible for safeguarding national independence, territorial integrity and maintaining order, while the Iranian Revolutionary Guards are responsible for maintaining their revolution and achievements and defending the Islamic Republic, both inside and outside the country, and preventing foreign interference. And prevent military coups.
