(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has confirmed that all applications for scholarship and teacher examination at all levels are not required to include a provisional certificate in the application. This is according to the announcement that Fresh News received on September 25, 2019.
According to the Ministry of Education, every year, the Ministry observes that students, after passing the high school diploma exam (Bakdup), rush to apply for a provisional high school diploma to be used for various reasons and also to be legalized. More.
For the convenience of students who are candidates for the Baccalaureate exam on August 19, 2019, the Ministry would like to inform that in completing the application form for admission to higher education institutions, application for admission to higher education institutions, application for scholarships, as well as The Ministry of Education does not require the provisional certificate to be included in the application form for all levels of teacher examinations.
The Ministry of Education also stated that students who are candidates for the high school diploma exam on August 19, 2019 can submit a temporary certificate after higher education or pedagogical school after a period of enrollment.
