Cambodia Celebrates World Tourism Day under the theme "Tourism and Employment: A Better Future for All of Us"
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia has designated Kampot Province as the venue to celebrate World Tourism Day 2019 under the theme "Tourism and Employment: A Better Future for All of Us" on September 25, the Ministry of Tourism together with the provincial administration Kampot has co-organized this event by disseminating the latest situation related to global, regional and national tourism.
Tith Chantha, Acting Minister of Tourism, said that the World Tourism Day aims to promote new ideas and share experiences of tourism development around the world in order to promote tourism development in response to current global trends. And the future.
He said that in 2019, the World Tourism Organization has set this day under the theme "Tourism and employment: a better future for all of us" which will be officially held in New Delhi, India on the 27th. September 2029 will be followed by a forum to discuss work and skills in the tourism sector.
The day will also provide recommendations to member countries of the World Tourism Organization in formulating tourism development policies towards sustainable growth, in particular, set out models and approaches to education, training, tourism skills and work to meet the needs of Tourism in line with the trend of globalization, increasing environmental concern and increasing competition between destinations in the context of the digital age.
In 2018, despite trade wars between some countries, the tourism sector continued to grow significantly, with 1.4 billion international tourists visiting the world at a rate of 5% higher than the forecast. .
In particular, in the ASEAN region, international tourism in 2018 increased to 135 million with a growth rate of 7.6%, of which ASEAN domestic tourism accounted for about 40%. ASEAN tourism creates about 30 million direct jobs and contributes about 10% of GDP. ASEAN as a whole hopes to maintain 7-8% growth in 2019.
In order to achieve the above vision, the Ministry of Tourism has been actively implementing four strategic angles, including: 1: Creating and promoting new products 2: Improving the quality of services through a campaign, a standard service 3: Developing human resources through a campaign One employee per skill.4: Smart Tourism development.
In line with the attention of the world, the Ministry of Tourism has been giving high priority to human resource development and considered as the core to support sustainable growth and contribute to the achievement of sustainable development.
At the same time, Mr. Tith Chantha also gave some suggestions in the ceremony, including:
1: 2019 marks the year that the global economy could slow down due to the US-China trade war, Britain's exit from the European Union, the tense international political situation, the threat of war in the Middle East, demonstrations In Hong Kong and so on. These factors may have a direct or indirect effect on world tourism, as well as some tourist destinations.
2: The Ministry of Tourism will continue to make more efforts on training and strengthening the capacity of working youth as well as students who are studying to achieve high capacity in accordance with national and ASEAN curriculum standards through continuous submission and implementation. One Person Skills Campaign and Strategic Plan for Human Resource Development in Tourism 2017-2025.
3: Tourism vocational education and training institutions and training programs should update their curriculum regularly to meet the rapidly changing needs of the skills market, that is, the skills training approach must also focus on self-empowerment. In adapting to new trends in the future.
4: All tourism businesses must pay more attention to the capacity building of their staff, with a program to develop skills and retain talent to be the basis for strengthening the competitive advantage of it. The Ministry of Interior will conduct a census of associations and non-governmental organizations from October 10 to November 29.
