Cambodian Red Cross Donates 3 Houses to People in Need
(Kampong Thom): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, built 3 new houses for 3 needy and elderly families living in Tbong Krapeu village, Kor Koh commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province. The donation was made through Ms. Khieu Sina Chea Chanto, Honorary Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Kampong Thom Province.
The new house, a gift from Samdech Kittipritthbandit, was officially announced by Ms. Khieu Sina Chea Chanto on September 24, 2019.
Poor people and the elderly who received new houses from these three families: First: Mrs. Tith Kea, second: Mrs. It On, and third: Mrs. Men, all three families live in Tbong Krapeu village, Ka Koh commune. The house is made of galvanized iron, 6 meters long and 4 meters wide, each worth 1,200 US dollars.
Ms. Khieu Sina stated that in fact, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit always take care of the well-being of the people who are always in need, especially the families of widows, the elderly and orphans. Apparently, like the three houses that were built for the people now, it is clear that all the time, the two princes live with the well-being of the people in all circumstances.
She said that you must live in hope and continue to strive as long as Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, President of the Cambodian Red Cross.
It should be noted that since 2008, through Ms. Khieu Sina, Samdech Kittipritthbandit has helped build 336 houses for the poor, the elderly and the families of widows in Santuk district.
