National Road Safety Committee conducts an education campaign to disseminate traffic laws on the occasion of Pchum Ben
(Phnom Penh): Seeing that road traffic accidents continue to occur every day, causing deaths, injuries, disabilities and leaving a tragic tragedy, the National Road Safety Committee has educated and disseminated road traffic laws. Land on the occasion of Pchum Ben.
These accidents have become a serious social and national development challenge. In addition to having a direct negative impact on victims, the loss of families, traffic accidents also cause significant financial and human resource losses, totaling approximately $ 350 million annually.
Ms. Mon Manvi, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and Secretary General of the National Road Safety Committee, said at the launch ceremony on the morning of September 25 that the campaign was carried out on all national roads to raise awareness. You travel to your hometown to pay attention when traveling.
She added that the Royal Government has also deployed law enforcement forces to maintain and protect the security and order of some people at the Pchum Ben festival. "Education and outreach work together with maintaining order, so the law enforcement officials are tired of maintaining order," she said. "So when there is order, we are free from traffic accidents."
At the same time, she also called on people as well as travelers to be right, respect traffic lights, do not drive fast, do not overtake in dangerous situations. Respect for priority is to respect the highway. Ask drivers, both small and large, to be polite in respecting driver rights and ethics.
"The restriction principle is that we do not allow anyone not to wear a helmet, to be fined and to have him wear a helmet and restrict drivers who do not wear seat belts until nightfall, we have the power to shoot or control," he said. That special speed is on National Road No. 4 and No. 5. When we put it, we see that the number of traffic accidents must be reduced. He said that when the authorities checked the alcohol and those who do not obey the traffic law.
At the same time, the deputy director of the department said that in recent weeks, traffic accidents have not decreased, sometimes in groups, and less than 1% of those who died were not wearing helmets.
According to the Road Traffic Accident and Victim Information System, nearly 2,000 people are killed and nearly 10,000 injured in road accidents each year.
(Takeo): Takeo Provincial Governor Mr. Ouch Phea this morning, September 25, 2019, led more than 300 government officials, units around the province and the Armed Forces to help the flood victims to prevent flooding. Let the waves break the road in Borey Chulsar commune, which is an important road to Borey Chulsar district hall.
Speaking on that occasion, the Governor of Takeo Province instructed the authorities at all levels, especially local authorities must be prepared to help prevent flooding or flooding of the Mekong River through activities such as today that we protect First, do not let the waves break the road to Borey Chul District Hall, which will lead to consequences for people who cross this road to receive services at the district hall.
Mr. Ouch Phea added that in addition to preparing to help the people affected by the floods, the authorities must help prevent the flooding of major roads in their locality through the bagging or sanding. The bank should not collapse the road and prevent it from affecting the houses of the people, and if there is a problem, the local authorities must act immediately to help the people in time.
At the same time, the governor of Takeo province also instructed the local authorities to educate the people living along the lake to be very careful about the rising river, especially children, because when people neglect it, it will make children Drowning is inevitable. In addition, the relevant authorities must educate people about living hygienically by drinking clean water or boiled water.
