Ministry of Tourism-Kep Provincial Administration to Turn Dolphin Street into Food Street
(Kep): Dolphin Street near the coast of Kep Province will become a food street as this morning, September 25, 2019, the Ministry of Tourism, National Committee for Clean City Assessment in collaboration with Kep Provincial Administration organized a dissemination workshop Contest program "Architecture work, food street in Kep province".
The workshop was chaired by Mr. Kim Sereyrath, Director of Accommodation Management Service, Tourism and Food and Mr. Prum Kunthi, Deputy Governor of Kep Province, and was attended by civil servants, members of the Kep Clean City Assessment Committee, Departments under the Provincial Administration. Kep and tour operators in Kep province, a total of about 100 people.
At the same time, professional officials of the Ministry of Tourism also presented:
At the same time, the director of the department proposed to the Kep provincial administration as well as the workshop on two important points, including:
1: Please, Kep Provincial Department of Tourism continue to disseminate to tour operators to join the Kep Provincial Administration as well as the Kep City Administration to participate in organizing better Kep Food Street.
2: Request the Kep Provincial Administration to continue to cooperate with the National Committee for the Evaluation of Clean Cities in order to establish a "Kep Food Street" as soon as possible.
It should be noted that for the preparation of Kep food street, Kep provincial administration has determined to select Dolphin Street as a food street in Kep province.
