On the occasion of the inauguration of the Constituent Assembly, all 120 members of the Constituent Assembly, who had just been elected on May 23-28, 1993, who attended the first session on June 14, 1993, unanimously decided. On behalf of all Cambodians as follows (3):
First, to give justice to His Majesty the King Father on this sacred occasion by annulling the coup d'état of March 18, 1970, which was committed in violation of the Constitution and the will of the people. At that time, he was considered the same head of state from the beginning of 1970 until now without interruption.
Second, to His Majesty the King Father of the Nation as a sacred place with full power and all the power in the position of Head of State so that he may have sufficient ability to save the nation and bring our nation back to the prosperity as it was today. Sangkum Reastr Niyum.
At its first plenary session on June 30, 1993, the Constituent Assembly established a Standing Committee to draft the Constitution. The main task of the committee is to finalize the draft constitution within three months, as stipulated in the Paris Agreement. The composition of this committee is as follows:
Immediately after its inception, the committee was tasked with drafting a new constitution in line with the Paris Agreement. However, in drafting this constitution, the committee must be based on two fundamental principles:
On June 18, 1993, Samdech Norodom Sihanouk made six recommendations to the Constituent Assembly as a principle in drafting Cambodia's future constitution. Those principles are as follows:
(3) There must be a strict separation of powers (legislative, executive and judicial). The judiciary must be absolutely independent of the government and political parties.
(4) Cambodia does not have military alliances with any country and does not allow foreign military bases or weapons bases on its territory. Cambodia's defense sector is united. Cambodia has always opposed the retention, production, and use of nuclear or veterinary weapons.
(5) Buddhism is the state religion. Islam and Christianity are officially recognized and protected by the state. Freedom of religion must always exist in Cambodia.
(6) - Cambodia absolutely avoids interference in the internal affairs of other countries and also does not allow other countries to interfere in its internal affairs. Cambodia will make friends with all countries and peoples of the world that respect its sovereignty, independence, neutrality, non-alignment, territorial integrity in its 1969 land and sea borders. Always ban the deployment of troops abroad.
Those principles are (4): (1) - The Constitution is the supreme law of the country. Amendments to the Constitution can only be made if there is an authoritarian system that deals with the approval of the legislature, a referendum, or by any of these means.
(3) The Constitution shall declare the status of Cambodia as a sovereign, independent and neutral state and the unity of the Cambodian people.
(4) The Constitution shall declare that Cambodia will implement a system of liberal democracy on a multi-party basis. The Constitution shall authorize the right to vote and to stand for election by universal and equal suffrage. The Constitution shall allow for secret elections, requiring sufficient and appropriate forms of voting to organize and participate in the electoral process.
(5) To establish an independent court that has the power to exercise the rights enshrined in the Constitution.
After three months of work, the Constituent Assembly has finalized the drafting of Cambodia's future constitution. Two different draft constitutions were submitted to Samdech Norodom Sihanouk for approval before approval.
On September 15, 1993, the Constituent Assembly began debating and approving a new Cambodian constitution to bring peace, stability, and national unity to the redevelopment of society after more than two decades of war. This is a journey on a detour where all the passengers are former dead and enemies on the battlefield and in the political arena.
The vote to approve the constitution was held in secret and freely. As a result, out of 120 members of the Constituent Assembly, 113 voted in favor, 5 against and 2 abstentions, and the final constitution was submitted to the King for signature on 24 September. 1993.
Samdech Norodom Sihanouk announced: "From September 24 (1993) onwards, we dare to claim that Cambodia will receive a constitution with the best democracy, broad freedom and the motherland of Cambodia will enter proudly. The most democratic country in the world.
"From now on, we, the Khmer people, adhere to a constitutional monarchy, democracy, freedom and pluralism," said Son San on behalf of all lawmakers.
Mr. Yasushi Akashi expressed his belief that Samdech Norodom Sihanouk would remain an essential leader of the nation and a great mediator and a mediator for the benefit of the country. Mr. Yasushi Akashi sees Cambodia as an interesting indicator for the world because difficult problems can be solved. Cambodia will be a great role model and example for all UN member states.
