The two fundamental principles of the Cambodian Constitution are constitutional monarchy and liberal multi-party democracy. Amending these two fundamental principles is tantamount to killing the constitution, or in other words, a constitutional coup.
The new Article 155 of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia states that "revision or amendment of the Constitution is not possible if it affects the system of liberal democracy, pluralism and monarchy based on the Constitution."
"These two points are fundamental principles of democracy, the rule of law in Cambodia, and the changes that affect these two principles can lead to chaos as well as catastrophe for our society, as we have seen the experience of catastrophic civil war," he said. "That happened in the history of Cambodia, which came out of the transformation of these two principles."
"Demands or amendments that affect these two fundamental principles can be considered constitutional coups," he said.
