"Congratulations on the 26th anniversary of the promulgation of the Cambodian Constitution. September 24 is the 26th anniversary of the official promulgation of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Starting from the Paris Agreement on a Joint Resolution to End the Cambodian Crisis, which took place on October 23, 1991, Cambodia was transformed into a new historical turning point with internal consensus on resolving political issues by Cambodia. Elections were held in May 1993 with the support of the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization (UNTAC). Then the National Constitution was made into history in 1993.
On September 24, 1993, in the Great Temple of Deva Vinich in the Royal Palace, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the former King Father, signed the Royal Decree promulgating the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Official. September 24 is the birthday of the 1993 Constitution, which in 2019 is the 26-year-old Constitution of Cambodia.
