(China): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that the National Bank of Cambodia will continue to contribute to strengthening good cooperation with ASEAN members and China to develop the financial sector of the two regions.
Mr. Chea Chanto made the remarks as he led a delegation from the National Bank of Cambodia to the 11th China-ASEAN Summit on "Cooperation and Development of the Financial Sector" and the International Forum on "Internationalization". The yuan and the use of member countries' currencies for settlement ”in Nanning, China.
The two conferences were held on the occasion of the 16th China-ASEAN Expo in Nanning, with the aim of enhancing China-ASEAN cooperation in the financial sector to support the development of the financial sector, investment, trade and economic relations. Of both regions.
Mr. Chea Chanto was invited to speak at the two forums, in which he praised the recent development of economic and financial cooperation in the field of open and transparent banking. There is regional integration, especially within the framework of ASEAN and ASEAN + 3.
Mr. Chea Chanto stressed that the National Bank of Cambodia has good cooperation and strengthened integration with China and ASEAN members. In particular, in 2017, the National Bank of Cambodia and the Central Bank of China allowed the riel to be traded on the interbank market of Guangxi Zhou province, and the riel and the yuan were allowed to be used for trade and investment between China and Cambodia.
Mr. Chea Chanto was also honored to sign an agreement to strengthen cooperation between Chinese financial institutions and ASEAN members.
