WASHINGTON (Reuters) - US President Donald Trump has said a fourth summit with North Korean leader Kim Jong Un could be held soon despite the stalemate over nuclear disarmament talks. This was released by Yonhap News Agency on Tuesday morning, September 24, 2019.
Donald Trump made the remarks when he arrived at the UN headquarters in New York on Monday to attend the UN General Assembly summit in response to questions from reporters. Do you plan to meet Kim again? "The meeting is likely to take place soon," Trump said briefly. But he did not elaborate.
In recent months, North Korea has test-fired a series of missiles, but Trump has maintained good relations with Kim Jong Un. Tram and Kim have met three times before, in Singapore in June 2018, in Hanoi, Vietnam in late February, and the last time in the inter-Korean demilitarized zone in June 2019. .
