The following is the history of the establishment of the Constitution in Cambodia since 1947:
* First Constitution: The first Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia has 12 chapters and 122 articles and was adopted on May 6, 1947. The 1947 constitution is a constitutional one, but this constitution does not change the form of leadership, only some changes according to the actual situation.
* Second Constitution: is the Constitution of the Khmer Republic with 11 chapters and 121 articles and was adopted on May 10, 1972. This constitution changed the political system from a constitutional monarchy to a US-style republic.
* Third Constitution: is the Constitution of Democratic Kampuchea, which has 21 articles, divided into 16 chapters, and was adopted on January 5, 1976. The Constitution of Democratic Kampuchea, which transformed the regime in Cambodia from a republic to a communist dictatorship, massacred its own people for three years, eight months and 20 days.
* Fourth Constitution: The Constitution of the People's Republic of Democratic Kampuchea has 93 articles and 10 chapters and was promulgated by Decree No. 01K dated June 25, 1981.
5th Constitution: On April 30, 1989, the National Assembly of the People's Republic of Kampuchea amended the Constitution by changing the name of Cambodia from the People's Republic of Kampuchea to the State of Cambodia in Article 4 of the Constitution states: Cambodia implements a multi-party political system. This constitution has 93 articles and 10 chapters.
After the election, the Constituent Assembly was active until September 21, 1993, approving the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia by 97% of the votes, and was officially promulgated by the King of Cambodia, King Norodom Sihanouk. Royal Kram, dated September 24, 1993.
