Russey Keo district administration hopes to believe in the spirit and generosity of a shared culture. All donations are kindly requested to be handed over to the Inter-sectoral Office and the Office of Administration and Finance at Russey Keo District Office every working hour. Honorary Dr. Khuon Sodary Introduces Cambodian Southeast Asian Youth Ship Delegation to Promote Cambodia's Prestige on the International Stage
(Phnom Penh): The Honorary Dr. Khuon Sodary, Second Vice President of the National Assembly, on September 23, 2019, expressed her hope and confidence that the delegation of the Cambodian Southeast Asian Youth Ship will be successful for the country after returning. From the program "46th Southeast Asian Youth Ship and Japan SSEAYP" in Japan, Singapore, Myanmar, Malaysia and Vietnam, especially to strengthen, expand and promote Cambodia's prestige on the international stage.
This warning and encouragement was made on the occasion that the Second Vice President of the National Assembly allowed the youth delegation led by Mr. Srang Kimly, President of the Cambodian Southeast Asian Youth Ship Association to pay a courtesy call and ask for recommendations and wisdom from all angles. When going out to attend the above program. This program lasts for 52 days from October 24 to December 13, 2019.
Please be informed that 29 young Cambodians will participate in the 46th Southeast Asian Youth Ship Program from October 24 to December 13, 2019.
At the same time, young people will be able to expand their knowledge as well as their vision of the world, which is the path to leadership in their various fields that contribute to the development of youth and society. Then the youth will have to share the art culture of each country. Accommodation with Dharma parents, and when the ship program crosses any country, the youth delegation will also pay a courtesy call on the country's leaders.
Ms. Khuon Sodary stated that young people must strive to learn more about general knowledge related to the legislature and international relations with which the Cambodian Parliament is a member, such as ASEAN, the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (IPA) and Other international organizations, especially the Asia-Europe Parliamentary Partnership Meeting (ASEP), which the Cambodian Parliament will host, will be unprecedented in 2020.
She recommended that all young delegates pay attention and learn from the situation of other countries and the progress of that country in order to bring good points to develop their own country. Must know how to love each other like brothers and sisters by working together, working in a team and helping each other in all circumstances, as the Khmer saying goes, "At home, the other mother goes to the same mother forest."
Ms. Khuon Sodary emphasized that all young people must be good guides, diplomats representing Cambodia, while preserving the honor, values and culture of the nation by striving to promote the culture, tourism and national identity as well. Maintain good relationships with young people from other countries.
Mr. Srean Kimly said that the Association of Southeast Asian Youth Ships in Cambodia has been operating so far due to the support of the leaders of the top institutions of the nation, ministries, especially the high honors of Ms. Kittisangkhor. Dr. Khuon Sodary, representing Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, as well as representatives of the national legislature.
Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Khuon Sodary wished all young people good health and a happy and safe journey and achieved the expected results. Her Excellency Dr. Khuon Sodary also provided 400,000 Riels for each Cambodian youth delegate.
Three Ministries issued a joint proclamation to determine the management and use of revenue for the crime of urban solid waste management
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, and Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, issued a joint proclamation on the management and use of revenue from international penalties. Violation of sub-decree on urban solid waste management. This is according to the inter-ministerial announcement received by Fresh News on the afternoon of September 23, 2019.
The Inter-Ministerial Prakas requires the Capital Administration to set up a commission in charge of implementing the Capital Action Penalties for the offenses set out in Chapter 7 of the Sub-Decree on Urban Solid Waste Management. The Committee for Implementation of Capital Penalties is responsible for leading, managing, monitoring, evaluating and providing guidelines on the implementation of penalties within the jurisdiction of the Capital Administration.
In particular, this income is divided based on the percentage of revenue collected at the following rates:
* 50% contribution to the budget of the relevant sub-national administration * 44% bonus to the sub-national administration * 5% bonus to the Department of Environment * bonus Incentive to provide 1% to the Department of Economy and Finance.
