Mr. Has Vary brought the suffixes of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the monks of Wat O'Kriet to dig a pond for the people to use
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Has Vary, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, led a working group to celebrate Kan Ben at Wat O'Krit Kea, Maung Russey district, Battambang province, on September 23, 2019.
The Kan Ben ceremony is dedicated to the merits of the patriotic warriors who sacrificed their lives for the liberation of the motherland of Cambodia in the past.
On that occasion, Mr. Has Vary brought $ 10,000 as a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, along with $ 5,000 from the wife of Mr. Kay Chan, who contributed to the digging of the pond. To the monks, to the Buddhists of Wat O'Kriet, Kea commune, Maung Russey district, to use in the future.
In addition, Mr. Has Vary also spent 2.4 million riels to prepare food for 24 monks at Wat O'Krit and Buddhists at the foot of Wat Pisar gathered on Kan Ben.
Mr. Has Vary donated 1 million Riels to the Chief Bishop of Wat O'Krit, donated 1 million Riels to Mr. Nget Sovannran, 1 million Riels to Disciple Song Khao and 2 million Riels to build another pagoda.
It should be noted that in the past, Mr. Has Vary spent 12 million riels to pour concrete on the pagoda and pay for electricity at the pagoda.
(Phnom Penh): The plan to export 1 million tons of rice has been set by the Royal Government of Cambodia in 2015 to be achieved. But the plan has not been successful due to some obstacles.
Despite the failure of the plan, Cambodia's rice sector has grown significantly in both rice exports and production. Exports have steadily increased to more than 600,000 tons in 2018, while in 2019 is expected to continue to grow despite the drought.
Regarding the export of 1 million tons of rice, the new president of the Cambodian Rice Federation, Oknha Song Saran, came out and claimed that Cambodia will achieve the plan of 1 million tons in 3 years, including the Rice Federation. Laid down some principles.
Speaking in an interview with Fresh News' "Special Guest of the Week", Song Saran said the Rice Federation had met with the board as well as other members of the 20th largest export company. More than 80 percent after the meeting, the federation set out a policy to boost exports to 1 million tons.
Mr. Oknha stated that currently Cambodia has a lot of leftover rice scattered in large provinces along the Vietnamese border, including the eastern and western provinces, including: Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Battambang, Pursat and Kampong Thom, so we need small warehouses. More based near rice production areas.
He added that the federation has considered building a trust and sustainable relationship between farmers and consumers, because the construction of technology, processing, waste from rice is a contribution to the money. Extra profit for farmers and mills.
Mr. Song Saran added that we have gathered resources to study together, support farmers' capabilities and raise farmers to another level to be ready, especially to reduce their costs.
