Kandal Provincial CamControl Branch Continues to Inspect Goods at Takhmao Market, But No Goods Containing Prohibited Chemicals
(Kandal): For food safety and Dak Ben season, Cam Kong Trol Branch Officer of Kandal Province, on September 23, 2019, in cooperation with Trade Officer, inspected all items displayed by traders in Takhmao Market, Takhmao City. Kandal province, but the results did not find any banned chemicals in the product samples.
Officials from Central CamControl said that during the operation, they inspected the safety of food products, including: cans, salads, seafood, vegetables, beans, ginger, meatballs, beef, noodles, yellow noodles, and food on display at Takhmao Market. Takhmao, Kandal province, did not find any products containing chemicals. However, the team confiscated two bottles of chili sauce and tofu that were out of use and stored them for incineration.
CamControl officials also instructed all vendors on hygiene and how to properly display the goods in accordance with each type of goods to avoid bacterial contamination, and advised traders in the market. To help inspect the goods themselves for the expiration date of the goods and also prohibit the display of goods that have expired.
