Senior Ministry of Labor official: For 7 years, the Ministry trained more than 110,000 apprentices in enterprises
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Pech Sophoan, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, on September 23, 2019, emphasized that for 7 years, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has been training apprentices in total enterprises. More than 110,000 people.
This emphasis was made on the occasion of Dr. Pech Sophoan presiding over the opening ceremony of the workshop on "Validation and Approval of the Second Cambodian Apprentice Training Procedures" at Tonle Restaurant Bassac II this morning, September 23, 2019.
Dr. Pech Sophoan stated, "Apprenticeship training is a way to develop the skills of workers, which means that before entering the job, you have to receive training through their procedures with clear standards, including the salary. "It says everything, and at the end of the training, you have to get a certificate, etc."
"Therefore, this is a reform for the apprenticeship training procedures set out in our Labor Law for factories that can be implemented under the Labor Law, and in the past we have not yet been able to comply with international standards," he said. The region is still, so we strive to find development partners to discuss the development of a standard that is a vehicle to the international.
At the same time, the senior official of the Ministry of Labor said that the project to develop the apprenticeship training procedures in Cambodia is very valuable to the field of education, technical and vocational training, especially for the implementation of quality apprenticeship training. In the future.
He also hoped that after the completion of the project to develop apprenticeship procedures in Cambodia, stakeholders and especially the International Labor Organization (ILO) will continue to provide technical and financial support to adjust apprenticeship procedures in line with the Cambodian context and Continue to disseminate the apprenticeship training project in Cambodia.
Please note that the above workshop was held for the purpose of presenting, validating, approving and further directions in the development and dissemination of the draft apprenticeship procedures in Cambodia in terms of improving the quality and implementation of the apprenticeship training. To the National Qualifications Framework.
The workshop was organized by the General Department of Technical and Vocational Education of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and the International Labor Organization (ILO).
