(Preah Vihear): This morning, September 23, 2019, Preah Vihear Provincial Administration celebrated the National Fish Day on July 1, 2019 at Tumnup 95 Community Fish Pond in Tumnup Village, Pal Hal Sangkat, Preah Vihear Province. At the same time, the provincial administration has set the strictest measures for professional officials and local authorities to eliminate the effective use of various types of illegal fishing gear.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province and Mr. Long Sovann, Chairman of the Provincial Council, and was attended by Mr. Peng Trida, Director of the Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, as well as the Director of the Department of Civil Service, Armed Forces and the people. Many more.
Mr. Prak Sovann confirmed that July 1 is the closing day of fishing across the country so that Metrey can spawn for the next year. That is why we decided to choose July 1 every year to celebrate as stated in Article 17 of the Fisheries Law and consider it as a nationwide fishery closure.
At the same time, the Governor of Preah Vihear Province instructed the Provincial Department of Agriculture to pay attention to strengthen the management and development of the fisheries sector in a sustainable manner by taking more stringent measures against the use of illegal fishing gear, such as the use of gear. Shocks and mosquito nets.
"We need to strengthen and re-establish community fish ponds that have been established and continue to create more new ones in villages, communes throughout the province as a way to re-enrich fish, the Department of Agriculture must educate and provide services," he said. Techniques for our people to strive to raise fish as a family, continue to cooperate with the relevant authorities to better manage fisheries conservation areas and continue to crack down on fishing offenses.
In particular, Mr. Peng Trida said that this is the 13th time that this National Fish Day is organized in order to connect the emotions with the people, especially the fishermen and inspire all people to actively participate in the care. Preserve fishery resources.
The Director of the Department of Agriculture also stated that the Fisheries District of the Provincial Department of Agriculture has worked hard to implement the work actively like the early rain, cooperating closely with the development partners, institutions and relevant authorities by using all means, comprehensive measures on a number of important goals, including:
Elimination of fishery crimes, especially the use of illegal equipment such as shocks and nets, which have a profound effect on all types of aquatic life * Promoting aquaculture through the movement of juvenile fish in natural waters Varieties and protection of replanting flooded forests.
