Minister of Commerce: China-ASEAN Expo makes Cambodia more attractive for Chinese investment and tourism
(Nanning, China): The Minister of Commerce of Cambodia, Mr. Pan Sosak, emphasized that the organization of the China-ASEAN Expo is a golden opportunity for Cambodia to promote the export of Chinese products, attract investment and tourists.
On that occasion, Mr. Pan Sosak highlighted the long-standing friendly relations and cooperation between China and ASEAN, which have become strategic partners in all fields. The two sides agreed to boost cooperation in the fields of economy and society and other areas such as finance, telecommunications and information technology, e-commerce, investment and banking.
The Minister noted that through this strategic partnership, China-ASEAN trade volume has increased by 587.87 billion US dollars, making ASEAN the second largest trading partner. Of China.
Mr. Pan Sorsak emphasized that the bilateral cooperation between Cambodia and China in the fields of economy, trade, investment, tourism, culture, diplomacy and between people and people has grown steadily based on the spirit of mutual trust in accordance with Win-win strategy. The fruitful results of this cooperation boosted the trade volume between Cambodia and China to reach $ 6.457 million in 2018.
China ranks first in Cambodia in 2018, investing about $ 3.594 million in garments, electricity, rice mills, agro-industry, mining and energy, construction and coal. The number of Chinese tourists visiting Cambodia also increased to more than 2 million last year.
The Minister stressed that Cambodia has supported the organization of the China-ASEAN Expo. In fact, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has been invited to the exhibition 11 times in the past, more than the leaders of other ASEAN countries.
According to the Minister of Commerce, Cambodia participated in 16 China-ASEAN Expo from 2004 to 2019, benefiting from the fact that Cambodian goods have penetrated the Chinese market. Trade at 4 locations in 4 different provinces.
Through this exhibition, major Chinese investment companies have invested billions of dollars in Cambodia and as a platform to attract and attract Chinese tourists to visit Cambodia.
It should be noted that 2019 is the 16th year that China and ASEAN have agreed to hold the China-ASEAN Expo, which has been held annually since 2004 in Nanning, Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, China. The China-ASEAN Expo has become an important forum for promoting trade, investment, economy, politics, tourism, culture and diplomatic relations, especially comprehensive cooperation between China and the 10 ASEAN member countries.
