The march began this Sunday morning in Tehran as well as other cities and was attended by various units of the Iranian Armed Forces. At the same time, Iran also has another huge military parade, which is taking place on the waters of the Persian Gulf with the presence of a total of 200 warships and warships.
The Iraq-Iran War erupted on September 22, 1980, when Iraq invaded Iran, and ended on August 20, 1988, almost eight years later. Accept the UN ceasefire.
The military parade comes amid renewed tensions in the Middle East over an attack on a Saudi oil base last Saturday, in which Saudi Arabia and the United States have accused Iran. Be the perpetrator. The United States has decided to send more troops to Saudi Arabia, while Iranian President Hassan Rouhani said at the ceremony that it wanted to destabilize the Persian Gulf.
