WASHINGTON: The USS Nitze, a missile destroyer equipped with a variety of missiles, was moved into waters off the northeast coast of Saudi Arabia as the United States decided to help its allies strengthen air defense capabilities after An attack on a Saudi oil base that both countries have blamed on Iran. This is according to a quote from RT on Sunday afternoon, September 22, 2019.
On the grounds of escalating tensions in the Middle East caused by Iran, the US Department of Defense has announced the deployment of additional troops and other weapons to the Persian Gulf. According to US military officials, the move will be limited and in a purely defensive manner, not to attack any country.
Last Saturday, two Aramco oil bases in eastern Saudi Arabia caught fire due to the attack. As Houthi rebels in Yemen openly claim it is their act, Saudi Arabia and the United States have accused Iran. Iran has denied the allegations.
