Analyst Chao Chak Smok: Coup mastermind and conspirator in overthrowing the Royal Government of Cambodia, legally betraying the throne, protesting against Cambodia will not escape the legal net
These traitors will not be able to escape the law, even though Sam Rainsy and these traitors continue to insult them again and again. They will be gone in the near future as the Royal Government of Cambodia, with the full support of its people, has repeatedly warned that no matter what the cost, traitors will not be allowed to destroy. Peace, political stability and development of the nation and its people.
The Sam Rainsy Party, which includes Eng Chai Eang, Mu Sochua, Chulong, Somuramen, Sokhemrin, Ho Van Nuth, Romduol, Long Reou, Chan Ruth, Ung Rithy, Sangha Trotsil But Bun Tinh, etc., was also among the coup leaders who played an active role in the coup. Organize a coup to overthrow the legitimate Cambodian government, overthrow the throne under the guise of Sam Rainsy's return to Cambodia, a drop of blood betrayed from father to son Sam Sary.
Sam Sary, historically described as a traitor, conspired and was a political tool used by the US CIA in an attempt to overthrow King Norodom Sihanouk's coffin in the 1960s. Now, Sam Rainsy, the son, will also be recorded in history as a traitor, conspiring with foreigners, serving foreign interests, and doing politics against the Khmer people like a ghost.
Sam Rainsy is also believed to have sold his head to a foreigner, and the prisoner proudly declared that he had never used a Cambodian passport to travel, including to Cambodia. Sam Rainsy boasts of being a patriot and a Cambodian, but this is not the case. Sam Rainsy insulted the Khmer, insulted the Khmer King, the symbol of the Khmer nation.
Sam Rainsy is an opponent of the throne and wants to lead a monarchical Cambodia, a people with a long history associated with the monarchy. Who exactly is Sam Rainsy? Clearly, Sam Rainsy was a Republican and did not want a monarchy.
That is why Sam Rainsy's policy was to stage a coup d'etat to overthrow the Royal Government, to eliminate the regime from the monarchy to the republic. The coup plan has been actively carried out by a group of traitors led by Sam Rainsy.
As for the activists of the CNRP, following in the footsteps of Sam Rainsy, the acting chairman of the party, who came from the coup to seize the legacy of the suspect, Kem Sokha, is also considered to be the target of a national conspiracy to destroy the nation. Face the law.
The coup plan has been planned for a long time, but it has been active since August 16, 2019, when some pro-Sam Rainsy activists received plans directly from coup leader Sam Rainsy Mu Sochua Eng Chai Eang. In Malaysia.
According to sources from some activists who went directly to receive orders from Sam Rainsy, Sam Rainsy confirmed that he had organized a force to volunteer to die on his behalf, ready to provide $ 100 each, and set up a network in the villages and communes to prepare. Come and receive Sam Rainsy when he returns to Cambodia.
Their plan is very detailed and intertwined because it is a return plan, not for democracy and human rights, but a plan to overthrow the current Cambodian regime.
As a result, conspirators in the coup plot of Sam Rainsy were arrested by the authorities and formally charged and remanded in custody pending trial. Sam Rainsy is still fleeing abroad, and those who will face the law on their behalf are activists who are drowning in subversive tactics against national peace and state security.
That is why the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Justice, has issued a press release informing the public and the international community of the plans for a coup d'etat by Sam Rainsy and his allies, both inside and outside the country, to overthrow the Royal Government of Cambodia, legitimately betraying the throne. Destroy the nation and destroy the interests of the Cambodian people.
The statement stressed that:
First, the plot to attempt a coup to overthrow the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia is a serious crime punishable under "murder" under Articles 451 and 452 of the Penal Code, with imprisonment of 15 to 30 years. If the perpetrator is a public servant, the penalty for this "murder offense" is life imprisonment.
Second, all persons who participate in this project shall be convicted of "conspiracy offenses" which is a crime punishable under Article 453 of the Penal Code and shall be punished with imprisonment from 5 to 10 years. This adds to the sentence of 10 to 20 years in prison if the perpetrator is a public servant.
Separately, any person who participated in the above conspiracy and confessed before the competent authorities and cooperated in suppressing this crime will be exempted from punishment in accordance with the provisions of Article 454 of Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Ministry of Justice also calls on our compatriots not to succumb to the deceptive tactics of criminals that could lead to their involvement in conspiracy, which is punishable by serious penalties under the law, and to join in the fight against the above-mentioned crimes of genocide. The above conspiracy plan and related subjects to the competent authorities at all levels to take effective legal action.
This is a strong recommendation that Samdech Techo, together with Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen and Venerable Bun Seangly, and his family attend the 9th Kan Ben Ceremony at Wat Monisovann, also known as Wat Champouk K'aek, in Sangkat Prek Thmey, Khan Chbar Ampov this morning. September 22, 2019.
Kan Ben and Pchum Ben ceremonies are one of the major religious festivals in Cambodia that the Cambodian people have been celebrating since ancient times.
The Kan Ben and Pchum Ben ceremonies are a time when Buddhists have the opportunity to perform alms-giving ceremonies and gather relatives in various places, especially at pagodas.
The Kanben and Pchum Ben festivals in 2019 take place from the 1st of Roach to the 14th of Roach, corresponding to the 14th to 27th of September 2019.
On the occasion of Kan Ben and Pchum Ben celebrations, the head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, urged authorities at all levels to increase security, safety, public order, order and facilitate traffic to facilitate the people who participate in This festival.
Understand the law: drug offenses
(Phnom Penh): Drugs always have a serious impact on society as a whole, in which young people are the most vulnerable group. A small number of young people are tempted to use it because it is fun in the early days.
Drugs have immediate effects on the body and mind and can cause serious harm to the mental and emotional development of young people.
Currently, the crime of drug trafficking, distribution and use is still a matter of concern and is affecting society, both in Phnom Penh and in the provinces across the country. The effects of drugs are wreaking havoc on human resources.
What are the effects of drug use on oneself, family as well as society? And what are the penalties for using this drug?
For this week, the Legal Awareness Program, which is a collaboration between Cambodian Lawyers, International Cooperation and Fresh News, raises topics related to "drug offenses" to the public. Under:
According to Article 4 of the Law on Drug Control 2012, the definition of the term "drug" refers to the drug plants, drugs and chemical compounds identified in the table in the appendix to this law.
According to Article 5 of the same law, drugs are classified as follows:
* Table 1: Plants and substances that cause serious harm and have no medical benefits, including heroin, marijuana, marijuana resin, marijuana oil, etc.
Table 2: Plants and substances that cause serious harm but have medical benefits, such as cocaine, opium, water, opium poppy, morphine, methamphetamine, etc.
* Table 3: Plants and substances that cause harm but have medical benefits, including ketamine, fentramine, lefetamine, etc.
* Table 4: Chemicals classified in the United Nations Convention against the Illicit Drugs and Substances of the Nervous System, 1988, or in the application of this Convention against the trafficking of drugs. Illegal addiction. These substances include: mountain essential oil, acetone, chloride acid, formic acid, sulfuric acid, etc.
But if we look at the general definition, the definition of "drug" is a substance that causes users to change their mood and behavior, as well as serious danger to life.
"Drugs" are plants or plant extracts, chemicals that alter the functions of the human or animal body and, in particular, alter the nervous system and the brain when used.
Drug use has an impact on users, families and society, such as:
* Side effects on the individual user include physical health effects that when the person consumes the drug, it penetrates the human body, including the liver, heart, kidneys and lungs, and causes toxic and infectious diseases. The body is thin, pale, not sleepy, not hungry and decreased strength.
For pregnant women, the use of drugs can have a direct effect on the fetus, both physically and mentally. For mental health, it can have side effects such as memory loss, blurred vision, hearing loss, memory loss or even loss of substance abuse.
* Impact on the family, such as loss of honor, destruction of family property, fear, domestic violence, loss of money, etc.
* Impacts on society include immoral acts (gender and sexual violence), traffic accidents, robberies and other crimes, as well as loss of human resources.
Attempts to commit misdemeanors as stated in the first and second paragraphs above shall be punished in the same manner as the above misdemeanors.
If the offense is committed with a small amount of drugs listed in Schedule I and Schedule 2 and committed within a regular diet, the prosecutor may acquit the perpetrator.
If the case goes to court, the court may decide that the perpetrator of the incident should not be punished or just blame the person. It should be considered as a habitual eating, non-addictive eating, and the local eater has been eating for a long time.
Offenses under the content of Article 45 must have two conditions:
* The perpetrator personally used the drugs in Table 1 and Table 2, such as sniffing, swallowing or injecting. * The perpetrator had already experienced forced treatment measures.
Example: Mr. A is seriously addicted to drugs and his parents have filed a lawsuit to seek medical treatment and rehabilitation.
After examining the doctor, he found that Mr. A was in a serious condition, so the court issued an order forcing him to receive medical treatment and rehabilitation, even though Mr. A did not agree to receive treatment. Even so.
After receiving treatment, "A" still stole drugs with his friends and was arrested. In this case, Mr. "A" is in a position to be punished under the provisions of Article 45 of the Law on Drug Control.
Overall, drug use is not a good way to solve the problem, because the use of drugs, it can cause harm to themselves, their families, as well as society.
In addition, a person who uses drugs may be liable to fines as well as imprisonment if the drug use exceeds the capacity set forth in the Drug Control Act.
