(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kham Sophea, a doctor who specializes in gastroenterology, presented a number of factors that cause people with gastritis, gastric bleeding and the development of gastric cancer, the main factor is the use of anti-inflammatory drugs. Too much pain is also associated with infections from eating raw foods and raw vegetables.
According to doctors, before the onset of gastritis is due to stomach ulcers caused by many factors. Therefore, if the stomach ulcer is not treated properly and does not heal, it will cause bleeding in the stomach and lead to stomach cancer.
Doctors say that taking too much painkillers and aspirin will make you sick to your stomach, which can lead to cancer if not treated properly. Among the foods that cause stomach upset are raw foods and raw vegetables that contain viruses that can cause stomach upset and stomach cancer.
"Eating a healthy diet includes more vegetables and fruits than eating meat, eating more meals, reducing the use of painkillers, or aspirin, which can cause stomach ulcers," he added.
Doctors say that stomach ailments can be transmitted through eating raw meat, raw foods and eating raw vegetables that have not been properly cleaned.
The doctor added that measures to prevent stomach ailments require him to have regular health check-ups to prevent alcohol and cigarette use.
(Phnom Penh): If we look at the history of Cambodia, we see that Cambodia has been ruled by a monarchy for centuries, since the establishment of the state, there have been both authoritarian monarchies (rich in monarchy) and constitutional monarchies. But the constitutional monarchy ended on March 18, 1970, when a coup d'état led by Lon Nol, Sirik Matak and Cheng Heng to oust Norodom Sihanouk.
From 1970 to 1993, three political regimes struggled to take control of Cambodia, among them a presidential regime that existed until 1975, when the Khmer Rouge overthrew and took over. Power replaced by cannon.
The group worked to build and defend the nation in a difficult situation, with one hand defending the return of the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime and the other hand building the nation. This regime existed until 1993.
Article 437 of the first chapter of the fourth article of the Penal Code states: Million Riels. "Legal persons may also be fined 10 million to 50 million riels, as well as one or more additional penalties in case the court finds them guilty of insulting the King."
Therefore, those who insult the King face four problems:
* First, the historical aspects and foundations of Khmer culture and civilization: Insulting the King means trampling on the history and foundations of Khmer culture and civilization. The person who insults the King is a non-religious Tamil and a person who does not deserve Khmer citizenship and Khmer land.
* Second, the legal aspect: the person who insults the King is seriously violating the Constitution, which is the supreme law of the nation, has a serious criminal offense that must be punished severely as stated in the Penal Code, and has violated the motto of Nation is nation, religion, king.
* Third social aspect: Khmer people throughout the kingdom respect the King and consider him a cool shade for the descendants of the Khmer people throughout the kingdom. Therefore, a person who insults the King is a person who tramples and insults the people throughout the kingdom, like a knife to stab the hearts of the people to the greatest pain.
* Fourth, the political aspect: A person who insults the King is a person who can not do politics in Cambodian society, a person who is not welcomed by the Cambodian people. A person who insults the King is a republicanist and may have conspired with foreigners to overthrow the monarchy in Cambodia.
Therefore, all Cambodians in all urban and rural areas, please be careful of such individuals. Any trend leading to the overthrow of the constitutional monarchy in Cambodia is an attempt to bring Cambodia back to the painful tragedy of the past.
