China reaffirms commitment to encourage more Chinese enterprises to bring high-quality investment projects to Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Through the leadership of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, the Chinese side has reaffirmed that it will strive to encourage Chinese enterprises to bring high-quality investment projects to invest more in Cambodia.
This assertion was made on the occasion of Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary-General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, and Mr. Ning Chi Jie, Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Development and Reform of China, chaired the Cambodia-China Ministerial Meeting on the afternoon of the 21st. September 2019 in Nanning, China.
The meeting was held to review the progress of the implementation of Cambodia-China production capacity cooperation, which the two countries are committed to strengthening and expanding to a comprehensive strategic level through the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding on the occasion of the official visit. Mutual heads of state and government of the two countries since 2015.
The meeting noted the proud progress made by attracting more and more Chinese investment flows to Cambodia, contributing significantly to increasing production capacity and increasing Cambodia's production base to the regional and global value chain. Strong.
The two sides pledged to jointly promote and facilitate quality investment to the level and goals agreed upon by the two heads of state and government in the past in order to maximize the benefits to the people and local communities.
To achieve this goal, the two sides discussed the implementation of the Best Practices for Investment Promotion and Facilitation Services of "China Table" established by the Council for the Development of Cambodia in mid-2019.
On this basis, the Chinese side reaffirmed that it will make efforts to encourage Chinese enterprises to bring more high-quality investment projects to Cambodia.
