Lt. Gen. Hun Manet continued that today's gathering was a very meaningful, intimate and emotional gathering, and proud to have given new ranks to the retired soldiers in the 2nd Army Division who retired in 2019. This is worthy of all the dedicated and sacrificial efforts to fulfill the duties of the nation during the war and peace period, especially in the direction of the Second Army Zone.
He continued, "Our country has been peaceful to this day only because of the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the participants in this win-win policy, including Um Po Ming, a retired military officer from the first generation since the liberation of the country and End of war. "This rank is not only for the soldiers in the era of the Cambodian state, but within the framework of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces as a whole."
