(Mondulkiri): In the operation to crack down on natural resources crime, the National Commission for Forestry and Mondulkiri Provincial Commission has continued its mission to investigate various crimes, including: forestry and gold mining. As a result, the joint authorities arrested Mr. Te Kimsan, the head of the Meas Chong Plas community, on suspicion of involvement in a number of illegal crimes.
Coalition forces arrested Mr. Te Kimsan, a member of the Provincial Gendarmerie, in cooperation with several specialized forces, led by Deputy Governor of Mondulkiri Province Chheng Sochantha, on the evening of September 20, 2019, in Chong Plas Commune, Keo Seima District, Mondulkiri Province.
Hem Bonarel, Commander of the Mondulkiri Provincial Gendarmerie, confirmed to Fresh News Agency in Mondulkiri this morning, September 21, 2019, that the suspect had been arrested as a result of a joint investigation by provincial officials. He hid several cubic meters of wood as evidence in his gold mine, and the suspect was sent to the provincial military headquarters for further legal proceedings.
Mr. Chheng Sochantha, Deputy Governor of Mondulkiri Province, in charge of the Chairman of the Provincial Commission for Natural Resources Suppression, also said that the arrest of the suspect after the search force found this person has stored many cubic meters of wood of all kinds.
Until the morning of September 21, 2019, professional officers are continuing their procedures to send the suspects to the Mondulkiri Provincial Prosecutor's Office for further action. Samdech Techo Hun Sen Donates 10 Million Riels to the Families of the Dead and 5 Million Riels to the Victims of the Landslide in Samlot District, Battambang Province
(Battambang): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, donated 10 million Riels to the families of the victims and 5 million Riels to the victims of landslides. Samlot district, Battambang province.
On September 21, 2019, Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Deputy Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, handed over the budget of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to Lt. Gen. Sam Oun, Deputy Commander of the 5th Military Zone. Battambang Provincial Referral Hospital and the family of the deceased at home.
Speaking to Fresh News this morning, September 21, 2019, Senior Minister Kun Kim confirmed that after Samdech Techo Hun Sen received this unfortunate news that one victim was killed and another was injured, Samdech provided Some money to hand over 5 million riels to the victims of the injured and 10 million riels to the families of the dead.
Senior Minister Kun Kim further stated that immediately after the incident, the National Committee for Disaster Management under the command of Samdech Techo Hun Sen ordered to search for all the missing victims, but unfortunately one of the victims died. Another was rescued on time and is being treated at a hospital.
Please be informed that the Battambang Provincial Authority on the evening of September 20, 2019 confirmed that a missing person in the case of Phnom Bak Kob land at the Cambodian-Thai border at Peam Ta crossing has now been found. The Samlot district administration in Battambang province confirmed that a 20-year-old missing man, Phan Ri, was found by Thai forces in Thailand, but unfortunately the man died and his body was swollen and rotting.
Authorities confirmed that the victim's body and relatives will be cremated at the location where the forces found the morning of September 21, 2019 on the territory of Thailand and then take the bones. Home Festival in Otreng Village, Ta Tok Commune, Samlot District, Battambang Province.
It should be noted that on September 16, 2019, seven Cambodians entered the forest at the Cambodian-Thai border at Peam Ta crossing, Ta Tok commune, and were flooded by rain, causing landslides, including residents. Four escaped, one was seriously injured and two were missing. But one missing person was found alive on September 19 and another was found dead on September 20.
Mikive School Presents Graduation Certificates and Prizes to Outstanding Students for the 2018-2019 School Year
(Phnom Penh): This morning, September 21, 2019, Mikive School held a ceremony to announce the results of the Khmer and English Excellence Students Examination in all 29 branches of Mikive School and presented the graduation certificates and prizes to the students. Outstanding.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Preap Kompheak, Director of the Primary Office of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Phnom Penh, with the participation of school leaders, staff, teachers, as well as students and parents.
According to the report of the Khmer General Education Office of Mikiwe School, the 29 branches of Mikiwe School have a total of 29,456 students studying English and Khmer General Education programs from Kindergarten to 12th level. There are 11,311 students in general education in Khmer, kindergarten, primary and high school.
The report added that in this program, the school invited 222 outstanding students (1st place in the branch) from all 29 branches to participate and give away prizes and certificates to them.
According to the report, out of the 222 outstanding students, 76 were selected as early students throughout the Mikive School for the 2018-2019 school year, with the school offering awards, scholarships, study materials and more. To those outstanding students as an encouragement.
Mr. Sem Sovan, Executive Director of Mikive School, stated that the selection of the best students for each school year of Mikiway School is one of the many mechanisms of the student quality improvement plan.
Mr. Sem Sovan also expressed his congratulations on the good results of the outstanding students and stated that the results of all the outstanding students were a meaningful return to their parents and a source of pride. One for yourself and for your family.
On that occasion, Mr. Sem Sovan thanked the students and parents of their parents and guardians for choosing the Mikive School by choosing Mikive School as a place to provide education for your children and grandchildren. - Mrs.
At the same time, the principal of Mikive School urges you and your parents to continue to support and cooperate with the school to promote the quality and efficiency of your student education.
Mr. Preap Kompheak, Director of the Primary Office of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Phnom Penh, remarked that Mikive School is a valid school and complies with the standards of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Phnom Penh and the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. He praised the progress and management system of Mikiwe School.
On that occasion, Mr. Preap Kompheak also addressed the members of the ceremony, emphasizing the strengthening of teaching and learning capacity from day to day, based on the implementation of the rectangular strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia with Samdech Techo. Hun Sen is the head.
