(Siem Reap): Mr. Hor Sarun, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, representing Dr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, this morning, September 21, 2019, presided over the opening ceremony of the seminar on "Smoke-free Environment in Tourism" organized by Made in Siem Reap.
Mr. Hor Sarun pointed out that this workshop on smoke-free environment has been held many times in Siem Reap province, but what is remarkable is that today's program also has a smoke-free environment award ceremony in tourism. To hotels and restaurants that have excelled in implementing a smoke-free environment in tourism in the past.
He said that in the first week of September, the smoke-free environment team in the tourism sector and partner organizations met with the Siem Reap Provincial Administration, which includes Mr. Pov Piseth, Deputy Governor, Mr. Mey Marady, relevant departments around the province. Agree to promote Siem Reap as a smoke-free tourist city by the end of 2019.
Mr. Hor Sarun pointed out that the team also inspected some hotels and restaurants based in Siem Reap and found 10 hotels out of 20 hotels and 10 restaurants out of restaurants. 20 places that excel in implementing a smoke-free environment in tourism.
At the same time, he stated that the selection of the best hotels / restaurants that have been awarded the smoke-free environment in tourism is based on the score of the questionnaire, which is designed with the correct criteria indicators according to the law. Inspection of tobacco products and legal documents under the law, including: sub-decree, proclamation, circular, instruction, etc.
He said that in its local premises, in any form, only one package of ordinary tobacco products per brand can be displayed or sold only tobacco products that have a health warning message in the form and 55% Khmer, printed on the upper two main surfaces of the tobacco product package.
On that occasion, he also mentioned that the two main measures that the smoke-free environment team is taking are: education measures and administrative measures.
* The first measure is an educational measure by organizing workshops, training meetings, billboards and throwing promotional materials and instructing all tourism service business owners to pay attention to and comply with the law on the control of tobacco products. Launched on May 18, 2015.
Under the umbrella of this law are sub-decrees on the printing of warning messages in Khmer and pictorial on tobacco product packages, sub-decrees on measures to ban smoking or fumigation of tobacco products in the workplace or public places, and other proclamations. .
The Ministry of Tourism has also prepared a guidebook on smoke-free environment to the owners of tourism service businesses throughout Cambodia, No. 007, dated 15 June 2016, distributed to the owners of tourism business establishments to understand and follow the instructions. This is for the better.
* The second measure: which will continue to be administered as an administrative measure, is to fine the smoker in the place where the business owner is allowed to smoke in their place, to sell tobacco products in violation of the limit and to fine up to Cigarette companies that import and sell tobacco products without warning messages in the form of advertisements for illegal cigarettes, etc.
