25 Iraqi officials successfully complete demining training from Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Twenty-five Iraqi officials have successfully completed a demining training course from Cambodia after 40 days of training.
This Friday afternoon, September 20, 2019, at the CMAC Headquarters in Phnom Penh, the closing ceremony of the Iraqi Training Course on the Destruction of Unexploded Ordnance (EOD) Level 3, supported by the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA), was held.
Heng Ratana, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC), confirmed that this is the sixth time that Iraqi trainees have come to Cambodia for demining training with CMAC.
He said that the sixth training course was attended by 25 participants from different institutions, including the Ministry of Interior, Mine Action Unit and the Ministry of Environment, which took place at the CMAC Mine Action Training Institute, the Peace Mine Action Museum in Siem Reap. The second mine and the 5th mine clearance unit will last for 40 days from August 12 to September 20, 2019.
