The Royal Government and employers are satisfied with the figure of $ 190 for workers' wages in 2020
(Phnom Penh): Regarding the results of the minimum wage of workers for 2020, which decided to increase to 190 US dollars per month, the Royal Government and the employers, although there are some problems embedded in it. However, the union side did not seem satisfied with this figure as it proposed $ 195.
After the discussion on the increase of the minimum wage, which was held at the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training this morning, September 20, 2019, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor, told reporters that during the discussion. A total of 13 bilateral and tripartite internal wages are really good, active, ethical and more mature.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng continued that all have accepted this result, although the figures are not the same, the number of unions is high, the number of employers is low, the Royal Government is in the middle, but in the end, the National Council for Minimum Wages has achieved an acceptable result. Yes.
The minister added that the union side had proposed 13 points. As for the request, which is the responsibility of the Ministry of Labor, the Ministry will try to resolve the request related to inter-ministerial institutions, the Ministry of Labor will continue to discuss with other ministries and institutions to find a solution for workers. There are a number of other issues related to the tripartite mechanism.
According to the Minister of Labor, the employers' side also raised four proposals related to trade facilitation and other procedures, and the Ministry of Labor will review and resolve any proposals that are within its competence and will discuss with the Ministry. Relevant institutions continue to resolve as promised to the union parties.
Oknha Van Soeang, a representative of the employers' side, said that his side accepted the result and hoped that the implementation of the new $ 190 per month salary would be done as planned.
Mr. Van Soeang pointed out some of the issues that the employers have asked the government to reduce the tax on profits and electricity prices. Another request from employers to unions as well as workers is to increase productivity while wages continue to rise, even if workers' holidays are too frequent, employers are less satisfied with some reductions.
The employer representative claimed that this would encourage investors to increase their investment in Cambodia and maintain competitiveness with neighboring countries as well as some countries in the region.
He also supported the proposal to increase productivity to increase the skills of workers and increase export competition, but he also did not agree with the limit to increase productivity excessively, which affects the well-being of workers. The workers have been complaining and this has been happening for three years.
During the discussion, the union side asked the employer to provide food directly to the workers or pay $ 1 for this lunch and to have a car to transport the workers from the place of residence to the workplace or to provide a reasonable price for them. He drove his own car safely. Sunrise at the top of Angkor Wat will happen again in the morning between September 20-22 (Video Inside)
