Ministry of Labor issues press release setting minimum wage for workers in 2020
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on September 20, 2019 issued a press release on the minimum wage for textile, garment and footwear workers for 2020, which increased to $ 190 in One month.
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training confirmed that the National Minimum Wage Council, a tripartite mechanism with 17 members representing the workers 'side, 17 representatives of the employers' side and 17 representatives of the Royal Government, was inaugurated. The first meeting was held on August 29, 2019 and held 8 internal meetings, 6 bilateral meetings and 6 tripartite meetings.
After several meetings, the stakeholders did not unanimously agree on any figures, with the workers 'representatives retaining their final figures of US $ 195, the employers' representatives retaining their figures of US $ 186 and the government side on the basis of Technology and science set the figure at $ 187.
Pursuant to Article 12 of the Law on Minimum Wages, the National Minimum Wage Council conducted a secret ballot procedure in the morning meeting on September 20, 2019 to support each figure with the following results:
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training would like to express its deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Prime Minister for maintaining peace, stability, social order and launching various reform programs aimed at maintaining the country's competitiveness and as a basis for attracting capital. New investments and new jobs for people.
The Ministry would also like to thank Samdech Techo Prime Minister for deciding to provide an additional $ 3 on the original figure of the National Minimum Wage Council, which will contribute to the livelihoods of garment workers. And produce better footwear as well as family.
The Ministry would also like to thank all stakeholders for their active, responsible and mature participation in the minimum wage discussions for 2020.
