The Cambodian Federation of Investors Association is committed to continuing to integrate food safety, food and medicine and provide TVET scholarships for bachelor's and master's degrees.
(Phnom Penh): The Federation of Cambodian Investors Association has set a goal that in the fourth quarter of 2019, the association will continue to provide training on food safety, hygiene and basic courses for pharmacists, as well as provide scholarships to students who want to get. Professional Technical Education (TVET) at the bachelor's and master's degree levels.
This commitment was made at the 7th Ordinary Meeting of the Board of Directors of the Federation of Cambodian Investors Association on the afternoon of September 19, 2019 at The Terrace TK Restaurant, chaired by Mr. Suon Rindy, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Association and attended by Mr. Nget Chadavy, Vice Chairman of the Council, Mr. Oknha Ly Hour, Vice Chairman of the Board, Mr. Samohak Dr. Ley Sopheap, Executive Director of the Association, and some other members.
The 7th Ordinary Meeting was held to pass and approve the minutes of the 6th Ordinary Meeting of the Board of Directors to approve the draft report on the results of the third quarter of 2019 and the main goals in the fourth quarter of 2019 of the Federation Association. Cambodian investors will pass the conditions for applying for support membership of the Federation of Cambodian Investors Association and other issues.
In the report summarizing the activities of Mr. Ley Sopheap stated that in the past three quarters, the Association of Investors Federation of Cambodia has focused on three main activities, including the activities of the council is to review and edit the minutes and reports of activities. Sectors have reviewed and revised support membership applications and conditions for supporting membership.
Activities The chairperson of the executive committee in the areas of health, tourism, education and trade met with members of the pharmacy three times, with nearly 1,000 participants.
In addition, the Association and the Executive Committee also met with the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to discuss and seek input on issues raised by the private sector in relation to the education sector in Cambodia and to address the issue of market access to a number of members. 35 cases and solve legal problems for 41 members.
In addition, the association and the executive committee also work in the fields of health, social affairs, tourism, culture, sports, economy, trade, services, investment, employment and vocational education, training, land and construction development, and business, network marketing.
Although the Cambodian Federation of Investors Association has achieved many results and results in the past, according to Mr. Ley Sopheap, the association still faces some challenges and difficulties, such as people's awareness of health protection and care is still limited. Make a lot of money when there is a serious illness, a small number of foreign business owners still do not cooperate in sending staff for training.
