(Phnom Penh): Samdech Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, stated that the draft law on construction, which the National Assembly is currently studying, will be an important law as a new legal standard in addition to the existing one to promote the construction sector in Cambodia. According to technical standards, safety, aesthetics and environment.
Samdech emphasized that the draft law on construction in the context of the construction sector is growing, bigger and higher. Especially at a time when the construction sector has made a significant contribution to promoting strong and sustainable national economic growth among other sectors such as tourism, industry, trade and agriculture.
Ms. Nin Saphon emphasized that this draft law is in response to the National Policy on Land Management of the Kingdom of Cambodia dated 8 April 2011, the National Strategic Development Plan 2019-2023 and the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 of the Royal Government for Growth. Equitable and efficient work to build the foundation towards achieving the vision of a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
The chairman of the National Assembly's expert committee added that over the past decade, investment in the construction sector has grown steadily and continues to grow, especially in the construction of high-rise buildings such as condominiums, shopping malls, shopping malls. Office buildings, hotels, multifunctional buildings, satellite city construction, housing estates, etc.
Ms. Nin Saphon emphasized that the larger, higher and more complex the construction, the more required the proper implementation of legal standards, technology standards and technical regulations to ensure the strength, quality, aesthetics and sustainability of construction.
The President of the National Assembly said that when it comes to the construction sector, one remembers the works of Khmer ancestors who built the temples of Angkor Wat and Bayon and hundreds of other temples across the country. The great architectural and engineering works of the Khmer ancestors became famous all over the world.
