Police arrest 17 people in Kampong Cham province in connection with drug use and distribution cases
(Kampong Cham): Police in Kampong Cham province arrested 17 people in connection with drug use and distribution cases in Cheung Prey, Batheay and Stung Trang districts. This operation took place on September 19, 2019.
Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Em Kosal, said that the operation was carried out in accordance with the Royal Government's plan to fight against illegal drugs for the fourth time and the order of the National Police General, Dr. Neth Savoeun. Measures to suppress drug activity.
According to the General Commissioner, after receiving information from the people, he assigned the Kampong Cham Provincial Anti-Drug Office to the Cheung Prey District Police Inspectorate, Stung Trang District and Batheay District, led by Lieutenant Colonel Chiv Seng Ros, Director of the Office for the Suppression of Trafficking Cases. Drug law using open administrative rules and incitement rules arrested 17 suspects.
Lt. Gen. Em Kosal further stated that during the operation, the police confiscated 17 packages of white gram powder, 5 mobile phones, 7 motorbikes, 1 electronic scale, 1 sword and some accessories. The suspects have now been sent to the provincial specialized office to build a case for further proceedings.
