General Meas Virith: No drug user was jailed (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): On September 19, 2019, General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, met with her. Gloria Lai, Asia Director, International Drug Coalition Policy for Work Discussion.
On that occasion, Ms. Gloria Lai stated that the purpose of the meeting was to find out the general situation of the drug problem and drug offenders in prisons in Cambodia.
In response, General Meas Virith informed the guests about the general situation of the Cambodian drug problem, which the Royal Government of Cambodia has been working to fight against drugs by launching a plan to fight against illegal drugs.
At the same time, General Meas Virith confirmed to the guests, "Through these four anti-drug campaign plans, Cambodia has cracked down on criminals transporting, storing and trafficking drugs and sent them to court to be punished. "According to the law, many people have been imprisoned, but no drug users have been arrested and imprisoned."
The general explained that the government considered drug addicts to be victims who received free medical treatment and rehabilitation. At the same time, Cambodia has a clear measure: do not leave any addicts alone, they must receive treatment at health centers, hospitals in their communities without discrimination. This is an additional confirmation from the general.
