(Phnom Penh): Once again, Mr. Chrek Soknim, President of the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors, reaffirmed that the real estate sector in Cambodia will remain stable for the next five years.
Mr. Chrek Soknim made this statement during a press conference on the current and future real estate situation in Cambodia, organized by the Club of Cambodian Journalists and attended by Mr. Puy Kea, Secretary General of the Club of Cambodian Journalists, Mr. Him Seiha, Director of VTRUST Research, Mr. Peng Serey, Vice President of the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors and Mr. Man Chandy, Vice President of the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Agents.
"I think in the next three to five years, the real estate sector in Cambodia will continue to be strong and have strong support from the banking sector, combined with Cambodia's growth and development," said Chrek Soknim. Constantly peace factor - political stability is improving. "Many investors believe in politics in Cambodia today, because if there is no confidence, the real estate sector will collapse accordingly."
He said that in the past, every election, people started selling their land because they were very worried, in the opinion of the people 15 years ago. But now the level of awareness of the people today is more knowledgeable, so they will think more without believing the propaganda.
After showing the growth of the real estate sector in the next 5 years, Mr. Chrek Soknim also showed the real estate sector, which is currently a strong momentum in Cambodia, with a lot of sales.
Mr. Sok Nim revealed the risk factors and benefits, as well as strategies for buying plots without fraud. He said that in order to buy land that does not pose a risk, such as fraud, you must first study carefully, which means that if you want to buy land in any area, must meet with the commune chief, village chief in the area we want to buy first. This is a good way to buy and buy without risk.
Concerns and problems of the private sector related to legislation, tax and governance are brought to the table!
The Deputy Prime Minister, through the efforts of each working group, has benefited the private sector as mentioned in the 18th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum on March 29, 2019, such as: Reduce logistics costs, reduce port lift fees, reduce electricity costs, develop small and medium enterprises.
These activities have made the private sector more favorable, which clearly shows the high level of attention and strong support of the Royal Government of Cambodia to the private sector doing business in Cambodia.
Five major proposals were discussed and addressed, including: 1. The Law on Public Administration:
With this law already passed, the Royal Government has already issued a sub-decree to implement this law. Currently, the Ministry of Economy and Finance is continuing to prepare prakas for the implementation of this sub-decree, with further discussions with the private sector.
2: Health warning message for cigarette packs:
This issue is carefully examined and responded to. The Ministry of Economy and Finance has also set up a joint working group composed of the General Department of Taxation and the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia to improve the features of stamps to avoid fraud, as well as to check compliance with the sale of cigarettes. Penalties for non-compliance with this principle of compliance.
3: Request for reduction of electricity price for telecommunication operators:
4: Registration of private hospitals in the National Social Security Fund:
This case has been implemented to some extent, in which the private hospital is allowed to pay by the PSC in case of emergency. Some private hospitals, which have a large number of patients, have signed an agreement with the PSU and are labeled Further action, the dissemination of national social protection policies and the review of quality conditions and appropriate compensation must continue to be more widespread where additional assistance from hospitals is needed.
5: Promoting payment and use of Riel:
The spirit of participation and promotion of payments and the use of the riel is welcomed. At the same time, the relevant units will continue to study the strategy based on all aspects to promote the use and payment in riel more widely, as well as to benefit the socio-economy of Cambodia.
In addition to the five major agendas above, the forum also discussed three other major issues raised by the private sector: tax audits and the abolition of tax fines, the implementation of a minimum tax exemption. % And payment of 1% income tax exemption and payment for branded services.
1: Tax audit and request for cancellation of tax fines:
2: Implementation of 1% minimum tax exemption and 1% income tax exemption payment
The Royal Government has decided to waive the minimum tax of 1% for all enterprises that are taxpayers under the self-declared regime who have fulfilled their tax obligations properly. In order to receive this exemption, all enterprises must follow the rules and procedures set out in Prakas No. 638 MEF.PrK dated 4 July 2017 of the Ministry of Economy and Finance on the Criteria for Incorrect Accounting. And minimum tax payment procedures.
For the payment of 1% income tax exemption, is the mechanism, rules and procedures of income tax collection that apply to all tax administrations around the world to collect income tax simply. Calculated separately. The down payment is required to pay in advance the deposit, which is similar to the income tax relief.
This deposit or redemption payment is made in order to maintain the current revenue for the government to use each month. In practice, the collection of income tax exemption is associated with the following minimum taxes:
- In case the income tax is paid less than the income tax exemption paid in each month of the taxable year, those income tax exemption is considered as a minimum tax and cannot be applied for as a loan or refund. No refund.
