It should be noted that in the ongoing negotiations for an increase in the minimum wage for garment and footwear workers in Cambodia 2020 on September 18, 2019, the union party representing workers requested a figure of $ 195 per month, while the employer asked for 186 Dollars, and the Royal Government proposed $ 187.
However, this figure is much closer than the negotiations on September 12, 2019.
However, the last meeting of the National Minimum Wage Council to decide on the minimum wage in the textile, garment and footwear sector for 2020 will take place in October 2019, and the entry into force of the minimum wage will Effective from January 1, 2020 onwards. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Labor.
It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia has set a policy to increase the minimum wage for garment workers every year since 2013. The minimum wage for workers in 2019 will increase to $ 182 per month, which may increase some more in 2020.
