Senior Ministry of Women's Affairs: Women and girls still face physical, sexual, emotional and economic violence
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Man Chenda, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, on September 19, 2019, said that in Cambodia, women and girls still face physical, sexual, psychological and economic violence. Such violence can occur in the home, at work, and in the community.
The ceremony was held on the occasion of Ms. Man Chenda presiding over the opening ceremony of the Media Code of Conduct for Reporting Violence Against Women event held at the Phnom Penh Hotel this morning. September 19, 2019.
According to the 2014 Demographic and Health Survey, she said:
One in five women between the ages of 15 and 49 reported having experienced physical violence at least once since she was 15 years old, and 9 percent experienced physical violence during The last 12 months before the survey.
Forty-nine percent of married women aged 15-49 reported experiencing physical or sexual violence from their husbands. About two out of five women asked for help to stop the violence they suffered, but only 24 percent sought help from official services.
Ms. Man Chenda continued that in the face of violence, stigma and discrimination in the community, women and girls continue to be abused by some media outlets, which may increase the risk of violence resulting from reporting on Violence against women does not focus on gender and does not respect the confidentiality of victims.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Women's Affairs added that although there is a code of conduct for the media, there are no specific standards to ensure gender awareness, respect and confidentiality when reporting violence against women. No, which has a positive impact on the morals, society, values of women and Cambodian families, and also the challenge of access to protection and other important services.
At the same time, she also said that in order to implement the media execution team to report on violence against women in a comprehensive and effective way, not just one or two media units, this work requires all stakeholders. Must be highly committed to implement together effectively.
