The Minister of Tourism ordered the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism to organize a model pagoda and food street on the occasion of Pchum Ben
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, stressed the need for the 25 Capital-Provincial Departments of Tourism to improve the quality of sanitation services, environment, hospitality in each tourist destination, especially to cooperate with the Ministry of Cult and Religion, local authorities in organizing the pagoda. Model tours and food streets for the occasion of Kan Ben and Pchum Ben this year.
He instructed the directors of all capital-provincial tourism departments to cooperate with law enforcement forces and relevant authorities to ensure the safety of tourists thoroughly at each tourist destination within its jurisdiction.
Such strong indications were made during the meeting to review the work of tourism for the first nine months of 2019 and the implementation direction for the fourth quarter of 2019 at the Ministry of Tourism on September 18, 2019.
In addition to the recommendations for the above Pchum Ben, Minister Thong Khon also outlined some important tasks that the Ministry of Tourism and the Department of Tourism in all capitals and provinces must pay attention to implement effectively, including:
* Master plan for the development of tourism in Siem Reap, Mondulkiri to be a special integrated tourism area and Kep to be a high-level beach resort.
Preparation of revision of the decision on the establishment of the National Committee for Tourism Development to a sub-decree on the establishment of the Tourism Development Commission.
Preparation of the bylaws and internal regulations of the Council for the Study, Marketing and Promotion of Tourism in Cambodia.
* Development of new tourism products such as tourist resorts, community tourism, pagoda tourism, etc. Human resource development in tourism (one staff, one skill) Improving the quality of tourism products and services (one service, one standard).
* Promoting the race, clean city, clean resort, good service and good hospitality.
Facilitate travel and tourism transportation, strengthen tourism security and safety.
At the same time, the Minister also instructed the Director of the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism to effectively implement the circular on improving the quality of tourism products on the occasion of the traditional Pchum Ben from September 27-28-29, 2019. In particular, efforts must be made to cooperate with the Ministry of Cult and Religion, local authorities to organize model pagodas and food streets.
