(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, on September 18, 2019, completely rejected the interpretation and accusation against Samdech that he ordered the authorities to prevent or oppress the people in the celebration. According to Buddhist tradition.
The dismissal of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng came after some individuals misinterpreted what Samdech had instructed the capital-provincial governors to control the security situation during the Kan Ben and Pchum Ben festivals without ordering Do not obstruct the people.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stressed that Samdech has the right to issue orders to his subordinates to control the situation, and any activities that attempt to destroy peace, political stability, incite violence, internal separatist movement leads to the overthrow of the Royal Government, all competent authorities. The hierarchy must have the strictest legal measures.
"On September 10, 2019, I, Your Majesty, sent a voice message to the provincial governor instructing the people to work hard and manage the security situation of public order on the occasion that people all over the country are celebrating Kan Ben and Pchum Ben without fail. Order to prevent or oppress any citizen from attending this festival.
However, there are some individuals and media outlets that have a tendency to oppose the business to interpret, exaggerate and slander in the sense that I, Your Majesty, have prevented or suppressed the people from celebrating according to the Buddhist tradition. This is a bad intention that I, Your Majesty, cannot accept.
As responsible for the security of public order for the nation, I, Your Majesty, have the legal right and obligation to issue regulations to maintain public order security for all events.
At the same time, I, Your Majesty, have the right to order subordinates to control the situation, and any activities that attempt to destroy peace, political stability, incite violence, internal separatist movement to overthrow the government, authorities at all levels. There must be the strictest legal measures.
Recently, on the occasion of Kanben and Pchum Ben festivals of all Buddhists, I, Your Majesty, would like to call on all our compatriots to join in maintaining peace and together build merit according to their respective forces with a pure heart. " .
