Ministry of Agriculture suspends import of live chickens, protests start, Ministry of Agriculture responds to protect local farmers
(Phnom Penh): Recently, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has introduced a new measure to suspend imports from Thailand, leaving only imports from Vietnam, causing traders who used to do business. Birds (chickens) living in Thailand for decades have suffered and especially affected the daily lives of both importers and buyers to resell to consumers.
The new move by the Ministry of Agriculture is based on the fact that the actual demand for imported live chickens from neighboring countries has increased significantly beyond domestic demand, and another reason is to affect poultry farmers and Other domestic birds as well.
However, traders and former chicken importers from Thailand are still insisting on a middle ground solution from the Ministry of Agriculture to keep their careers running and if they stop immediately, they will not be able to do so. Flex or change the direction of exports from Vietnam that has never been.
The traders also asked the Minister of Agriculture, if possible, to extend the import permit from Thailand, reducing the number of some imports and reducing some imports from Vietnam to be equal so as not to affect much.
Regarding the decision to temporarily suspend the import of poultry (chicken), Mr. Tan Phannara, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production, confirmed to Fresh News as a measure to prevent over-importation. Which leads to losses for local farmers.
He stated that the demand for party animals per day, Cambodia needs only 17,000 animals, but now the principle of importing up to 44,000 animals per day.
In fact, on September 17, 2019, a company and a group of traders in Phav commune, Batheay district, Kampong Cham province, requested the head of the Royal Government to intervene to request the right to renew the process of importing live chickens from the country. Thailand.
Mr. Je Bunthorn, President of Live Chicken Import Company and other traders, said that he has been licensed since 2017 to import live chicken from Thailand and Vietnam, but until July 17, 2019, the Director General of The General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production, Ministry of Agriculture, has stopped importing from Thailand.
He said the suspension of his company from doing business appeared to be non-transparent because at the same time the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production had allowed other companies to renew their validity.
Ms. Morn, a representative of the chicken traders, also said that they were doing business with Jere Bunthorn Company, which brought chickens from Thailand, and there was good business cooperation, as the company owners did not put pressure on the traders. No. But after the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production did not renew the company, it made them really difficult.
