Ministry of Water Resources warns of heavy rains causing floods in 11 provinces from today to September 23 due to low pressure system
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has warned of excessive rainfall in some provinces from today to September 23, 2019 due to the low pressure system that is flowing over Cambodia.
A press release and additional statement from the Ministry of Water Resources stated, "According to the evolution of the weather conditions, it shows that the low pressure system (ITCZ) will continue to extend over Cambodia, while currently making the provinces "Some have been harassed by the floods."
According to the Ministry of Water Resources, the low pressure system will increase its coverage in Cambodia, and the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology would like to inform the people in the provinces to continue to be more vigilant against the floods caused by excessive rainfall. Especially Koh Kong, Preah Sihanouk, Kampong Speu, Kampong Thom, Pursat, Battambang, Pailin, Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Oddar Meanchey and Preah Vihear provinces from September 18-23, 2019.
