Separately, in Pursat province, the water level of Pursat river has risen to a level where a state of emergency has been declared.
In order to be prepared for natural disasters such as floods along the rivers in Pursat province, the Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology would like to inform that after monitoring the weather conditions, it was raining from the Cardamom Mountains, Stung Arai. Stung Prey Khlong and Stung Thom are high on the Pursat River.
The influence of the above river will cause the water level of Pursat River to increase continuously and may cause flooding in Pursat province between 2-3 am on September 18, 2019 tomorrow.
According to the above weather conditions, the Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology would like to inform the authorities of municipalities, districts, communes, sangkats at all levels and people throughout Pursat province, especially people living along the Pursat and related rivers, please pay more attention. High to avoid any possible accidents and be prepared to find a safe place for the evacuation of vulnerable people.
