Khmer traditional houses are built high above the ground, light construction type, without digging deep into the ground and have 5 types, each type differs in the style of the roof.
In that, the APSARA Authority also considered the paint of the roof of the house to be made of tiles using burnt earth color or cement color, fibro or zinc must be used red or green, the brick walls below can be painted with cement or earth color no longer fade To the color of the wood, the walls, doors, windows made of wood must be natural wood or painted like natural wood. Other colors that are bright are prohibited.
