Britain announces it will continue to provide preferential tariffs to Cambodia despite leaving Europe
A senior British diplomat confirmed this during a meeting with Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, on the afternoon of September 17, 2019 at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia.
After the meeting, Meas Kimheng, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, quoted a British diplomat as saying to the Cambodian Foreign Minister that if her country leaves the EU successfully, Britain will continue to provide preferential treatment to Cambodia and other countries. Other less developed countries as well.
Mr. Meas Kimheng stated: "Ms. Wheeler reiterated that in the near future, Britain will be able to leave the European Union, but she emphasized that Britain still provides trade preferences to Cambodia and the country. "In all 48 underdeveloped countries, the UK continues to provide."
According to a senior Foreign Ministry official, Cambodia's exports to Britain include clothing, footwear and bicycles, while exports are valued at more than $ 1 billion. He also said that the provision of preferential treatment from the British superpower will be a contribution to the development of Cambodia and Cambodia will benefit more and more.
"If he gives us preferential treatment, we will benefit from Britain now in the European Union, after Germany, Britain is the second largest exporter to Europe, Germany is over 1 billion," he said. The dollar to the UK is also more than 1 billion dollars. This is an additional confirmation from Mr. Meas Kimheng.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon expressed his deep gratitude for Ms. Wheeler's remarks. He said that Britain has helped a lot to develop and build Cambodia, especially provided various assistance such as education, demining and the Khmer Rouge tribunal.
