If the environment continues to be destroyed as it is today, the earth will warm up to "7 degrees Celsius" by 2100.
A new study on the Earth's climate shows that greenhouse gases emitted into the atmosphere through fossil fuels are warming the planet faster than previously thought. This is according to a quote from CNA on Tuesday evening, September 17, 2019.
According to meteorological studies by two leading research centers in France, the average temperature on Earth will rise to 6.5 to 7.0 degrees Celsius by 2100, in addition to the current temperature. Currently, if greenhouse gas emissions continue at current levels without reduction. This forecast is higher than in previous years.
The new study also said that the goal of the Paris Climate Agreement on setting global temperatures below 2 degrees Celsius or below 1.5 degrees Celsius, if possible, would be more difficult to achieve. Achieved as well.
According to several meteorological studies in 2014, global temperatures will increase by "3 degrees Celsius" by 2100, or at least 2 degrees Celsius if joint efforts to reduce emissions. Successful carbon dioxide. The above new study results may also be used to replace the old study results at the United Nations (UN).
