The Ministry of Labor of Cambodia announces the results of the 3rd Labor Ministerial Conference on CLMTV Labor Cooperation in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has issued a press release announcing the results of the 3rd Labor Ministerial Conference on Labor Cooperation for Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar, Thailand and Vietnam (CLMTV) under the theme " "Towards the Protection of Migrant Workers in CLMTV: Social Security Cooperation"
The Ministerial Conference on Labor took place on the morning of September 17, 2019 at the Apsara Palace Hotel in Siem Reap, which was officially opened under the chairmanship of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The Minister of Labor, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, chaired the discussion of the 3rd Ministerial Conference on Labor, which was organized with the aim of promoting cooperation in the field of labor and consensus on a common mechanism towards the establishment of a framework. Joint on Social Security Mobility for Migrant Workers in CLMTV.
The conference achieved the following important results:
* Agreed on the “Siem Reap Roadmap for the Issuance of the Minister of Labor Statement on Social Security Mobility for Migrant Workers of CLMTV - A Common Framework to Ensure Migrant Workers Benefit from Security Society at the time of repatriation or relocation in Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar, Thailand and Vietnam.
* Issued a joint statement on the outcome of the 3rd Ministerial Conference on Labor, emphasizing the strengthening of better cooperation to achieve the protection of migrant workers in CLMTV through the launch The mechanism of mobility of the social security system.
