(Siem Reap): On the morning of September 17, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the opening ceremony of the 3rd Ministerial Conference on Labor within the framework of CLMTV: Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar, Thailand and Cambodia. Vietnam under the theme "Towards the Protection of Migrant Workers in CLMTV: Social Security Cooperation", which was organized at the Apsara Palace Hotel in Siem Reap.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen Remarks at the Opening Remarks of the 3rd Labor Ministerial Conference within CLMTV
* Samdech Techo commends the Ministry of Labor of Cambodia for working well with the relevant authorities to organize the 3rd Meeting of Senior Officials and the 5th Minister of Labor
* Samdech Techo stated that in the past, migration for work was only in border countries, but now due to more means, it is easier for people to find work in other countries.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that within the framework of CLMTV also consider the social security system for migrant workers as he changes jobs from one place to another
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says Cambodia supports the introduction of legal standards that support migrant workers
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the pre-transition period from one country to another was not easy, especially during the Cold War.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says that during the Cold War, Vietnam sent workers to the Soviet Union and Europe
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says integration has given Cambodian workers the opportunity to work abroad
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says that Japan is now making it easier for workers to go to work, while South Korea receives more workers
* Prime Minister claims that for ASEAN countries that lack real labor force are Brunei, Singapore and Malaysia
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says Thailand is the largest recipient of workers from Cambodia, Myanmar and Laos. If Thailand expels workers from these countries, the Thai economy will suffer.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says employment is an effort within the framework of ASEAN, while the Philippines has the largest number of migrant workers.
* Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia is in discussions with the Thai side to arrange for the preservation of seniority for Cambodian workers working there when returning to work in Cambodia.
* Samdech Hun Sen recalls the old story when Aung San Suu Kyi called for her workers to leave Thailand. How many Myanmar workers have returned to their country so far? In this case, the Cambodian opposition party attacked Samdech
* Samdech's finally say that Myanmar workers did not go home at the urging of Aung San Suu Kyi, only to work in Thailand more due to lower labor costs in Myanmar
* Samdech Techo says that now the movement of workers is not limited to ASEAN, some workers have gone to work in countries in the Middle East.
* Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia is honored to host the CLMTV Meeting as the Royal Government launches a migration policy in line with the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4.
