Anti-trafficking police crack down on orchid massage parlors
(Phnom Penh): Police from the Office of Anti-Human Trafficking and Protection of Minors conducted a search operation in collaboration with local authorities in Sen Sok district and arrested 37 people in connection with prostitution cases, including: 3 managers, 4 regular staff. , A security guard, 23 masseuses (2 suspected minors) and 6 guests.
This operation was directed by Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner General and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, coordinated by Ms. Seur Vanny, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and led by Lt. Gen. Chan Kittikhom, Deputy Commissioner in charge of the office. Anti-Trafficking and Protection of Minors of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
Please also note that the massage parlor has a total of 27 massage rooms for hand sex services from $ 30 and up and sex from $ 50 up. Some of the money received from the guests was distributed to three male officers who were Cambodians.
Experts said that before arresting the suspects, the Anti-Human Trafficking and Juvenile Protection Bureau conducted several days of investigation until the operation to arrest three officers and a woman. Twenty-three masseuses were immediately removed and some condoms were confiscated and brought to the office. At the end of the interrogation, those who were not involved were allowed to return to normal.
Currently, the police have detained 3 male officers in order to build a case file. Meanwhile, the masseuse was handed over to the Department of Social Affairs in Phnom Penh. Today is the 4th Ben! Discover the history of Pchum Ben, a tradition of the Cambodian people.
