(Pailin): After heavy rain in the upper part on the afternoon of September 16-17, 2019, Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, accompanied by Mr. Khlok Nouy, Deputy Governor, Mr. Sam Sareth, District Governor of Sala Krao and leaders. Relevant officials have inspected the water condition along the Pailin River to be prepared in case of possible flooding.
On that occasion, Mr. Phan Chanthul said that due to the heavy rain these days in the upper mountains, which caused the water level of Pailin River to be abnormal. Therefore, local authorities and relevant officials must be prepared in advance to facilitate the release of water and rescue people in time in case of flooding.
The provincial governor urged local authorities to cooperate with relevant professional units, especially the provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology to study the location of water release if there is flooding and rescue people in time.
