In the aftermath of the attack on Saudi Arabian oil refinery ARAMCO, Houthi rebels in Yemen (backed by Iran) have claimed responsibility and even the media reported that the attack was from Yemen. But US officials have since claimed that the attack originated in Iran or Iraq.
The simple answer is that acknowledging that the tiny Houthi rebels were behind the attack is tantamount to acknowledging that the US multi-billion dollar Patriot defense system on Saudi Arabia is Incompetent or useless because even the attacks from the Houthi rebels could not resist.
Some experts have differed on this claim, concluding that the United States is trying to bring charges against Iran because it wants to mobilize international forces to put pressure on and impose sanctions on the Tehran regime. An additional excuse to carry out any military attack on Iran.
Saudi Arabia has claimed that the US air defense system is capable of intercepting and destroying missiles from Yemen. But in 2018 and 2019, Riyadh itself claimed that Houthi rebels in Yemen had led a series of attacks on infrastructure on its territory, particularly in the capital, Riyadh. The heart of this oil kingdom.
