(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia and the State Bank of Vietnam have organized an annual bilateral meeting to strengthen cooperation and friendly relations between the two banks.
The bilateral meeting is aimed at strengthening ties, cooperation and friendly relations between the two central banks. The two sides exchanged views on the macroeconomic situation and the banking sector and the progress of bilateral cooperation.
Both sides praised the progress of cooperation between the National Bank of Cambodia and the State Bank of Vietnam, which has contributed significantly to the development of the banking and economic sectors of the two countries. The two central banks exchanged experiences on key tasks aimed at strengthening the central bank's core operations, as well as strengthening economic and financial sector integration that supports trade and investment between the two countries.
Mr. Chea Chanto said that the current bilateral meeting continues to have good cooperation to support the banking and financial sectors in both countries.
He added that the State Bank of Vietnam has provided assistance to the banking sector in Cambodia, including technical assistance, human resource development, which is the basis for building the banking system in Cambodia.
He added, "I would like to thank the Governor of the State Bank of Vietnam for always supporting the good cooperation between the two institutions, especially the contribution of human resource development, which has provided scholarships to the National Bank of Cambodia to study in Vietnam."
Mr. Le Minh Hung said that for the past 40 years, the relationship between the National Bank of Cambodia and the State Bank of Vietnam has been close and has always helped each other in the development of the banking sector due to the indications of the central banks of both countries. 2 Make both economies achieve remarkable results.
He added that through the annual bilateral meetings, the close ties and cooperation between the two countries' central banks could be demonstrated.
