(Siem Reap): Following the decline in tourists at the Siem Reap-Angkor destination, the Inter-Ministerial Commission has announced the launch of four strategic plans for tourism development, mainly to jointly address relevant issues to revive the growth of tourists in the area. Four key potentials have also been identified that need to be developed into essential tourist destinations.
The announcement of the necessary strategic plan was made during the third meeting of the Inter-Ministerial Commission to prepare the master plan for tourism development in Siem Reap at the Sokhalay Hotel in Siem Reap on September 16, 2019 under the chairmanship of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, as well as some leaders who are members of the Inter-Ministerial Commission.
Angkor Prachum announced the launch of the Master Plan for Tourism Development in Siem Reap and the short-term action plan for 2019-2020 under the motto "Turn challenges into opportunities".
The four strategic plans include: 1- Diversification of new tourism products and extension of stay of tourists 2- Creating competitiveness 3- Creating connectivity and 4- Creating a new identity of Siem Reap.
At the same time, the Inter-Ministerial Commission has identified the Tonle Sap Lake, Phnom Kulen, Siem Reap and surrounding areas as areas to be developed into new tourist destinations besides Angkor:
4. Angkor Temple Area: Study and launch a project to visit Angkor Wat at night. Lighting and visiting outside the temple for the night, but to protect the safety of the temple and artifacts. Arrange a special tour of Angkor Night to visit some temples at night. Promote cycling tourism as this type of tourism is growing rapidly and brings a lot of added value.
