(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Environment, has issued a letter celebrating World Ozone Day on September 16, 2019, committing to join the international community in eliminating ozone depleting substances. This is according to the letter from Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment.
According to a letter from the Ministry of Environment, obtained by Fresh News, "Cambodia is committed to continuing to engage with the international community in the successful implementation of all its obligations to ensure the effectiveness of the reduction. And eliminating the use of ozone depleting substances and substances with high potential for overheating.
September 16, 2019, is the 34th anniversary of the establishment of the Vienna Convention on the Protection of the Ozone Layer and the 32nd anniversary of the establishment of the Montreal Protocol on Ozone Depletion.
The Ministry of Environment, on behalf of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, also congratulates governments and nations around the world on celebrating World Ozone Day under the theme "32 Years of the Montreal Protocol and the Improvement of the Montreal Protocol." "Ozone Layer" to inspire people from all walks of life to continue to participate in the protection of the ozone layer and celebrate the success of the Montreal Protocol on the protection of the ozone layer.
According to the Ministry of Environment, so far the nations of the world have almost completely eliminated ozone depleting substances, and we hope that the ozone layer will return to normal by 2050. Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, September 16: 742 Illegal Vehicles Found and Fined
