"We have traveled around Cambodia to find students who are struggling and in need of scholarships to continue their education," he said. "Better education means more opportunities for them to serve the nation."
Ms. Leakena, an employee of SCG who has been involved in this volunteer work for more than 5 years, said, “At SCG, we have different approaches to selecting scholarship students. "We focus not only on well-educated students, but also on having a good attitude and a willingness to help society."
She added: "Visiting home and seeing their living conditions gives us a better understanding of their actual living conditions, which they really need help to have the opportunity to study better. "Really."
SCG has been running this dream sharing program for 5 years, since 2014. "SCG plans to continue this scholarship program in Cambodia for a long time to come, so that Cambodian students can achieve their dreams for a better future."
In 2019, this is the sixth year for the SCG Sharing Dreams program, and SCG, in collaboration with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, will continue to provide 250 scholarships for high school students and 20 higher education scholarships for students. Former SCG Scholarship Shares Dream of Continuing Education at Universities
