(Phnom Penh): The ballet bridge across the Tonle Sap River in Phnom Penh's Russey Keo district will reopen on September 16, 2019, after a hiatus due to an oil tanker collision.
Mr. Saing Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport, told Fresh News on the evening of September 15, 2019 that due to the efforts of engineers and workers day and night so far to repair the ballet bridge. Re-completion is complete and ready to launch tomorrow morning.
The director of the Department of Public Works hopes and believes that the Chroy Changvar bridge, which has been congested in recent days, will reduce traffic congestion and return to normal after the ballet bridge is reopened.
Please be informed that the authorities decided to temporarily stop the traffic over the ballet bridge connecting Russey Keo to Chroy Changvar on September 11, 2019 to inspect after the bridge was hit by Savimex oil tanker at 3 pm. September 10
The new Ballet Bridge across the Tonle Sap from Sokimex Oil Depot on National Road 5 in Russey Keo District to the Chroy Changvar Satellite City Development Zone in Chroy Changvar District was officially inaugurated on the afternoon of May 08, 2018. The construction process has been going on for the past six months.
