Please note that as of today, a total of nearly 4,700 families across the province have received donations from the provincial Red Cross branch. Legal Awareness: Topic on "Consumer Loan Contract"
(Phnom Penh): The Civil Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia clearly stipulates the general rules and types of contracts. The term contract is a legal act that establishes a legal relationship and a legal obligation between two or more persons, the parties expressing their willingness to enter into a contract through a request and a swipe.
There are 13 specific types of contracts in the Civil Code, however, in Cambodian society today, there are many more types of contracts that occur by mutual agreement and are valid and legally enforceable. Limited in the Civil Code. Commonly used contracts include: sales contract, lending agreement (loan agreement), lease (lease contract), employment contract, etc.
In particular, this week, Fresh News' Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation, would like to raise a topic related to the food loan agreement to interpret and share as follows:
Pursuant to Article 578, a food loan contract refers to a type of contract which one party is called a lender in which there is a case of free delivery of food, money or other substitutes during a certain period of time to the other party. We call borrowers. In particular, the borrower is obliged to return to the lender an item of the same quality and quantity as the item received from the lender.
This means that in the event that the lender returns the money or in the form of rice, the borrower is free to use or consume the rice, and the borrower is required to repay the lender an equal amount or Rice of the same type and quantity or quality after a certain period of time has arrived.
Example: Mr. Sok lent Mr. Sao to borrow 30 kg of Rumduol rice to solve daily life problems. Both parties agreed to return it on September 10, 2019, and that rice must be Rumduol rice. Therefore, at the appointed time, Mr. Sao is obliged to return 30 kilograms of rumduol rice to Mr. Sok.
The mortgage agreement shall be entered into with the agreement of both parties, and the parties may also enter into a contract subject to interest repayment by agreeing to establish a debt-related right so that the interest-bearing liability is retained. Effective unless the agreement is in writing, the parties must thumbprint or sign the contract.
Consumer loan contracts are divided into two categories:
* Interest-free food loan agreement * Interest-free food loan agreement
1: Interest-bearing loan contract
An interest-bearing loan agreement is that the lender is obliged to return the item to the borrower, and the item must be defective (items in good condition). In particular, if the item you lend to a borrower is a defective item and the borrower is unaware of the defect, the borrower may demand that the lender exchange the defective item.
In addition to claiming to replace a defective item, the borrower can also claim damages. In principle, the interest rate is determined by mutual agreement, called the "contract interest rate". In case the parties have promised to pay interest but have not set the interest rate, the interest rate shall be calculated according to the law called "interest rate set by law".
Restricted interest rate refers to the interest rate set in accordance with the law, by agreement between the parties, as determined by law and other legal norms through the Prakas of the Ministry of Justice on interest rate No. 128 KY.Prak / 11. December 21, 2011 The limited interest rate is limited to 18% (eighteen%) per annum.
In other words, with respect to the time of interest payment, if the parties do not have a fixed period of payment, the interest shall be paid to the lender at the end of each year, starting from the time of delivery. Which is the subject of the loan, but if the borrower agrees to repay the object within one year, the interest must be paid upon delivery of the object which is the subject of the loan.
In the event of a late non-payment of interest for a period of one year or more, even if the lender urges you to repay, the borrower still refuses to repay the interest, the lender may add interest. Into the principal.
2: Interest-free eating loan contract
This type of contract is widely used in daily life, such as borrowing money between friends or relatives. For a non-interest-bearing food loan agreement that has been entered into in writing, the lender shall have a case of return of the object which is the subject of the lending agreement.
However, in the event that the food loan agreement is made orally, if the lender has not yet delivered the specific loan, the lender may terminate the lending without a clear reason (Article 580 of the Civil Code). ).
Please also note that for the oral loan contract, Party A can stop lending without a clear reason, except that the object of the loan contract has already been given.
Separately, if the contract is made in writing, Party A has the case of handing over the object (jasmine rice) to Party B by agreement.
Termination of a loan contract erupts with a loss of confidence in the borrower from the time the contract is formed until the time of delivery of the object of the contract if the borrower's economic condition deteriorates significantly, leading to obstruction of the performance of obligations. Repay.
In conclusion, a mortgage loan is a type of contract that is often used in daily life as well as in business, depending on the size of the needs of the people or the needs of the actual business situation.
In addition, the mortgage agreement is a contract that plays an important role in ensuring the integrity and honesty between the lender and the borrower in order to ensure clarity in the implementation of the rights and obligations of the parties.
Police in Po Sen Chey district cracked down on 4 motorcycle thieves
(Phnom Penh): A group of robbers in Phnom Penh were raided by the 2nd Kakap Police Station of Po Sen Chey District Inspectorate and 4 others were fleeing. After the thieves took a corner stick and robbed one of the victims, they took the motorcycle three days ago.
Mr. Yim Saran, Police Inspectorate of Po Sen Chey District, told Fresh ews news agency on September 15, 2019 that the above robbery case, the suspects acted on September 11, 2019 at 01:55. Minutes of concrete road, Chamkar Ovulk 2 village, Sangkat Kakap II, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The four suspects also used drugs and confiscated: a small pink (MINI) motorcycle without license plate, 2 transparent plastic bags, a small bag, a mobile phone and drug paraphernalia. Some.
Mr. Yim Saran, the inspector, said that the story before the victim and his girlfriend came back from a walk, when they arrived at the rented room, sitting and chatting on the concrete road near Bright Time Private School. At the scene above, there was a group of unknown suspects, three of them dressed in civilian clothes, holding a corner stick, and two others were waiting to cover their buttocks and walk towards the victim and then robbed him. The motorcycle decided once and then escaped.
Mr. Yim Saran said that immediately after the incident, his police force was informed of the case, he immediately ordered his forces to launch a search operation until the target of arresting four thieves in the gang. 5 people use for 3 days.
The suspect has now been sent to the specialized unit of the Police Inspectorate of Po Sen Chey District for questioning and temporary detention, waiting to be sent to court for legal proceedings.
