Analyst: Sam Rainsy is a traitor, a traitor to the King
7 Khmer-Australian-New Zealand Association: Sam Rainsy, a political prisoner, repeatedly insulted the King
(Phnom Penh): Seven Cambodian-Australian-New Zealand Associations on September 14, 2019 issued a joint statement condemning Sam Rainsy for repeatedly insulting the King.
The seven Cambodian Citizens' Associations based in Australia and New Zealand include: 1. Cambodian Cultural Association of South Australia 2: Cambodian-Australian Association of Queensland 3: Cambodian Australian Citizens Association of Victoria 4: Cambodian Urban Youth Association Sydney 5: Association of Cambodian Friendship and Culture in South Australia 6: Khmer Cultural Support Association Wellington 7: Khmer Hamilton Association - Phnom Penh
The seven Khmer Associations wrote: "The words of Sam Rainsy, which were made public on Radio Free Asia, as mentioned above, are the most serious insult to the power of the King, which has already been committed. Once again, Yang Kklin, who proves that this prisoner is a bad politician who does not respect the Constitution and the laws of the Kingdom of Cambodia at all.
The statement continued: Article 7 of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia states that "The King cannot be violated by anyone." Article 8 states that the King is a symbol of national unity and sustainability. The King is the guarantor of the national independence, sovereignty and territorial integrity of the Kingdom of Cambodia. He is the guarantor of respect for the rights and freedoms of the people and respect for international treaties.
The seven Khmer Associations also requested the relevant authorities and courts at all levels to take immediate and strict legal action against Sam Rainsy, who has committed serious violations of the King. The noble role in accordance with the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the cool shadow of the Cambodian people who are living in peace, stability and development as it is today.
TOP NEWS: Gendarmerie Forces Across Cambodia Condemn Sam Rainsy Prisoners and Ready to Implement Arrest Warrant and Order
(Phnom Penh): The National Gendarmerie has strongly condemned the convict Sam Rainsy for insulting the King of the Kingdom of Cambodia. The words of the convict, Sam Rainsy, which were made public, seriously damaged the reputation of His Majesty the King, the highest deity.
The action of Sam Rainsy violates the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which states in Article 7 "The King can not be violated by anyone" and is an insult to the King, which is punishable under the provisions of Article 437 "Duplicate" of the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Royal Cambodian Gendarmerie would like to express its support for the court's action and be ready to implement the court order and implement all the orders of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, in order to maintain security and social order for all citizens.
