(Koh Kong): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, this morning, September 15, 2019, brought donations of food and some money to the officers and soldiers of the Defense Battalion. Border No. 3, which stands guard at the border in Cham Yeam village, Pak Klang commune, Mondul Seima district, Koh Kong province.
Lieutenant Colonel Rom Mony Sopha, Commander of the 3rd Border Brigade, gave a warm welcome and reported to the Minister and the accompanying delegation on the tradition of the sisterhood between the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the 3rd Border Guard Battalion. Since 2006, and, of course, through this sisterhood, the battalion on this remote ridge has evolved.
Based on the achievements of the Sisterhood, the Lieutenant Colonel, on behalf of the brigade leadership, expressed his deep gratitude to the leadership of the Ministry at all levels and subordinates for their dedication, both physically and mentally, in the direction of helping. The development of this small battalion is in line with the slogan, "Defend the nation for all, all for the defense of the nation."
