(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and Lok Chumteav, as well as leaders at all levels and civil servants, on September 15, 2019, attended the second Ben at Wat Saravan Techo, Phnom Penh.
On that occasion, Minister Vong Soth said that holding Pchum Ben is a tradition from Khmer ancestors and the purpose of Pchum Ben is to allow all monks to remember the rain in the temple. In other words, to commemorate the souls of ancestors who passed away to the next world.
Mr. Vong Soth stated that this Pchum Ben festival is a traditional Khmer national festival that people have been following the path of Buddhism for a long time because the country is peaceful and stable under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government, has supported and cared for the field of Buddhism, making rapid progress. All Cambodians have the right to freedom of religion at all times.
On that occasion, in order to contribute to the promotion of religion, Mr. Vong Soth and Lok Chumteav donated 11 million Riels for the construction of the pagoda yard and also donated money to the grandparents and students who stayed in the pagoda. .
It should be noted that every festival season, Mr. Vong Soth and Lok Chumteav, as well as leaders at all levels of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, always go to the festival to dedicate to relatives and wish good luck to the family. Brothers, compatriots and the whole nation.
