(Prey Veng): Five of the 13 districts of Prey Veng province, including: Sithor Kandal, Pearang, Po Rieng, Peam Ro and Svay Antor districts, equal to 32 communes, 191 villages are experiencing floods and the provincial authorities are taking action. Emergency.
According to the Deputy Governor, 455 families were short of food and 5 families were sick, 1,284 houses were affected and 3,753 hectares of rainy season rice were affected and 100 hectares were damaged.
Mr. Duch Kunthea continued that for this flood, Prey Veng Provincial Authority, led by Mr. Chea Somethy, Provincial Governor, led a team to directly inspect the flood situation and instructed the people to be very careful and recommend more local authorities. High vigilance in preparing to save the people and find a safe place for them to ensure safety.
In particular, areas that are dangerous or prohibited to pass through must be marked with a sign for them to know, and all authorities must be stationed in places that face severe flooding to ensure the safety of the people, especially. Prepare and distribute food to the people as well. This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Duch Kunthea.
According to Mr. Duch Kunthea, the emergency level in Prey Veng province was 7.50 meters, now the water level is 6.32 meters.
