KCE International School officially launches a multilingual international curriculum in one program
(Phnom Penh): After announcing the launch of a new curriculum recognized by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports in a new context of modern learning, KCC International School and KCE Language Center have officially launched the international curriculum. There are three languages in one program: Khmer, English and Chinese in response to the progress of the social context.
Ms. La Sopheak, Director of KCE International School, said that the school offers a multilingual international curriculum in a single program in Khmer, English and Chinese to respond to the progress of social contexts as well as The whole world, with Khmer as its native language, English as an international language and Chinese as the most widely used language in the world, especially China's economic growth.
KCE International School operates kindergartens from 3 to 12 years old, incorporating general education in Khmer in accordance with the curriculum of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, and English taught in the Cambridge curriculum. And more importantly, the addition of Chinese language courses on the same general tuition fee.
It should be noted that on September 12, 2019, the management and staff of KCE International School and KCE Language Center held the official opening ceremony of KECE International School and KECE Language Center located in 21 AB, Street 146, Sangkat Phsar Depot II, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh, with the participation of many guardians and guests.
Your child will receive three languages at the same time: Khmer, English and Chinese, the new school year starts on September 9, 2019. You will receive a scholarship of up to 30% with a free school bus ride for registration before October 2019.
