Minister of Agriculture encourages pig farmers in Kampong Speu to strengthen and expand raising to ensure both quantity and quality
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, this morning, September 14, 2019, visited O'Neang Hing Village, Tang Kroch Commune, Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province to inspect pig farms. Meat is Chang Touch's industry.
With the support and encouragement of professional officers in the field of technical training in breeding and support from the project to study the medium-sized biogas plant for smart environment, along with his own investment budget, led him to expand the farm and implement contract farming. With CP Cambodia partners.
At present, the farm has 5 cages per cage with 6,000 pigs, a total of 3,000 pigs. In one year, he paid his expenses and earned more than $ 60,000, and this strong income led him to repay all his bank loans and even give him the opportunity to expand his farm, which is preparing land and building cages. 3 more.
On this occasion, the Minister praised and appreciated the efforts of farm owners, he confirmed that this growth is in line with the development of the national economy, population growth, and especially the needs and preferences of the market.
The Minister encouraged and instructed professional officials and CP Cambodia to continue to support him and the pig farmers throughout Kampong Speu to strengthen and expand the breeding to ensure the quantity, quality and well-being of consumers.
In the morning of the same day, the Minister and the provincial governor, together with his colleagues, continued to travel to Kaheng commune, Samrong Tong district to inspect the vegetable cultivation of farmers who are members of the suburban mixed vegetable community. Looking at the actual situation, most of the farmers in this commune like to grow vegetables, lettuce and prawns, which are additional sources of income to improve the family's livelihood besides rice.
The Minister and the Governor expressed their happiness and congratulations on the achievements of the farmers and the whole community and encouraged them to continue their efforts based on the right technical principles, including seed, cultivation and care. Insect juice, harvesting, packaging, storage and delivery to the market with quality and hygiene, make our vegetable products have a good market and high prices.
He also advised the department to provide additional technical training and the General Department should bring new projects to the area, focusing on the use of net houses and vegetable irrigation systems, the implementation of good agricultural programs (GAP). Customer trust through quality and safety of products.
In addition, the department should study the possibility of establishing vegetable collection facilities to ensure supply and quality, and should also strengthen packaging techniques and provide clear labeling, and in particular promote the establishment of credit services in its community to reduce the risk of private credit. There is a high interest rate.
Delighted to see good quality international cattle farms, bringing technology from Korea to good use, the Minister praised and highly appreciated Kim's willingness to invest in farms, and can also be said to be The best beef cattle farms in Cambodia today, based on the management of infrastructure, feed quality, hygiene, the environment around the number of animals and the health of the animals.
The Minister supported and encouraged the plan to expand livestock production in the future, as it will contribute to the improvement of the beef production sector in Cambodia to be better and better, while the trend of raising cattle. Nationwide, there has been a significant increase.
On the other hand, it will positively contribute to the supply of beef with hygienic standards, quality and safety produced from a farm and slaughterhouse, with strict technical inspection on all production lines.
At the same time, he also advised the Office of Animal Production and Animal Health to continue to cooperate with the farm to the fullest for the sustainability of the farm's investment process. In particular, the General Department of Animal Production and Animal Health should organize internships to exchange experiences on breeding techniques between this farm and other farms or breeders whose implementation of breeding techniques, management and production of feed is still limited.
