(Phnom Penh): As of the evening of September 13, 2019, it has been 6 days and the rescue team has not been able to tow the ferry that hit the pillars of the Prek Tamak Bridge, despite using almost all means. Case. For today's operation, a team under the command of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol used a tugboat for additional assistance, but was still unsuccessful.
Reports from the scene claim that from the day of the incident until September 13, the authorities from all institutions have joined forces and used almost all means to pull the barge to transport the sand from the place, but not Still successful, only a slight shaking of the head, and the biggest obstacle in this operation is due to the strong currents.
According to the report, Shanghai Company, the company that got the right to build the Prek Tamak Bridge, also arrived at the scene to check the actual situation with the Cambodian authorities. The company also claimed that the ferry that hit the bridge did not affect the quality of the bridge, so there is nothing to worry about.
Please be informed that this rescue operation was carried out by the technical team of the relevant ministries and experts from the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port led by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport.
On the afternoon of September 7, 2019, a sand barge opened and got stuck with the Prek Tamak Bridge (the third pillar), causing it to get stuck on the third pillar of the Prek Ta Mak Bridge. Immediately after receiving the information, the Governor of Kandal Province, Mr. Mao Phirun, went down to intervene to find a way to pull the ferry from the bridge.
