Real estate experts and citizens see the importance of relocating factories to the suburbs to people's livelihoods
(Phnom Penh): After the Phnom Penh Capital Administration issued a notification on the plan to relocate factories, enterprises, warehouses and large car repair garages from urban areas to the suburbs along the Third Ring Road. Made the people living along the three ring roads very happy.
Expressing the people's happiness for the relocation of factories, enterprises, warehouses to the three metropolitan areas, which will help create a bustle and easy to create jobs and help the suburbs to develop more.
Dr. Kim Heang, President of KW Cambodia Real Estate and a well-known real estate expert, said that the relocation to the suburbs is reasonable because in Phnom Penh there is another increase in the population in the suburbs. The land is cheap, running a factory will run smoothly.
He added that in addition to reducing traffic in the city, moving the factory to the suburbs has provided benefits and opportunities for middle- and lower-middle-class people to buy land in the area. Can buy a house to live and run a business because the middle class can not afford to buy a house in the city center.
He stated that this is a contribution to facilitate the livelihood of the people to some extent.
Born Long, chief of Khleang village, Udong district, said that people were happy after hearing that the project to move factories to the suburbs, which will create job opportunities for them, while Trach Tong commune has become an important target to build factories and other enterprises. ⁇. Such claims are due to the fact that many companies have visited the site, combined with a lot of land splitting activities.
"On behalf of the authorities and the people here, I am pleased with the news of the relocation of the factory to the suburbs, because the land in the suburbs is large and practically favorable in Trach Tong commune, which is close to Ra Trach Tong and the national road in the ring road area," he said. Third, already.
Ms. Ven Hoeun, a resident of Ra village, Trach Tong commune, said that she was happy and ready to welcome the construction of a local factory. "Nowadays, we only see the division of land near Ra Trach Tong and there are a lot of people coming and going to buy, but if the factory comes to work here, I will be happier because I want to see development, jobs, especially house construction," she said. And big villas in my village.
(Battambang): The police force of Maung Russey district, Battambang province, executed an arrest warrant according to the court order on the morning of September 13, 2019 and sent it to the provincial court for legal action.
According to the local police, the arrest of the accused was made by implementing the arrest warrant issued by the Investigating Judge of Battambang Provincial Court, Mr. Rem Sopheak on August 21, 2019 and following the directive. From Major General Ouch Sokhon, Battambang Provincial Police Commissioner.
Brigadier General Sar Kimlong, Police Inspector of Maung Russey District, led the police force to implement the arrest warrant for the above accused in connection with aggravated intentional violence and aggravated intentional damage at the district level. In the past.
Defendant Vith Vutha, alias Chrouk, 21, resident of Po 1 Village, Kear Commune, Maung Russey District, Battambang Province, committed aggravated intentional violence and aggravated intentional damage committed on 14 July 2019. Passed at Kear 3 village, Kear commune, Moung Russey district, Battambang province on July 14, 2019.
At present, the accused is under the authority of Maung Russey district and the case has been sent to the Battambang Provincial Court for further proceedings.
