WASHINGTON: US-China Business Council (USCBC) said US exports to China in 2018 totaled $ 118 billion, down 7 percent from a year earlier. But trade wars. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Friday evening, September 13, 2019.
In a report released Thursday, the USCBC also noted that 265 of the 435 regional congressional offices across the United States found that US exports fell last year. 2018 was stronger than 2017 and 61 other offices saw export growth of less than $ 10 million over the same period.
However, China remains the third largest export market for the United States after Canada and Mexico, with 1.1 million jobs dependent on exports to China.
In its report, USCBC also called on the two sides to return to talks to find a solution to the current trade war, while US and Chinese officials are expected to meet again early. This coming October, with the expectation of positive results.
