Cambodian Ambassador Reacts to Indonesian Tourism News Report Wrongly Writing "Angkor Wat Belonging to Thailand"
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Embassy in Indonesia has reacted strongly to the publication of an Indonesian tourist newspaper, Tempo, which wrote that "Angkor Wat is Thai." Along with this reaction, the Cambodian Embassy demanded that the above newspaper be corrected immediately.
Angkor Wat or Angkor Toch is a Khmer temple of wonder, located in the northern part of Siem Reap, Cambodia. This huge temple was first built by the Khmer king Suryavarman II in the early 12th century. Currently, Angkor Wat, Cambodia is listed as a World Heritage Site and is becoming one of the largest tourist destinations in the world, receiving millions of foreign tourists each year.
Takeo Governor Tells Cadastral Officers to Re-Inspect Plans for Trespassing in Tram Kak District
(Takeo): The Governor of Takeo Province, Mr. Ouch Phea, instructed the Director of the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction to review the case of Mr. Tram Kak District Land Chief Mr. Lon Huot who issued some land titles in Tram Kak District. Normal, leading to criticism in the press and on Facebook.
Speaking at the Traffic Dissemination Meeting of the Royal Government of Cambodia related to the Disaster Management Committee on the morning of September 13, 2019 at the Provincial Hall, Mr. Ouch Phea instructed the Director of the Provincial Cadastral Office to inspect the officials. Its re-established, especially with each issuance of a title deed.
The provincial governor said, "The case of people building a fence and breaking into a canal in Ang Ta Som commune, Tram Kak district, is a sensitive issue that the newspaper has published and posted on Facebook." The construction owner claims that they built according to their land plan issued by the Cadastral Officer.
The provincial governor added that all canals always have the back of the canal and the canal feed, and no one can issue a plan to the back of the canal to own it, so never, so please the director Cadastral review this issue, especially all local authorities to avoid problems in the future.
On that occasion, the Governor of Takeo Province also told his officials not to blame the media or social media coverage of the case of the construction of a canal in Tram Kak district, because what is published or posted is seen as a reality. However, the authorities did not ignore it, we went down to measure and have the owner dismantle the fence that encroached on the canal.
However, the authorities ordered the builders to dismantle the fence that violated the canal, and the builders have already agreed to dismantle according to the authorities' instructions. Vietnam's timber exports to increase in 2019, expect to earn $ 11 billion
The Vietnam Forestry Administration said on Friday that the Southeast Asian country could earn $ 9.4 billion from timber and wood products exports in 2018, with key export markets including the United States. Japan and China. For the whole of 2019, Vietnam plans to earn up to 11 billion USD from the export of timber and wood products, including 700 million USD from the European Union.
Vietnam currently has nearly 5,000 wood and wood products enterprises, and it is expected that in the future, 3.5 million hectares of trees will be planted for commercial purposes and will provide 35-40 hectares of timber. Million cubic meters in the next 10 years.
