(Phnom Penh): The General Department of CamControl of the Ministry of Commerce on the morning of September 13, 2019 organized the 4th Judicial Police Officer Training Course for its officers at the meeting hall of the General Department of CamControl under the coordination of Mr. Phan Oun, Deputy Director General of CamControl and Mr. Svay Samnang, Deputy Prosecutor General, were the keynote speakers.
Mr. Phan Oun, Deputy Director General of the General Department of CamControl, said that the purpose of this training was to supplement the knowledge, strengthen the capacity, roles and responsibilities of the officers of the General Department of CamControl who have been trained as law enforcement officers for law enforcement jurisdiction. In particular, the law on quality control, safety of products, goods and services to be appropriate and effective.
Mr. Svay Samnang said that before becoming a justice official, the Ministry of Justice has supplemented the capacity of CamControl officers, such as the skills of finding evidence, identifying crimes, the investigation process and the procedure to send the case to court in order to punish the perpetrators according to the law. The Judicial Police Officer Training Course has already been conducted in 4 sessions with a total of 608 participants.
It should be noted that after the Royal Government of Cambodia has simplified the task of CamControl from the border to fulfill its duties in the country, the General Department of CamControl has made more efforts to strengthen the capacity of professional officers in all fields, especially laboratory officials to protect health and safety on food. And protect economic interests, including providing inspection services for goods, food products, and ensuring warmth for the people.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh: The 2023 SEA Games in Cambodia is the biggest honor after a 54-year hiatus
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense and Chairman of CAMSOC, said that the upcoming 32nd SEA Games 2023 is the most prestigious historical event that Cambodia has hosted. Homes after a 54-year hiatus from 1959 to 2023.
At the same time, Samdech Picheay Sena advised to widely publicize this important ASEAN SEA Games 2023, issues, knowledge, wisdom, experience of organizing major sporting events to share and transfer knowledge for all of us to practice. Work efficiently and warmly to the friendly Southeast Asian countries as well as the sports tourists who are invited to participate in the SEA Games from all over the world.
The forum is also a pillar of a collaborative mechanism between all stakeholders in strategic planning towards the goals of the expected outcomes in managing sports events as well as social change events during the SEA Games. Sure.
* First: the implementation of pre-event planning, such as training of resources, players, officials, skills and experience in organizing the multi-sport game that we are implementing today * Second: planning during the event and post-event planning * Third: The organization of sports infrastructure and public infrastructure to support the above three activities is an important factor in the master plan because it is interrelated.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh stated that if we have a strategic plan, a clear roadmap, a sports infrastructure in accordance with technical standards, it will enable players and coaches to find the best quality. At the same time, we are inseparable from the flexibility, ingenuity and experience of organizing multi-sport, which is a key factor in the success of hosting.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense and Chairman of CAMSOC, instructed all sports federations to pay attention to the implementation of development plans in accordance with the five sports strategies to achieve success. Success in the upcoming 2023 SEA Games, which Cambodia is hosting.
The development plan according to the five sports strategies that Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh reminded the leaders of the sports federation include:
First, to send athletes to train abroad for short, medium and long term with high ability and quality of sports to ensure national excellence as the host of the tournament.
Second: Promote participation in the Olympic qualifying level sports and qualify for the "Ranking" internationally at all levels and as determined by the International Sports Federation.
Fourthly, pay attention to sending sports officials, coaches, referees, judges to attend overseas sports skills training courses and open accurate sports skills courses at all levels, both standard and professional sports theory.
Fifth: Promote the ability to organize events or participate in events to promote traditional sports, national identity, such as Khmer martial arts, bokator and chess, as well as other sports that are ready to be included in the SEA Games.
In order to achieve the above five sports specialization strategies, the Sports Federation, the General Secretariat, the Finance and Supply Committee, as well as the relevant institutions must pay attention to the following activities:
First, to promote and promote participation in the education of sports values, sports benefits and sports concepts of the influence of the SEA Games in the national society to be active and to strengthen cooperation with the sports authorities of the National Olympic Committee of Southeast Asian countries. Global and international Olympic movement towards the effectiveness of the SEA Games organizing process.
The remarks of the Prime Minister of Laos were made during his courtesy call on Samdech Say Chhum, Acting Head of State of Cambodia at the Senate this morning, September 13, 2019.
