(Kampot): The community of mangrove forest in Changhon village, Prek Thnout commune, Teuk Chhou district has requested the relevant authorities and institutions to take action to find the perpetrators who stole many hectares of mangrove forest in the coast of Changhon to take the land as their property. Legal punishment without parole.
However, senior officials of Kampot Provincial Hall and fisheries officials have confirmed their joint position that they will take strict action.
"The deforestation and encroachment of the perpetrators' land has been going on for about a month now without the knowledge of the relevant authorities or institutions other than the mangrove community," he said. "The site of the destruction of the mangroves above, where the perpetrators were clearing at night, was quiet and no one was passing by."
According to sources, they used to report to the village and commune authorities, especially the head of the mangrove community, but so far no measures have been taken to crack down on the crime. Therefore, they request and request the relevant authorities and professional institutions to take the strictest action against the perpetrators who are not afraid of the above law.
On September 8, 2019, Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Mr. Pil Sophal, Deputy Governor of Kampot Province also visited 33 families of Trapeang Sangke fishing community in Prek Thnout Commune, Kampot Province. Also.
Report to the Minister: Mr. Sim Him, President of the Fisheries Community, said that the community was established in 2009 and officially registered with the Ministry of Agriculture in 2011. Currently, 734 members from 527 families cover an area of 337 hectares. Throughout Prek Tnaot commune, there are 3 villages, including 37 hectares of mangrove forest, planted 30,000 more trees, and there are plans to plant more mangrove trees for the benefit of the community in the future.
Recognizing the potential of mangrove forests, the Minister encouraged and continued to support all community development and conservation activities to protect this area, which is the national natural resource and the sustainability of community economic growth both now and in the future.
In addition, the Minister advised the community leaders and members to work hard to learn more about community management, tourism, guesthouses and other services that are the basis for participating in the development of this community to grow further.
(Kampong Cham): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the Disaster Management Committee, and Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, this morning, September 13, 2019, accompanied by the leadership of civil servants, relevant departments and units, inspected the activities of Rehabilitation of Prek Achar Suon Bridge in Toul Roka Village, Peam Koh Sna Commune, Stung Trang District, Kampong Cham Province.
According to the report of Mr. Sok Srun, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kampong Cham Province, after the collapse of one of the pillars of the bridge, the technical team decided to build two more one-story billboards on the existing one. To strengthen the bridge for temporary traffic during the flood season by using 36 steel panels at the place where the pillars collapsed.
