(Kampong Thom): 70 families living in Prey village, Rolous village, Koki village, Kraing village, Dey Krahorm area in Sochet commune, Sandan district, Kampong Thom province are very worried because Kampong Thom provincial environmental officials cut down their cashew crops. 60 hectares without finding a reason to solve for them, while their family livelihood depends on this cashew crop, and some families have an area of 2 hectares, some 3 hectares and 5 hectares.
Another resident, Chheang Kheng, who lives in Pren village, said that he cleared the land in 2012 and planted 5 hectares of cashews in 2016 for three years, but was also cut down by environmental officials. He said with a sad face and worried that he had nothing to rely on.
Mr. Chhun Chen, First Deputy of Sochet Commune, said that his people enjoyed the benefits from 2011-2012 until August 7, 2019, when the environmental experts of Kampong Thom Province cut down all his cashew crops. Find a reason to solve them.
People are wondering why the land that has been used for so long has just not been able to be planted, just planted, why it has just been cut down. 70 families living in Sochet commune call on the leaders to help them find justice and provide them with land, otherwise they have nothing to rely on.
