TOP NEWS: Minister of Justice orders the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to take immediate and strict legal action against Sam Rainsy for insulting the King
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Justice has ordered the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to take the most serious and strict legal action against Sam Rainsy, who dared to insult the King, the most revered of the Cambodian people throughout the kingdom. On September 13, 2019, the Royal Palace issued a statement strongly condemning the insult to the King.
The order, signed by Minister of Justice Ang Vong Vathana on September 13, 2019, states: "Sam Rainsy's public statement has seriously damaged His Majesty's reputation. The King of the Kingdom of Cambodia is the highest deity that the Cambodian people throughout the Kingdom of Cambodia love and respect for life.
"Serious insult to the power of the King above is an act in violation of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and this act is considered a criminal offense under the provisions of Article 437 of the Penal Code. This is according to the content of the order of the Minister of Justice.
