Minister of Agriculture Instructs Forestry Administration and Department of Agriculture to Strengthen Forest Law Enforcement
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on September 13, 2019, introduced to the Forestry Administration and the Capital-Provincial Departments of Agriculture 6 points to strengthen the implementation of forest laws and related legal documents. Effective in the spirit of strengthening, preventing, eliminating, suppressing, restoring and developing community forests, forest cover, wildlife and biodiversity.
The introduction was made on the occasion of Minister Veng Sakhon presiding over the closing ceremony of the workshop on "Strengthening Forest Law Enforcement" held at the Forestry and Wildlife Training Center (Phnom Penh Thmey) on the morning of September 13. This year 2019.
The six instructions that the Minister of Agriculture gave to the Forestry Administration and the Capital-Provincial Department of Agriculture include:
First: Implement strictly according to the contents of the Notification No. 1229, dated 23 August 2019 and the Notification No. 1348, dated 12 September 2019 of the Office of the Council of Ministers.
Second, to monitor, evaluate and transparently evaluate ELCs, strictly demarcate boundaries, implement contracts and master plans clearly.
Third, to continue to monitor and strengthen the management of timber industry, handicraft, processing and timber business, as well as to take measures to prevent and eliminate the export of timber and wood products of all kinds without permission to eliminate activities. Illegal transportation with high efficiency.
Fifth, continue to cooperate well with the local authorities, the armed forces, prosecutors, courts at all levels and relevant units in order to achieve good and effective results in the spirit of Sub-Decree No. 156 dated 31st. March 2014 and Circular No. 05, dated September 22, 2016.
Aquarius signs MoU with National Police Football Club
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia Beverage Company (Coca-Cola) has signed a memorandum of understanding with the National Police Football Club for the first time in the Kingdom of Cambodia at the football field of Cambodia Beverage Factory (Coca-Cola) with the aim of becoming a strategic partner in promoting the sector. Sports as well as support the Cambodian Premier League football.
Aquarius is a well-known brand of Coca-Cola and has become the number one brand in the field of soft drinks in Japan. In Cambodia, Aquarius is recognized as a popular and prominent brand among the most competitive products.
Aquarius always pays attention to and promotes almost all kinds of sports activities from basic sports, districts, Khans, provinces, capitals to the national level.
Aquarius, for example, sponsored the "National Student Sports" program in June, the first national competition for general education students, with the participation of more than 3,000 male and female athletes. On 11 different disciplines.
In addition, recently organized a football tournament called "Aquarius Cup Trophy Kampuchea" which is composed of young people from 7 districts in Kampoul.
Cambodia Beverage Co., Ltd., the exclusive right to manufacture and distribute Coca-Cola products in Cambodia, has been continuing to provide a wide range of high quality beverage options to suit the tastes, lifestyle and diet. Different foods.
It should also be noted that after the signing ceremony was completed, there was also a friendly football match between Coca-Cola staff and the coaches of the National Police Football Club.
