Kandal Provincial Department of Public Works announces temporary suspension of waterway traffic at Prek Tamak Bridge (Video inside) (Kandal): Kandal Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport on September 12, 2019 issued a notice on waterway traffic suspension. Temporarily at Prek Tamak Bridge from September 13, 2019 until further notice.
The announcement of the Department of Public Works stated that due to the accident of the sand ferry stuck at the Prek Tamak Bridge and the technical team is rescuing, so the Department of Public Works would like to close the traffic of all types of boats, waterways, waterways on the Mekong River at the bridge. Prek Tamak is temporarily in Khsach Kandal and Muk Kampoul districts of Kandal province from 6 am on September 13, 2019 until further notice.
Please be informed that a large sand ferry collided with the Prek Tamak Bridge on the afternoon of September 7, 2019. So far, a technical team with the participation of relevant ministries is carefully preparing to remove the ferry, as the water level at the scene is very difficult, making it difficult to operate.
