Announcing the transfer and assignment of more than 400 police officers at Kampot Provincial Police
(Kampot): 446 police officers of Kampot Provincial Police were announced to transfer their duties and equip their ranks on September 12, 2019.
The ceremony was presided over by Major General Mao Chanthurith, Kampot Provincial Police Commissioner, and was attended by several commissioners and relevant police officers.
Speaking on that occasion, Major General Mao Chanthurith urged all police officers to pay more attention to the work, be responsible for the implementation of roles and responsibilities, be honest with the people and respond to timely intervention.
In addition, the General Commissioner also instructed the officers to take turns to strengthen and continue to strictly implement the Rule 006 of the National Police Force to increase the new capacity to work in the unit effectively and efficiently.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor Holds a Meeting to Discuss Water Shortage Challenges
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, held a meeting to discuss the problem of lack of clean water for the people in Sihanoukville with the participation of Mr. Ounha Kok An, President of Ankor (Water Supply). Preah Sihanouk Province and professional officers at Preah Sihanouk Provincial Hall on September 12, 2019.
Mr. Oknha Kok An, President of Anco (Water Supply Company) confirmed that the company has been increasing the network of pipelines from 400 to 600 lines and increasing the construction of water reservoirs up to 100. 000 cubic meters and will continue to distribute water to Sihanoukville per day 10,000 cubic meters in 2016 and 35,000 cubic meters in 2019.
The company currently has a water treatment plant, a water storage and distribution station near the RCI factory in Sangkat 1, Sihanoukville, and plans to build a third water treatment plant in the future to increase the amount of water distributed to people and Business locations in Sihanoukville and some districts such as Prey Nob and Stung Hav.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun said that the provincial administration has explored all means to address the concerns of the lack of clean water for the people of Sihanoukville, despite the rainy season, some areas in Sihanoukville still face shortages of clean water. Days. On the other hand, because Sihanoukville is a highland area, there are some high places that do not have enough clean water for daily use.
As a result, Anco (Water Supply) has agreed to follow the instructions of the Governor of Sihanoukville to increase the production of water supply to the people according to the needs of the people in Sihanoukville.
