623 Families Affected by Floods in Kratie City and Chit Borei District, Kratie Province Receive Joint Humanitarian Donations from the Cambodian Red Cross and the National Committee for Disaster Management
(Kratie): On September 12, 2019, the Cambodian Red Cross, chaired by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, assigned a team from the Cambodian Red Cross Headquarters to bring humanitarian aid to flood victims. 623 families living in Kratie city and Chet Borey district.
The ceremony was held at two safe places, the first safe place in Kratie city for 188 families and the second safe place in Bos Leav commune, Chit Borei district for 435 families.
The ceremony was also attended by General Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, Mr. Vathorn, Honorary Chairman of the Branch, Mr. Thorn Kry, Chairman of the Branch Committee.
On the occasion of the meeting with the victims, Dr. Uy Samath, Director of the Disaster Management Department of the Cambodian Red Cross, brought the words of Samdech Kittipritthbandit, President, who sent a message of deep love and concern for all the people affected by the floods in the rainy season. This.
At the same time, General Kun Kim said that Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen has always considered the well-being of the people and assigned officials under Get down regularly and save people's lives from the impact, do your best.
Finally, the General thanked and appreciated the people who know how to monitor the flood situation regularly and evacuated to safety in a timely manner without endangering lives.
Please note that in addition to the donations provided by the Cambodian Red Cross, including: 1 box of noodles, 10 cans of fish, all 623 flood-affected families also received: 25 kg of rice from the National Committee for Disaster Management And provinces. Separately, Kratie Provincial Health Department also supported one mosquito net per family.
