Japan vows to help Cambodia strengthen tourism professionals when there are flights from Japan to Siem Reap by the end of 2019
(Phnom Penh): Representatives of the ASEAN-Japan Center expressed optimism in front of the leadership of the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia that when there is a direct flight connection from some major cities of Japan to Siem Reap - Angkor at the end of 2019 tourists Japan and tourists from third countries will increase in Cambodia, so Cambodia needs to expand and strengthen the capacity of tourism professionals even more.
Along with such confidence, the ASEAN-Japan Center is also committed to assisting the Cambodian side to increase the training and capacity building of more Japanese language tourism professionals to prepare for the future growth of Japanese tourism.
During the opening ceremony, the Secretary of State highlighted the growth of Cambodia's tourism sector under the shadow of peace and development in all areas arising from the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Mr. Pak Sokhom continued that this training workshop was organized on time and in accordance with the request of tourism experts in building human resources in the tourism sector, especially to improve the Japanese language skills to become more proficient. In order to provide better and more satisfying tourism services from tourists, especially Japanese tourists who have been steadily increasing in visiting Cambodia.
It should be noted that for the first seven months of 2019, Cambodia received more than 3.8 million international tourists, an increase of 11.1% compared to the same period in 2018, in which Cambodia received Japanese tourists. 113,159 people, an increase of about 2.6%. It is estimated that by 2020, Cambodia will be able to receive about 7 million international tourists and create nearly 1 million direct jobs.
Meanchey District Governor Urges Relevant Authorities to Crack Down on All Kinds of Gambling
(Phnom Penh): Meanchey District Governor Mr. Pich Keo Mony urged all relevant authorities, including the Sangkat Unity Command, to crack down on all forms of gambling, regardless of the location of the net and fishing games and cockfighting venues in the parallel district. At the request of the people.
The urging of the authorities to crack down on this crime took place at the Meanchey District Council Dissemination and Consultation Forum of the 3rd Mandate under the chairmanship of Mr. Em Sok Leang, Khan Councilor and Mr. Pich Keo Mony, Meanchey District Governor on the morning of September 12. This year 2019.
He added that within a month from now, all online games, entertainment, fishing games, including shopping malls and cockfighting must be eliminated.
Mr. Meanchey District Governor emphasized that the tasks assigned now must be carried out, regardless of whether the Deputy Governor in charge of Police Inspector, Chief of Administration Post must crack down from now on.
