The President of the National Assembly of Cambodia is satisfied and supports the results of the cooperation between the Government of Cambodia and Laos.
(Phnom Penh): During a meeting with Dr. Thongloun Sisoulit, Prime Minister of Laos, on the afternoon of September 12, 2019 at the National Assembly, Samdech Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, expressed his support for the outcome of the bilateral talks between the two heads of government. Of the two countries on the morning of September 12 to further strengthen cooperation for the benefit of both sides.
Dr. Thongloun Sisoulit said that the Prime Ministers of the two countries signed a joint statement to strengthen the friendship and cooperation between the two countries in the sense of "comprehensive partnership, stability and prosperity." Long-term.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin expressed his great pleasure to see the progress of the traditional friendship and cooperation between Cambodia and Laos in all fields, which has brought benefits. The highest between the two nations.
The President praised and supported the efforts of the governments of Cambodia and Laos in erecting the demarcation line, which achieved 86%. Samdech encourages the two governments to continue to discuss and resolve the remaining issues in the spirit of friendship, honesty and mutual trust in order to turn the border of peace, friendship, cooperation and development into a legacy for future generations.
Samdech Heng Samrin also briefed the Prime Minister on the good relations and cooperation between the two parliaments. The National Assembly of Cambodia and Laos exchanged experiences at all levels. In particular, the two parliaments have supported each other on the international stage through inter-parliamentary forums.
