(Phnom Penh): Secretary of State for the Ministry of Tourism, Ms. Hun Dany, on behalf of Dr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, on September 12, 2019, presided over the opening ceremony of a workshop on Gender Mainstreaming on "Leadership and Enhancement." Economic empowerment for women ”in tourism. The ceremony was held at the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia (NOCC) in Phnom Penh.
The workshop was organized by the Ministry of Tourism with the aim of enhancing the capacity of gender facilitators in the capital, provincial and private tourism departments to better understand the art of public speaking, leadership, economic empowerment for women, and Gender policy in tourism.
The goal of empowering women is to reduce women's vulnerability, maintain economic growth, and strengthen the role of men in society as an integral part of society.
She stated that Cambodia's tourism sector is considered "green gold" as a priority sector is set in the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 of the Royal Government. This sector has been strongly involved in promoting socio-economic development, contributing to job creation, improving living standards and reducing poverty.
Currently, there are about 620,000 direct workers in this sector, of which about 60% are women. Therefore, white women play an important role in the development of tourism by being present in all services, in addition to private women in the tourism industry and outstanding women. The Ministry of Tourism always encourages them to have the courage to participate more in response to the growth as well as the needs of tourists.
