Director of Forestry Administration instructs Forestry Administration officers to continue cracking down on forest crime in protected areas
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Keo Omalis, the Royal Government of Cambodia delegate in charge of the Forestry Administration, instructed all Forestry Administration officials to continue to work to crack down on forest crime in protected areas more effectively in order to implement it. The order of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia that has been issued so far.
This kind of introduction by Dr. Keo Omalis was made this morning, September 12, 2019, on the occasion of the opening of the seminar on "Strengthening the implementation of forest law" in Phnom Penh with the participation of From the leadership of the Forestry Administration, the director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, district chiefs, section chiefs, commune chiefs, forestry administrators across the country, a total of 400 people.
The purpose of this workshop is to strengthen the implementation of the law more effectively and increase awareness of the law and legal documents in order to support the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia on forest protection.
At the same time, the Director of the Forestry Administration further urged the Forestry Administration officers to carry out research, control and crackdown in their areas of management and in protected areas that are suffering from illegal logging in almost all areas in order to jointly prevent and suppress the crime. Violate the forest to be highly effective.
