Lt. Gen. Hun Manet Brings Out Proud Results for the Cambodian Army and the Cambodian People on the International Stage
(Thailand): Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander-in-Chief and Commander of the Cambodian Army, has brought proud and national prestige results for the Cambodian Army and the Cambodian people across the country on the international stage.
Bringing pride and prestige to the nation took place on the occasion of the Lieutenant General attending the three-day Indo-Pacific Army Commander-in-Chief Conference from 9 to 11 September 2019 at Thailand. The conference was chaired by the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Thailand Prayuth Chan-o-cha and was attended by the commanders of the land forces of the superpowers and regions.
This is another development in which the Commander of the Cambodian Armed Forces, General Hun Manet, has strengthened and expanded relations and cooperation with the Commander of the Armed Forces, world powers and other regions, which is a source of national pride and prestige for the Army. Cambodia and the Cambodian people across the country.
