Veal Veng District Gendarmerie Commander said that during the crackdown, police arrested two suspects, including Ms. Kang Hev (Yeay Hev), the owner of Kang Hev Restaurant and Ms. Kang La, the owner of Srey La Restaurant. Exhibits of more than 172 kilograms of wildlife meat, including: 57 kilograms of scorpion meat, 68 kilograms of wild boar meat, 28 kilograms of ox meat, 9 kilograms of test meat, 8 kilograms of turtle meat and 2 game meat. 5 kg.
Speaking at St. Petersburg, Mr. Thong Rathasak, Director General of Tourism Development and International Cooperation of the Ministry of Tourism, said that at the 23rd General Assembly, the World Tourism Organization (WTO) showed the growth of world tourists in the first six months of 2019. Receiving 671 million tourists, an increase of 4% compared to the same period in 2018.
Among the growth in tourism that the world has received are: Middle East, 8%, Asia-Pacific, 6%, Europe, 4%, Africa, 3% and 3%, respectively. The Americas grew 2%. In Southeast Asia, Southeast Asia and East Asia also increased by 1-5%.
He added that the 4% growth in world tourism was in line with the World Tourism Organization's forecast last year and was an important economic trend for the whole world.
According to the World Tourism Organization, the factors that drive the growth of tourism is due to the participation of a number of relevant sectors, such as new tourism products have been created to facilitate the travel of tourists, especially road travel. Air combined with airfare is also more affordable and visas for tourists have also been facilitated.
But while celebrating the growth, the World Tourism Organization (WTO) is also concerned about the impact on tourism caused by the trade war crisis between the United States and China, Britain's exit from the European Union (Brexit) and Some of the problems that arose from the Industrial Revolution 4.0.
