Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Calls on Flood Victims to Be Extremely Vigilant
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, called on the people affected by the floods to be very careful and hurry to the nearest health station when their families are sick or have poisonous animals or bites.
Mr. Un Chanda said this morning, September 12, 2019, on the occasion that he led the team to visit and distribute gifts to 33 families affected by floods in Srey Santhor district. Kampong Cham.
Mr. Un Chanda said that during the rainy season, the health department is ready to provide medicine to supply health problems, especially diarrhea and rabies or bites to the people, the health department also has a team. Doctors are on duty 24 hours a day and will transport patients such as cars and buses to the Kampong Cham Provincial Referral Hospital in severe cases.
It should be noted that during the visit and conversation with the flood victims, the provincial governor distributed some tents and money to 33 families to alleviate the hardships and reduce costs to some extent.
Please note that Kampong Cham has about 197 safe places in the 9 districts - cities are ready, including the supply of clean water, medicine and a team of doctors on duty 24 hours.
