In a joint statement between the leaders of the two countries, obtained by Fresh News on September 12, 2019, it was stated: "Both sides have agreed to promote cooperation between the sister cities. "Phnom Penh and Vientiane and between Siem Reap and Champasak."
In addition, the two sides agreed to urge their respective officials in border provinces to hold regular meetings and consultations to enhance cooperation and mutual assistance in all areas of mutual benefit. Come back.
The two sides agreed to further enhance cooperation within the sub-regional framework and regional mechanisms for comprehensive and sustainable regional economic development through the implementation of the agreement. Existing, especially within the framework of Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam development triangle cooperation.
It should be noted that Dr. Thongloun Sisoulit led a high-level delegation to Cambodia at around 9:30 am on September 12, 2019 for a two-day official visit on 12-13. September 2019 at the invitation of the Prime Minister of Cambodia.
"The two sides agreed to enhance the relationship between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Lao People's Democratic Republic to the level of a comprehensive and long-term strategic partnership in order to strengthen and expand the spirit of solidarity as a brotherhood," the joint statement said. "And cooperation between the two countries in the fields of politics, security, economy and socio-culture."
The joint statement stressed that the two sides will continue to develop friendly relations based on international law, especially the principles enshrined in the UN Charter and the ASEAN Charter.
The joint statement reiterated that the two sides reaffirmed mutual trust and confidence and adhered to the principle of non-interference in each other's internal affairs, non-use of force or threats of force. Resolve disputes peacefully and do not allow any foreign politicians or armed forces to use their territory against the other side.
Dr. Thongloun Sisoulit led a high-level delegation to Cambodia at around 9:30 am on September 12, 2019 for a two-day official visit on September 12-13. September 2019 at the invitation of the Prime Minister of Cambodia.
"Both sides have agreed to assign the Joint Boundary Commission of the two countries to jointly draft a border demarcation treaty between the Kingdom of Cambodia and Cambodia as soon as possible," the joint statement said. The Lao People's Democratic Republic is concerned about the demarcation of the border, which the two sides have already demarcated 86% of the border between the two countries.
The joint statement added that for the remaining border demarcation, the two sides agreed to continue discussions to find a peaceful solution as soon as possible.
The two sides also agreed to assign the Joint Boundary Commission of the two countries to discuss the erection of additional border posts on 86 percent of the border and to produce a border map showing the border line, the statement said. Which both parties have accepted as an annex to the above-mentioned treaty.
