Ministry of Interior Signs a Memorandum of Understanding with the European Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia on Combating Imports of Counterfeit Products
(Phnom Penh): The Committee on Combating Counterfeit Products, which pose a high risk to health and social safety (CPPCC), the Ministry of Interior and the European Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia (EUROCHAM) this morning. In 2019, a Memorandum of Understanding was signed on "Cooperation in the fight against the import, production and distribution of counterfeit products in Cambodia."
The ceremony took place in accordance with the Royal Decree No. 46 of the Royal Government of Cambodia dated 21 June 2019, which granted General Miech Sophanna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Chairman of the NEC. PK to sign the Memorandum of Understanding.
He added that the signing of the MoU is a mechanism and further strengthens the responsibility of protecting partnerships in the business sector for the trust and influx of foreign investors to Cambodia from European countries and countries. Countries around the world. In the past, the CPP has cracked down on hundreds of tons of illegal counterfeit products and arrested the perpetrators and prosecuted them in dozens of cases.
He hoped that the agreement signed today would be another important driving force and reason for urging the European Union to reconsider Cambodia's intentions and willingness to work with the European Union and the world to protect The interests of both domestic and foreign investors and economic growth, peace, prosperity, respect for each other's interests and non-interference in the sovereignty of their respective countries.
"By signing the long-awaited MoU, we hope that not only our members but also the entire private sector will see their claims against fraud properly," he said. Resolved effectively.
Mr. ARNAUD Darc also called for close and effective cooperation between all relevant authorities, such as the Ministry of Interior, the General Department of Customs and Excise, the Ministry of Justice and the Ministry of Health in cases of counterfeit medicines and cosmetics. Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh sends a message of condolences to Mrs. Kham Phean, wife of Elder Bou Thong and her family
