Read the full text of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh's message: Construction of the new passenger terminal of Sihanoukville Airport will start in early 2020 with a capacity of 3.6 million passengers
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Mao Hovannal, Minister in Charge of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation, chaired a technical meeting to review and pass on the master plan on expanding the infrastructure of Sihanoukville International Airport on September 12, 2019 with a presentation. Alan Brown, the new Director General of the Airport Concession Company (SCA) and the team.
In principle, the master plan for the expansion of the infrastructure of Sihanoukville International Airport, proposed by the Airport Concession Company (SCA), was approved by the technical working group at this meeting.
At the same time, the Minister also advised all stakeholders to cooperate well to achieve the goal of construction to be completed as planned, especially to prepare for the special flight of the top leaders from the countries. Cambodia will host the ASEAN Summit at the end of 2022.
Please be informed that according to the master plan, the new terminal of Sihanoukville International Airport will start construction in early 2020 with a capacity of 3.6 million passengers for the first phase in mid-2022 and has the capacity to expand to accommodate more passengers. Up to more than 10 million people in the next phase.
In addition, the international airport is in the process of expanding its runway from 2,500 meters to 3,300 meters (800 meters) and is scheduled to be completed by mid-2020, which will be able to accommodate all types of aircraft, including large-scale. Other infrastructure of the airport has also been strengthened and expanded in response to the current surge in domestic and international flights.
