Ministry of Planning Launches New Poor Household Identity Data Management System
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kittisetha Dr. Chhay Thorn, Senior Minister and Minister of Planning, this morning, September 12, 2019, presided over the opening ceremony of the seminar to disseminate and launch the new poor family identification data management system. The ceremony was held at the Cambodiana Hotel in Phnom Penh.
According to Senior Minister Chhay Thorn, in order to ensure the effectiveness and acceleration of poverty reduction, the Ministry of Planning has prepared two sets of service interventions, including:
* First: Service Intervention Kit to Increase Income * Second: Service Intervention Kit to Reduce Costs by Focusing on the Poor and Most Vulnerable People to Improve Livelihoods, Develop Human Resources and Protect Them from Potential Crisis Causing them to fall into poverty or aggravate their difficult situation.
Minister Chhay Thorn stated that in order to achieve the objectives of this work, we really need the data of poor families, which specifies the name of the head of the family, the number of family members and the place where the family lives and is serial in each village, commune, sangkat. Is an indispensable need.
At the same time, the Minister also said that the Royal Government of Cambodia is continuing to strive to achieve the vision of Cambodia 2030 and 2050 as a high middle income country and a high income country. In this context, the Royal Government of Cambodia recognizes that the development of the social protection system is an important factor in achieving equitable and environmental economic growth.
He said that based on a high sense of responsibility, the Royal Government has set a long-term vision for the development of the social protection system is to build a social protection system that is environmentally effective and financially sustainable as a tool to reduce and prevent poverty. Vulnerability and inequality and contribute to the development and protection of human resources more widely and promote economic growth.
Senior Minister Chhay Thorn said that based on this vision and on the basis of political stability, macroeconomic stability and the results of socio-economic development, the Royal Government has adopted a comprehensive national social protection policy framework 2016-2025, focusing on On the two pillars are the social assistance system and the social security system.
Aims to develop a strategic plan to ensure income security and reduce the economic and financial vulnerabilities of the people, to promote welfare and social solidarity, as well as to reduce poverty to the maximum. This is the additional emphasis of Minister Chhay Thorn.
Senior Minister Chhay Thorn emphasized that the National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025 is to nurture, consolidate and strengthen existing programs to increase the efficiency, transparency and consistency of programs in the social protection system.
The Minister also said that the Ministry of Planning has continued to revise the questionnaire and database of poor households to diversify the data: poor families with HIV and AIDS, poor families with disabled family members Veterans, poor families, the elderly and so on.
