Kampot provincial governor orders authorities to use an unidentified bulldozer to rape a man at the mouth of the Kbal Romeas creek in Teuk Chhou district
The direct order of the Governor of Kampot Province was made on September 11, 2019 at the point of natural canal near Kbal Romeas Bridge, north of National Road 33 in Trapeang Thom Village, Chum Kreal Commune, Teuk Chhou District, Kampot Province.
Mr. Chiao Tai stated that all public lands of the state can not be occupied by any person or intentionally encroached upon illegally. Obviously, this land location is a tributary of the canal, which plays an important role in releasing water into the Kbal Romeas canal into the sea.
The provincial governor also instructed the relevant authorities to remove the rubble that was poured into the canal as soon as possible and also reminded the local authorities as well as the relevant authorities before allowing any people to apply for a permit to pour. Land for the development of a site must be adequately checked for all legal documents to see if the site for which the people have applied for the land has a legal title.
He stressed that otherwise, the local authorities should not allow the land to be dumped, because such a ban is to jointly prevent all crimes or individuals who often encroach on public or private land that leads to disputes. Land disputes will cause difficulties for the authorities or leaders.
