In this video, Mr. Kem Sokha made it clear to himself that since 1993, after being elected to the first House of Representatives, he was first called by the United States to the United States as a Cambodian politician, and until he resigned from a political party. Standing on the orders of foreigners in 2002, established an organization called the Cambodian Center for Human Rights.
In the video, Kem Sokha stated that in order to carry out his policies successfully, the United States had instructed him to follow the example of the revolutions of Yugoslavia and Serbia, which overthrew the legitimate government. A dictatorship.
And the plan to make a revolution to overthrow the legitimate Royal Government of Cambodia, Mr. Kem Sokha added that he did not follow his own ideas alone, he received training from experts. Professors at universities in Washington and Canada, hired by the United States to provide him with strategies to change leaders in Cambodia.
In connection with Kem Sokha's revelations about the plot to overthrow the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Hun Sen, has previously questioned whether Kem Sokha was the sole accuser of the United States. Is the US accusing Kem Sokha?
It should be noted that the release of three videos that led to the arrest of Kem Sokha came after a US State Department spokesman released a video calling on the Cambodian government to drop the charges against Kem Sokha. .
A State Department spokeswoman issued a statement on the night of September 10, 2019 in response to a statement from US State Department spokeswoman Morgan Ortagus.
A spokesman for the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs also reminded that "the failure to attempt to push for regime change through non-democratic means is not an exercise in fundamental human rights and democracy." The Royal Government of Cambodia has the full sovereignty to take the necessary legal action against any person or entity that violates the Cambodian Constitution and other applicable laws aimed at protecting its national security and the rule of law. ”
Below is the video shown by the Ministry of Justice: Samdech Techo ordered to pay the salary for September and 50,000 Riel allowance to civil servants in the second week to celebrate Pchum Ben
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of Pchum Ben 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, decided to pay the salary for September once and provide 50,000 Riels per person to the Armed Forces civil servants. Contract staff, floating staff and retired officials across the country in the second week of September.
This decision of the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia was made this morning, September 11, 2019 in the Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers to discuss and cross some agenda at the Peace Palace.
According to the announcement of the results of the Cabinet meeting, which was received by Fresh News, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that on the occasion of Pchum Ben 2563, the Royal Government decided to pay salaries. For September, a total of 50,000 Riels per person will be provided to civil servants, armed forces, contracted staff, floating staff and retired officers in the second week of September.
(Pursat): There were two other cases of violence caused by drinking alcohol, with one woman pulling a knife, stabbing her husband, her intestines ruptured, and the other drunkenly beating his wife, breaking her head and bleeding.
Case 1: A housewife who could not resist arguing with her husband pulled out a knife and stabbed her husband, causing his stomach to rupture. His family sent him to Pursat Referral Hospital in Pursat Province.
This rare incident happened at 4:30 pm on September 11, 2019 at the victim's house in Dey Krahorm village, Anlong Reap commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province.
Mr. Theang Leng said that before the incident, the suspect had been drinking heavily because he was addicted to alcohol. Caused serious injuries, ruptured left abdomen, sent to emergency room at Pursat Provincial Referral Hospital.
Currently, the victim has recovered a bit and is waiting for further treatment, while the housewife, who was very drunk, was arrested and sent to the Veal Veng District Police Inspectorate for processing.
Case 2: On the morning of September 11, 2019, in Kampeng village, Prongel commune, Phnom Kravanh district, the police arrested a suspect named Tith Sengly, 56 years old, who was drunk. A hot water pipe hit the victim's wife, Wen Phally, 53, on the left side of her head, causing her to bleed three stitches. In this case, the authorities promised to educate and return home as well.
