Prudential Cambodia opens new branch in Kratie
(Kratie): Prudential Cambodia, a leading life insurance company in Cambodia, has opened a new branch to expand its business in Kratie. The establishment of this new branch is also to meet the growing needs of financial security and long-term financial planning, as well as provide peace of mind to families in Cambodia.
The inauguration ceremony was presided over by Mr. Tuy Bun Sereyroth, Deputy Governor of Kratie Province, Mr. David Nutman, Executive Director of Prudential Cambodia and Mr. In Matra, Representative of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, as well as distinguished guests and staff of Prudential. The new branch is located on Sihanoukville Road in the center of Kratie.
The inauguration of the new branch means that Prudential Cambodia is currently present in Kratie, Siem Reap, Battambang and Phnom Penh. The company also plans to expand its business to cover other major cities in the future. Prudential Cambodia Life Insurance products are also available through ACLEDA Bank, a partner bank since 2013. There are 156 branches nationwide.
Mr. David Nutman stated, “Prudential Cambodia is proud to be the leading life insurance company in the country and the most trusted company by its customers. We are committed to serving the protection needs of the Cambodian people and helping them achieve their long-term financial goals by providing our best professional services and solutions. ”
Prudential Cambodia has recently achieved a remarkable achievement, becoming the first life insurance company in Cambodia to sell 200,000 insurance policies, with a total savings and savings of over $ 4.3 billion (as of June 2019), which reflects the growing confidence in the company's products and services.
He added that the insurance sector has two main components: providing savings and protection that is different from other sectors. Encourage the company to build trust and confidence for its customers and wish Prudential success in its business.
