Mr. Hang Puthea confirmed this to the media at Phnom Penh International Airport on the morning of September 11, 2019, after concluding his official visit to Russia to learn and gain experience related to the use of digital systems. In the election process with the NEC from about 30 other countries.
Mr. Hang Puthea emphasized that this visit to Russia has two main tasks: 1: Participate in the International Conference on "Digital Use in the Electoral Process" and 2: Participate in observing the lower house elections in the city. Moscow
He added that Russia was the first to organize a digital election, and the NEC of Cambodia and more than 30 other countries were participating in the survey.
Regarding the question of whether the NEC of Cambodia will use digital in the election process? Mr. Hang Puthea explained that he would report on the digital voting process to NEC members and expert committees to learn more about whether or not we should use the digital voting system.
However, he believes that the use of digital in the electoral process is good, but not certain that it can be implemented within the framework of Cambodia in the current situation. Cambodia needs laws, budgets, capacity, officials, electricity and internet ....
Negative factors include:
* Social and unprofessional social media can be used to serve any political group that hinders the progress of democracy and elections through the spread of more confusing information.
Anonymous inside and outside the country can attack computer systems, etc. As for participating in the lower house election observation in Moscow, Mr. Hang Puthea assessed the extent to which he observed that there were some areas in Russia. Use digital and some areas do not use digital. Overall, the election in Moscow, Russia went smoothly.
He informed that the NEC of Cambodia has already used some digital systems, such as the transition from manual voter registration to computerized registration. The NEC is also considering setting up a program to register political parties and candidates using a computer system for the upcoming election. Pursat Provincial Governor Meets 7 Candidates for A-Level Candidates
(Pursat): Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province, on the afternoon of September 11, 2019, allowed teachers, guardians of students, especially candidates of Pursat Province, who received 7 A-Levels in the High School Diploma Examination. 2019 Meet and greet politely at his office in Pursat Provincial Hall.
Each of the seven candidates received a laptop and 300,000 Riels to encourage and congratulate them on their efforts. Separately, 12 teachers each received 500,000 Riels, 14 parents each received 3 sarongs and 50,000 Riels.
Mr. Mao Thunin expressed his high pride with the efforts of all of them to succeed in passing the high school diploma exam, which took place on 19-20 August 2019, especially in Pursat province. Score A 7 people.
At the same time, he would like to thank the parents, teachers, the team to help the grassroots and all stakeholders who have contributed to support, motivate, teach and teach all the children to be successful today.
Mr. Mao Thunin reminded the children to continue their efforts to study to achieve their dreams in the future and to contribute to the development of our province to grow under this strong peace. Kratie Asia Institute of Cambodia Continues Cooperation with Partners to Develop Education
(Kratie): The Asia Institute of Cambodia, Kratie Province, has continued to cooperate with partner countries to develop its education sector, strengthen the quality and capacity of its education to compete with other institutes and universities in capturing students. Come to study at your institute.
In fact, on the morning of September 11, 2019, the University of Indonesia (UII) was invited to visit and exchange experiences of its successful teaching work to show students and professors at the Asia-Cambodia Institute in order to continue the cooperation. Partner.
According to Ms. Chan Soulikar, a third year student, she confirmed the benefits of the institute and cooperation, gaining new knowledge and experience through study tours with her university at home and abroad, especially the living environment. In society and partner countries in the world as well.
She added that working with overseas partners is important because the Asian Director of Cambodia has increased the exchange program to study both in the country and abroad and give him new experiences and new ideas. .
The Director of the Asian Institute of Cambodia added that the purpose is to strengthen and improve the quality of education of the Institute to be in line with national and international curricula to compete with human resources with ASEAN countries or to work in the country. ASEAN as well.
The study tour of the University of Indonesia is now on the partnership in the Association of more than 81 schools of ASEAN countries in order to provide opportunities for students to learn and gain new knowledge and experience from Partner universities and living cultures of countries in the world, and especially to collaborate, strengthen the teaching work of professors and exchange professors with each other.
In addition, the Institute has 17 ASEAN-China partner schools, of which there are 3 schools in Cambodia: the Asian Institute of Cambodia, Svay Rieng University, and Meanchey University, which are partners this year and will host the event. ASEAN-China Meeting with Svay Rieng University to Strengthen Further Cooperation
(Kandal): Authorities decided to suspend the construction of the statue of "Preah Si Ary Metrey" on Phnom Saang in Saang Phnom commune, Saang district, Kandal province after finding that it was built illegally. The suspension was made on the afternoon of September 11, 2019.
Local police officials said that the suspension of the construction of the statue without permission was made by the force of the Saang District Police Inspectorate in cooperation with the police force of Saang Phnom Commune Administration Post and with the participation of relevant authorities.
According to the report, the construction was only a letter from the commune chief, but the pagoda committee and the monks did not know and did not allow it.
Please be reminded that the statue of "Preah Siare Metrey" was built by a person who claimed to be a military officer on Phnom Saang in Saang Phnom commune, Saang district, Kandal province, which was worshiped by monks and Buddhists there. There are priests and claim that there is no permit from the authorities and professional officials.
The man, identified as Yem Rachana, who also claims to be a military officer, used workers to pay for the statue on a natural stone that had grown on Phnom Saang for a long time, but there were no relevant authorities. One goes down to interrogate to do the prevention.
The above information was leaked from the working group to strengthen Saang Phnom commune when meeting with monks and Buddhists to organize the Pchum Ben festival on Phnom Saang on the afternoon of September 10, 2019.
Sources from the Saang Phnom Commune Reconstruction Team confirmed to Fresh News that they would like to ask for help from a person named Rachana who has been building a statue of "Preah Siare Metrey" on a large natural stone that has already grown in On Phnom Saang without permission or any letter from the authorities as well as professional officials. Minister Pan Sosak Leads a Cambodian Delegation to the 51st ASEAN Economic Ministers' Meeting and Related Meetings
(Thailand): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Minister of ASEAN Economy for Cambodia, led a Cambodian delegation to attend the 51st ASEAN Economic Ministers' Meeting and Related Meetings in Bangkok, Thailand from May 5-10. September 2019 and get the following results:
Bilateral Meeting with the ASEAN-US Business Council: The Minister warmly welcomed the ASEAN-US Business Council delegation led by Ambassador Michael Michalak, Senior Vice President, ASEAN-US Business Council and informed The Royal Government of Cambodia is committed to promoting trade, investment and the business environment in Cambodia.
During the meeting, the Minister recommended the ASEAN-US Business Council to have a representative in Cambodia to help promote business activities as well as cooperation between the two countries. The meeting also discussed Cambodia's plans to improve infrastructure, connectivity, good governance and human resource development, digital economy, e-commerce and small and medium enterprise development.
