More Than 1,000 Families in Tbong Khmum Province Affected by Floods Evacuated to Safety, Senior Minister Kun Kim and Provincial Governor Distribute Donations
(Tbong Khmum): More than 1,000 families were evacuated to safety in Tonle Beit commune, Tbong Khmum province because their houses were completely flooded. These people come from four communes: Chiro 1 commune, Tonle Bit commune, Boeung Boul commune and Peam Chiliang commune, Tbong Khmum district, Tbong Khmum province.
Due to such natural floods, on September 11, 2019, Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management and Tbong Khmum Provincial Governor, Mr. Cheam Chansophorn, cooperated with Caritas Cambodia to respond in time by assisting 4 boats Equipment and engine, 1 boat, 2 tanks, 4 toilets, 2 mixed water tanks, 125 blue tents to distribute and check the condition.
Separately, the National Committee for Disaster Management, 400 tents for relief for daily use.
Speaking on the occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim, on behalf of the disaster, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, also commended the provincial authorities for their timely rescue work to ensure that no one was harmed.
In addition, Senior Minister Kun Kim thanked Caritas Cambodia for its continuous cooperation in the event of a disaster and thanked the Ministry of Health for taking a doctor to a safe place to be ready to help with other ailments. ⁇.
