Royal Government Releases 1,000 Tons of Rice and 2 Billion Riels to the National Committee for Disaster Management to Prepare for Flood Victims (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, announces that the Royal Government Cambodia has decided to release 1,000 tons of rice and 2 billion riels to the National Committee for Disaster Management to prepare for the relief of people in the provinces facing floods.
The announcement of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made at the meeting of the Council of Ministers at the Peace Palace this morning, September 11, 2019, discussing and approving some of the planned agenda.
According to the announcement of the results of today's cabinet meeting, during the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has decided to release 1,000 tons of rice and 2 billion riels. To the National Committee for Disaster Management to prepare for the rescue of people in the provinces facing floods.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also ordered the National Committee for Disaster Management to cooperate with the Cambodian Red Cross to bring rice and other supplies to distribute to flood victims.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen further stated that the Royal Government has also instructed ministries, institutions and local administrations at all levels to cooperate in providing rice seeds to farmers in the provinces who have grown rain-fed rice and suffered. Damage caused by floods.
