Ministry of Social Affairs: Community rehabilitation for people with disabilities as a strategy for poverty reduction and the inclusion of people with disabilities in society
(Pursat): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation recognizes that community rehabilitation for people with disabilities is a strategy for rehabilitation, equal opportunities, poverty reduction and inclusion. In society. This work has played an important role in promoting the access to social services and the full right to participate in social activities.
The common principles of community rehabilitation work are environment, participation, sustainability, empowerment, self-advocacy, and a non-disruptive environment for people with disabilities, and it has the potential to improve the lives of people with disabilities. Social attitudes toward people with disabilities as well.
This was stated by Mr. Nhek Vannara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and a representative of Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation at a workshop to exchange experiences on environmentally friendly community development programs in Pursat. For 2 days from September 11-12, 2019.
The workshop was also attended by Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province, Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation of Pursat Province and many other national and international partner organizations.
Mr. Nhek Vannara added that the workshop was aimed at compiling documents related to the Eco-Community Development Program, which was previously a community rehabilitation program but has now been transformed into an Eco-Community Development Program. And Cambodia plans to host in 2023.
He added that in order to carry out this work successfully and effectively, those who play an important role in this work are:
1. At the national level, relevant ministries and institutions act as managers, coordinators and planners, provide capacity building, monitor and evaluate community rehabilitation programs. Cooperation between relevant ministries, institutions and NGOs should be strengthened.
2. At the capital and provincial levels, the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and other departments are responsible for overseeing activities and providing reports to the national level on the progress of rehabilitation work in the community.
3. At the grassroots level, the Office of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, commune councils, NGO staff, village chiefs, the disabled, their families and their communities should work together to implement and support effective community rehabilitation activities. -
Mr. Nhek Vannara stated that this workshop is really short, but it is very important for the work management, coordination and implementation at the national, capital, provincial and local levels to strengthen the quality and efficiency of rehabilitation services in the community. For the disabled.
He expects that by presenting the results and strengths, the points should be improved, the sharing of good experiences from each other and the discussions of the workshop, we will get fruitful results and good recommendations to be a compass for Preparation of action plans for the next year.
