Oil tanker touches Ballet Bridge across Tonle Sap, authorities temporarily suspend traffic across the bridge
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, told Fresh News this morning, September 11, 2019 that the authorities decided to temporarily stop traffic across the Ballet Bridge connecting Russey Keo to Chroy Changvar. This morning, to inspect after the bridge was hit by Savimex oil tanker at 3 pm on September 10 yesterday.
The director of the department confirmed that officials and relevant authorities were immediately inspecting the scene to confirm whether the collision affected the bridge or not. As a preliminary result, the construction team needed some time to complete the repairs and resume normal operations in the coming days.
Please be informed that the new Ballet Bridge across Tonle Sap from Sokimex Oil Depot on National Road 5 in Russey Keo District to Chroy Changvar Satellite City Development Zone, Chroy Changvar District was officially inaugurated on the afternoon of May 08, 2018. After the construction process for the past 6 months.
The new ballet bridge is 12 meters wide and 500 meters long, with a construction cost of $ 9 million and took six months to build. When operating, vehicles weighing more than 15 tons and with a height of more than 2.8 meters are not allowed to pass.
