This morning, September 11, 2019, the Svay Rieng Provincial Administration, led by Mr. Hem Piseth, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province, represented Mr. Men Vibol, Provincial Governor, attended a working meeting with Delegation from the Ministry of Public Works and the Asian Development Bank (ADB) Project Representative on Management and Training for Landfill (MRF) in Bavet City.
Mr. Hem Piseth said that the project to build a landfill is being coordinated between the Ministry of Public Works, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, provincial authorities and the Asian Development Bank to implement the next project, which includes wastewater treatment and Landfill.
The forthcoming project is a follow-up to the construction of a drainage and sewerage system and a landfill implemented under the Southern Corridor Economic Development Project of the Greater Mekong Subregion. Notice! Authorities stop traffic on the road from Bek Chamkar district to Stung Trang district town, Kampong Cham province due to flooding
(Kampong Cham): Due to the flooding of Road 71C, Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, this morning, September 11, 2019, decided to temporarily stop the road from Thnal Bek, Chamkar Leu District to Stung Trang District Town.
Mr. Un Chanda led a team of officials from relevant institutions to inspect immediately after receiving the news that the water flooded Road 71C, which is the road from Chamkar Leu district to Stung Trang district town.
(Ratanakkiri): An online cockfighting betting site in Chey Chumneas Village, La Ban Siek Commune, Banlung City, Ratanakkiri Province, was raided by the Police Force of the Provincial Police Commission in collaboration with the Banlung City Police Inspectorate led by Mr. Leang Ou, Prosecutor. Deputy of Ratanakkiri Provincial Court cracked down on the afternoon of September 10, 2019.
Colonel Meas Pov Bora, director of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Police Bureau of Minor Offenses, said that during the operation, police confiscated 27 motorcycles, three LED TVs and a lottery machine. Accessories and board number 2 and brought to the provincial police to carry out the procedure.
He said that the owner of the online cockfighting betting site was Boy Thi Ngoc Ha, a Vietnamese national. In the past, the authorities have educated, instructed and contracted many times, but the owner of the above location did not comply, leading to the crackdown today.
Currently, the specialized force is building the case of those involved and the above game and sent it to the Ratanakkiri Provincial Court for legal proceedings.
Two failed candidates drown a day before the results are released
(Kampong Cham): Two high school candidates drowned a day before the exam results came out as the results showed that they passed the exam.
The bodies of the two candidates were found by the authorities at 4 pm on September 10, 2019 at Boeung Dolphin Chong, Angkor Ban 5 village, Angkor Ban commune, Kang Meas district, Kampong Cham province.
Authorities confirmed that the young victim went missing on September 8, 2019 and was a candidate for the high school exam after the results were released on September 9, 2019.
At the same time, the authorities set up a committee to examine the body at the scene, as a result, found that both the head, neck, body and limbs were not scarred. Upon examination, the commission concluded that the drowning body was not involved in any criminal offense. The body was handed over to the family for traditional rites. OPPO unveils four features of the new A-Series 2020!
