MANILA: Philippine President Rodrigo Duterte has revealed that Chinese President Xi Jinping will make a "good deal" on energy if Manila does not recognize the International Court of Arbitration's ruling against Beijing over the China Sea dispute. South. This is according to a quote from CNA on Wednesday afternoon, September 11, 2019.
According to Duterte, Xi Jinping told him during a recent meeting that if he did not recognize the ruling of the International Court of Arbitration in 2016, China would agree to be a partner in an energy project in the China Sea. South and let the Philippine side hold more shares.
The Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs as well as the Chinese Embassy in Manila have not yet commented on the remarks. Since coming to power, Duterte seems to have sought to forge closer ties with Xi Jinping with the hope of attracting more investment, and has also sought to avoid a direct confrontation with China over the South China Sea. Also.
The new chairman of the International Monetary Fund (IMF) in Cambodia is committed to strengthening good cooperation with the government to maintain macroeconomic stability.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, expressed his gratitude and appreciation to the International Monetary Fund, which has always strengthened close cooperation and actively contributed to the development of Cambodia.
He also briefed Mr. Yasuhisa Ojima on the need and capacity building of professional officers for Cambodia to assess the impact of internal and external challenges and risks on the economic situation, trade volume, financial sector and affairs. Develop the society with the goal of setting out strategic, policy and package measures for the short, medium and long term in a proactive, timely and comprehensive manner.
He also pointed out the strategy to develop the capacity of Cambodian professional officers, focusing on three levels:
1. Strategic work for coordinating leadership, such as coordinating the budget system reform, revenue collection strategy, public procurement reform strategy, etc.
2. Equipped with additional technical skills (Skill developments) for the management of the public financial system, such as information technology systems for public financial management, public debt management systems and monitoring and evaluation mechanisms, etc.
3: Separate special training program to increase professional skills that can respond to specific needs or solve any specific problems that occur during the implementation of the program.
