(Central): The three-day operation to extract nearly 2,000 tons of sand barges attached to the third pillar of the Prek Tamak Bridge has not yet yielded good results, despite the efforts of the rescue team. In many ways.
On the morning of September 11, 2019, the rescue team consisting of relevant ministries and experts from the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port under the command of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, decided on a common principle: Add sand from the bottom of the barge attached to the pillar to pull it out.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized that the dredging, according to experts, may take 2-3 hours to complete the dredging from the bottom of the ferry. He said that because of the high water flow, it was difficult to pump sand from the barge, and had to use anchors and use a boat to pull the barge into the dredger.
Please note that on the afternoon of September 7, 2019, a sand barge opened and got stuck with the Prek Tamak Bridge (Pillar 3), causing it to get stuck on the third bridge of Prek Ta Mak Bridge. Immediately after receiving the information, the Governor of Kandal Province, Mr. Mao Phirun, went down to intervene to find a way to pull the ferry from the bridge.
According to General Commissioner Eav Chamroeun, for this incident, the provincial governor ordered to temporarily stop the other sand ferry crossing under the bridge, waiting for the ferry to pull out to avoid further accidents.
