Cambodia will host the CLMTV Ministerial Meeting and Conference from September 16-17 in Siem Reap, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will open the conference
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has issued a press release on hosting the 5th Senior Officials Meeting and the 3rd Ministerial Conference on Labor Cooperation. Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar, Thailand and Vietnam (CLMTV) after the theme "Towards the Protection of Migrant Workers in CLMTV" on 16-17 September in Siem Reap-Angkor.
A press release from the Ministry of Labor, obtained by Fresh News on the morning of September 11, confirmed that the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will preside over the opening ceremony of the third Labor Ministerial Conference on September 17, 2019.
The main purpose of the conference was to discuss a common framework related to social security mobilization for migrant workers in CLMTV, such as:
* Encourage continued sharing of experiences and best practices among CLMTV countries related to the protection and promotion of the rights of migrant workers, especially the mobility of the social security system.
* Discuss and agree on a joint mechanism to determine the future implementation of the mobility of the social security system
* Working towards the establishment of a joint framework for CLMTV on the mobility of the social security system for migrant workers.
