(Kandal): On September 10, 2019, a delegation of Kandal Province led by Mr. Mao Phirun, Governor of Kandal Province and Major General Eav Chamroeun, Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner and many officials. Another to An Yan province, Vietnam to hold a two-day meeting to review the work of the first six months of 2019, September 10-11, 2019.
Dr. Mao Phirun, Governor of Kandal Province, told Fresh News reporters in Kandal province tonight that the meeting with Vietnam focused on the upcoming issues along the border. These include: security, border development, economic cooperation, cooperation in various fields related to the interests of the two provinces (Kandal-An Yan), prevention of drug trafficking, prevention of smuggling of illegal goods.
He said that as a result of the first day, the two sides agreed on many issues in the sense of joint cooperation on better border work and many other issues.
The provincial governor added that the meeting is held every six months, the first six months of the meeting in Vietnam and the last six months of the meeting in Cambodia. Minister Mam Bun Heng Urges Health Officials to Improve Quality and Provide Better Services to Citizens
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bunheng, urged health officials to improve the quality and improve the provision of better services to the people in response to the current development of the medical field.
This statement was made on the occasion of the Minister handing over the ISO 15189 certificate to the National Referral Laboratory of the National Institute of Public Health on September 9, 2019, Bayon Hall of the National Institute of Public Health.
The Minister of Health continued, "In order to improve the quality, we must work together to do it, and that will have good results." In addition, to keep up with the progress of the medical field, we need to seek to strengthen the skills associated with entering the race to know our talents as well.
In addition, Minister Mam Bunheng urged all hospitals to make efforts to improve their public laboratories, with some shortcomings to be addressed through the training of quality control systems of those laboratories. .
The minister said the ministry wants all medical laboratories to improve their service quality by using existing quality improvement services in the country, especially services provided by the National Institute of Public Health, such as training on quality management system. Experiments as well as participation in external quality assessment and measurement of necessary equipment used in the laboratory, such as pipette and thermometer.
The Minister instructed the laboratory staff to continue to maintain the quality of their services to provide accurate, reliable and timely results to patients, as the acquisition of international quality recognition is just the beginning, but the implementation By consistently and sustainably maintaining quality is a work that needs to be done continuously to contribute to improving the quality of health services in Cambodia.
At the same time, the Minister strongly believes that the National Institute of Public Health will use the experience gained through the assessment of quality standards of Canada as a model to strengthen and expand training programs to public and private laboratories across the country.
At the same time, Prof. Chhea Chhavann, Director of the National Institute of Public Health, is committed to using the success and experience of this international quality assessment to improve the Institute's laboratory quality management program to make the program more effective in helping Improve the quality of laboratory services in Cambodia.
He added that at the same time, the Institute will further expand its services, especially training in quality control of the laboratory, external quality assessment and measurement of the necessary equipment used in the laboratory to assist the department. Other experiments.
On that occasion, Mr. Michael A. Newbill, Representative of the US Embassy in Cambodia, stated that this achievement is part of the goal of the Ministry of Health in improving the quality of private and public laboratory services throughout the country to ensure accurate and Timely patient care and response to outbreaks.
