New KOICA President in Cambodia Pledges to Increase Cooperation to Promote Cambodia's Development
Mr. Noh Chun made the remarks during a courtesy call on Mr. Chheang Yanara, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary-General of the Cambodian Committee for Rehabilitation and Development of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (NCDC). A) On September 10, 2019.
During the courtesy call, the two sides discussed and exchanged views on the agenda, including: 1) International Development Cooperation Day 2019 in the Republic of Korea; New projects for 2021, 3) Review the progress of cooperation and 4) - Identify priority areas for future cooperation.
In this meeting, Mr. No Hyun Joon invited Mr. Chiang Yanara to participate in the International Development Cooperation Day 2019, which is scheduled to be held in late November 2019 in the Republic of Korea. He stressed that the day will focus on development cooperation for peace, prosperity and the 30th anniversary of the Korea-ASEAN Development Cooperation and beyond.
Mr. Chheang Yanara examined the possibility of participation and believed that the Day of International Development Cooperation 2019 would provide an opportunity to strengthen and expand bilateral cooperation with Cambodia and ASEAN within the framework of Official Development Financing (ODA).
Minister Chiang Yanara also thanked the Government of the Republic of Korea through the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) for its contribution to the development of Cambodia in all fields.
Noon Chun outlined the "New South Policy to ASEAN" aimed at strengthening cooperation with ASEAN members, including Cambodia, saying KOICA would increase the opening of official development financing (ODA) for ASEAN. Up to 20 percent by 2023 in response to South Korea's new policy.
It should be noted that the cooperation between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea is better and more comprehensive. In fact, the development cooperation expanded by the Government of the Republic of Korea to contribute to the socio-economic development of Cambodia has increased significantly.
