Since the morning of September 10, 2019, Preah Vihear Provincial Authority, together with the Director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, led Tbeng Meanchey District Authority, Tbeng Meanchey District Police Force and several military police forces to rescue many pigs. Head in a flooded farm.
According to Lieutenant Colonel Rith Sona, Tbeng Meanchey District Police Inspector, as of this afternoon, the rescue of pigs has continued. He said that out of 3,600 pigs, about 600 were lost, and about 1,000 more were being evacuated to safety this evening and the rescue operation had to be completed.
Separately, Mr. Non Vanny, the owner of the pig farm through Fresh News, he would like to express his deep gratitude to the Preah Vihear Provincial Authority, Provincial Agriculture Department, Tbeng Meanchey District Authority and the police and military police, as well as the people who participated in the rescue. His pigs survived the floods. The youngest of the Vital family with a capacity of 250mL is now on the market
The event was held on September 10, 2019 at Aeon Mall 2 Sen Sok City, with more than 300 participants, most of whom are Debo distributors of Vital water products, small and large in the market.
She said that in general, attending large events means drinking less water and throwing away leftover water bottles. This is the reason why we decided to produce new capacity to meet the needs of this market.
Ms. Chheng Sokuntheavy, Managing Director and Board Member of Vital Company, expressed her deep gratitude to Vital customers, especially the owners of beverage depots, who have always strived to support the successful distribution of Vital to the market throughout Cambodia, accelerating the growth. Vital traffic on the market is leading the way.
She sincerely hopes that for this new product, there will be more help from all business partners to push Vital products through mainstream and inform customers about the quality, advantages and benefits of Vital 250mL.
According to Ms. Chheng Sokuntheavy, Vital will not remain silent because Vital has the vision to become a leading national company in the field of drinking water production in both domestic and foreign markets.
She added that Vital is committed to continuing its efforts to create new and better programs to best serve the Cambodian people and also in return for the trust that Cambodians have in Vital. Nation.
According to Ms. Chheng Sokuntheavy, in the nine years of Vital's presence in the Cambodian market, Vital has achieved great success in terms of both sales volume and quality recognition.
That's why today the company released the new 250mL Vital Drinking Water, which has a special design that makes this water look unique, beautiful, show the highest honor and have the right amount, suitable for use in Many events such as weddings, religious ceremonies and reception of guests in shops and at home.
(Kandal): The statue of "Preah Siya Metrey" was built by a person who claimed to be a military officer on Phnom Saang in Saang Phnom commune, Saang district, Kandal province, which was visited by monks and Buddhists at There is a priest and claims that there is no permit from the authorities and officials.
