Mr. Chan Mony, an old journalist with nose cancer, needs emergency care, but his family is in need, please call for donations
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chan Mony, a veteran journalist who currently works for Kampuchea Thmey newspaper in Kandal province, fell seriously ill due to nasal cancer after being injured by shrapnel in 1997. While covering the news in front of the National Assembly.
Mr. Chan Mony started his career as a journalist in 1988 by working for People's Newspaper and then moving to National Radio and then working as a reporter for Cambodian newspaper today before He moved to work at Kampuchea Thmey newspaper until today.
MP Many Many Shares Achieving Cambodia's Development Goals at Inter-Parliamentary Union Conference in Paraguay
(Paraguay): At the invitation of the Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPU) and the Paraguayan Parliament, Hun Many, Member of the National Assembly and Chairman of the National Assembly's Committee on Education, Youth, Sports, Cult, Religious Affairs, Culture and Tourism, led a young member of the National Assembly to attend the Global Conference. Sixth Young Member of Parliament of the Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPU) in Paraguay from 9 to 10 September 2019.
At the Global Conference, the Head of Delegation and members shared Cambodia's efforts and achievements in achieving the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).
Attending the Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPU) conference, a meeting for young members of the IPU Parliament, is a valuable mission for the Cambodian parliamentary diplomacy. During the conference, a delegation of young Cambodian parliamentarians will attend a series of meetings to share experiences and exchange views with parliamentarians of other countries to build peace and sustainable global development through parliamentary mechanisms.
