In addition to the joy of success in the exams of many students, there are also students who do not get good results as expected. This factor discourages some students and makes them lose hope for future goals.
As experienced in failing the high school diploma exam last year, but did not give up hope and continued to study until succeeding in next year's exam, three young men and women shared their experiences. Therefore:
Ms. Chhean Chheang Huy: “Last year, I failed the science exam, but this year I passed the social science exam, I am very happy. At first, I was also ashamed of failing the exam, but because I wanted to continue my studies, I decided to study in the 12th grade again. And now I have done it.
Ms. Ny Ratana: “When we failed the exam, some people really said words that discouraged us, and also some people encouraged us. However, I urge all parents to say something that discourages children, because during the results like this, they can think short.
As for Mr. Va Bonna, a student who failed the high school diploma exam last year, decided to study for an associate's degree first, then he registered for the Swarin exam by studying himself online. He finally got good results in this year's competition.
