(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bunheng, stated that we will continue our joint efforts to train medical students at our National University with high capacity and quality to update modern technology to meet international standards.
Especially when going out to practice as a doctor, there are both clear and high quality professional skills to provide safety to the people. Therefore, at the University of Health Sciences, we are now continuing the reform of teaching by equipping students with advanced technical equipment from abroad for students to practice professionally before applying to patients.
Minister Mam Bunheng said this on the occasion of inspecting modern medical equipment from abroad at the simulation laboratory of the University of Health Sciences on September 9, 2019.
Minister Mam Bunheng continued, "Equipping modern equipment at the University of Science and Technology is indispensable to train students to acquire knowledge, skills and talents when coming out to treat people with quality. "
In particular, in line with the policy of the Royal Government is to make our doctors provide quality and effective medical care to citizens. Therefore, to achieve this quality and effectiveness, only if our training school has Technical materials and qualified teachers to increase the knowledge of our students and our specialists.
"Therefore, the equipments and practices in this university are necessary to make our doctors competent and able to provide services to our people with high quality and efficiency," he said. If the school is not up to date, we produce quality doctors who are not up to date with modern technology.
In addition, the school must improve the quality of training and use modern technology until doctors go out to be able to use this modern technology skillfully. "Therefore, we will work together to train our doctors to meet the standards in the modern area as the telecommunication system develops like other countries."
At the same time, the Rector of the University of Health Sciences, Prof. Saphon Vattanak stated that the goal of the development and reform of the University is after teaching theory and we will continue to teach more students practice with tools. Modern, ingenious, before applying to patients.
"So for the safety of the patient and the skills of the students, we turn to practice in the simulation room on Malacca, although not 100% human, but it will be able to provide his skillful performance," he said. "There are improvements before the actual implementation."
In addition, the vision of the University of Health Sciences is to increase quality human resources, because quality is the key to provide safety to people.
