At the same time, Mr. Hun Many also encouraged the candidates who have not been successful this time to continue to work harder for the next exam and to succeed in the future.
The President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia posted a message like this: "Congratulations to all of you who have achieved good results in the high school diploma exam in 2019. The results you are getting now are the result of your hard work, self-discipline, and the support of your parents and guardians.
Today's success is the beginning of a new step for his career and career. From today, especially in the context of rapidly evolving civil society, young people should continue to study, seek higher education and grasp a basic skill for life goals and to become a potential driver and become An outstanding citizen of Cambodia.
In particular, I would like to encourage you who have not been successful today, please do your best to practice more and prioritize more study for the next exam and to be successful in the future. "
It should be reminded that the Baccalaureate exam, which took place on 19-20 August 2019, has 202 examination centers in all capitals and provinces, 4,724 examination rooms and 117,043 registered candidates. 1835 candidates were absent.
Minister Vong Soth sends condolences to the family of the late General Sim Tai, who died at the age of 63
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and all leaders and civil servants of this Ministry sent condolences to the family of the late Major General Sim Tai, Director of the Intelligence Office of the Ministry of National Defense who died of a disease. At 2:50 pm on September 08, 2019 at the age of 63.
In this condolence message, Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, expressed his sorrow that the death of Major General Sim Tai, Director of the Intelligence Office of the Ministry of National Defense, was the loss of a son who served the national interest The king also sacrificed everything for the cause of sincere service to the people and society.
Minister Vong Soth also expressed his deepest condolences, extended his deepest condolences to Major General Sim Tai and his family, and prayed for the sacred objects in the world and the merits of the Buddha, Dharma, and monks. Nurture and take care of the soul of Major General Sim Tai to eternal death forever.
The life insurance market in Cambodia is growing rapidly today as more companies come to invest.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Youk Chamroeun Rithy, General Director of Forte Life Insurance Company, said that the current life insurance market in Cambodia is growing rapidly due to the large number of insurance companies coming in and helping the market to grow.
He added that in fact, Forte Life Insurance Company has a 6-month life insurance policy and a general life insurance policy that is more than 20 years old.
Mr. Youk Chamroeunrith stated, "The insurance market is growing rapidly due to the influx of life insurance companies, which makes the market grow and for life insurance companies this year will be able to earn revenue in the entire Cambodian market. "$ 250 million."
Mr. Youk Chamroeunrith said that it is the tradition of the Cambodian people in the past, when they were sick, they always sold their houses, cattle and other property to treat the disease, so that they could survive. Used to treat and spend when sick, he will start again with another empty foot.
He added that seeing this aspect as an insurance worker does not want this to happen again in Cambodia, Forte has partnered with foreign insurance companies to bring a new insurance policy that Can effectively protect the health of Cambodians and can go to treatment with world-renowned hospitals that are its partners.
She said that in addition to developing new insurance products, Further also offers other related services ranging from medical expenses to doctor appointments, travel and accommodation. In addition, the company also provides interpreters and translation services for medical reports. The water level of the Mekong River in Tbong Khmum province has risen above the emergency level, today the provincial governor intervened and distributed gifts to the people
