(Tbong Khmum): The flood of the Mekong River in Tbong Khmum province has exceeded the declared emergency level and is now at a height of 15.64 meters, while the emergency level is only 15.20 meters, which inundated some villages. River.
Responding to this issue immediately, Mr. Hak Sok Makara, Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, on September 9, 2019, led the working group and relevant authorities to visit and distribute to the affected people in Chiror 1 commune and commune. Peam Chiling, Tbong Khmum district, living along the Mekong River.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Hak Sok Makara expressed his condolences to all the victims of the floods that flooded their homes and crops, as well as flooded their travel routes.
The deputy governor also called on people living along the river to take care of family members, especially young children and the elderly, always drink boiled water and eat clean, drink clean, live clean and be careful of poisonous animals. Harm to you. And if there is any problem, please report to the authorities and doctors who are on duty 24 hours to help you immediately.
Ministry of Tourism: 70 Cambodian Tourism Professionals Receive Japanese Language Capacity Building
(Phnom Penh): Under the cooperation between the Ministry of Tourism and the ASEAN-Japan Center and the Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center, about 70 Cambodian tourism professionals have been receiving training to strengthen their Japanese language skills to improve their Japanese language skills. Proficiency.
The opening ceremony of the training course was held at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh on the afternoon of September 9, 2019, chaired by Mr. Pak Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and attended by Ms. Mizuho Kanda, Head of Tourism and Representative of the ASEAN-Japan Center. Of Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center, professional officers, tourism experts, students, a total of 70 participants.
In the opening ceremony, the Secretary of State highlighted the growth of Cambodia's tourism sector under the shadow of peace and development in all areas arising from the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
This training workshop was organized on time and in accordance with the request of tourism experts to participate in building human resources in the tourism sector, especially to improve the Japanese language skills to be more proficient in participating in tourism services. To be better and more satisfied by tourists, especially Japanese tourists who have been steadily increasing in visiting Cambodia.
It should be noted that for the first seven months of 2019, Cambodia received more than 3.8 million international tourists, an increase of 11.1% compared to the same period in 2018, in which Cambodia received Japanese tourists. 113,159 people, an increase of about 2.6%.
