Speaking at the ceremony, Dr. Hean Sahip emphasized that the reform of public financial management is a key and key reform program as stated in the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the 6th legislature of National Assembly for employment growth, equity and efficiency.
The Public Financial Management Reform Program was first officially launched in 2004 by the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and has achieved many important achievements. In particular, achieving budget credibility in the first phase and financial accountability in the second phase.
The training and training at this time is really organized in a timely manner and really respond to the need for the implementation of public procurement to be more effective in accordance with the laws and regulations in force, especially in the spirit of the corrective strategy. Public procurement system model 2019-2025 and strategic plan on capacity building and development within the framework of the third phase of public financial management reform program.
