Minister of Agriculture instructs investment partners to plant trees to speed up planting activities
The purpose of this meeting is to report to the Minister on the progress of investment projects in planting trees for the wood processing industry and for the construction of buildings, factories, furniture and exports.
Mr. Chang thanked the Forestry Administration and especially the Minister for his cooperation, encouragement and support for the tree planting development process from the beginning to the present, and he hoped that the Forestry Administration as well as the Ministry would continue to provide assistance. Collaborate for the company to achieve the investment plan as expected.
Taking this opportunity, his team reported on the achievements that the company has achieved so far, such as planting seedlings, planting seedlings such as oil, air, acacia, teak, etc. Since 2017, the company has planted more than 2,000 hectares of trees and is planning to expand to another 5,000 hectares by 2020.
He also stated that because the company has invested more than 2 million US dollars to establish a tree research and breeding institute in Kampong Thom province to promote tree species, training techniques to improve the quality of trees and the sustainability of the supply of seedlings and as Especially due to the favorable environment of Cambodia, the trees that are being planted will be only 6 years old and can harvest 150 cubic meters per hectare.
The Minister praised the achievements of the company, including planting, nursery and especially the establishment of the Plantation Research Institute, which will contribute significantly to the development of Cambodia's forestry through research, promotion, planting and planting. Reforestation in accordance with the policy of the Ministry and especially of the Royal Government.
The Minister instructed the company to make more efforts in cooperation with the Forestry Administration, the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to accelerate activities on planting work as planned.
The Minister said that the Ministry will look forward to cooperating with the company in order to encourage and support the company's investment in order to improve the supply capacity of industrial plant products in the domestic and foreign markets, compete to promote the use of plant products. The use of natural wood, and especially to create and maintain forest cover, create jobs, increase income and sustain the national economy.
