(Kampot): The section of National Road No. 3 from Veal Rinh to Kampot, about 20 kilometers from the junction of Veal Rinh, has been severely damaged after construction. This damage caused people to criticize and express their great wonder that the reason why the road was not built yet was so damaged?
To solve this problem, the company decided to build using a new technology by raising the road about 8 water and the foundation is poured with stone under it to prevent further damage as it is now. This was confirmed by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also confirmed that the company has guaranteed with him, and the use of this new technology guarantees that the road will last for about 5 years, and if you want to last longer, only dig the soil to a depth of 18 meters. But the ministry could not choose how to dig the land, as the road needed to be speeded up to be used for the Sea Festival in Kampot and the world-class cycling event to be held in late 2019.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also said that in order to improve the road construction technology, the Ministry will request an additional loan of more than 4 million US dollars from the World Bank.
It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia, through a loan from the World Bank, has decided to rehabilitate and rehabilitate 54.30 km of National Road No. 3 between km 147 + 100 to km 201 + 400 from the Veal Renh roundabout to the city. Kampot province, with a budget of about 12 million US dollars. This section of road is repaired and improved by AC paving.
(Preah Sihanouk): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, this morning, September 9, 2019, led a technical officer under the Ministry to inspect natural canals to release rainwater, sewage and infrastructure in Preah City. Sihanouk, with the participation of the Ministry of Technology and officials of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Sihanoukville.
After days of heavy rain, Sihanoukville has been threatened by flash floods, causing severe flooding and severe damage to road infrastructure.
Please be informed that the flood situation in Sihanoukville is caused by excessive rainfall and the drainage system is congested and currently there are 5 natural streams for releasing rainwater in Sihanoukville, including: Ochheuteal, O Sam Ath, O Andong, UNTAC, O Spean Fires and streams are shrinking due to landslides, debris and soil, and shallow natural canals due to congestion and encroachment by building buildings into streams.
Speaking during the inspection, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol confirmed that the Ministry is ready to cooperate with relevant ministries and institutions to release machinery to solve the congestion system to easily release water from the city to avoid road impacts. Roads are congested and difficult for people to travel.
The senior minister also stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has provided about 100 million US dollars in financing projects and about 400 million US dollars from the private sector for the rehabilitation and maintenance of 22 roads in Sihanoukville that were damaged by floods. Rain.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. HUN Manet said that currently the education sector in Cambodia has made significant progress in both quantity and quality, and the progress of the education sector has really contributed significantly to the current social and economic growth of Cambodia. .
This statement was made on the occasion that Mr. HUN Manet, Representative of Samdech Techo HUN SEN and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, presided over the graduation ceremony for the winners of the Doctor, Doctor, Pharmacist, Associate Degree, Nursing, Bachelor and Masters degrees. A total of 437 students were at the International University (IU) last weekend.
Mr. Hun Manet added that the progress in all areas of the country, the sustainability of Cambodia's economic growth and competitiveness, both now and in the future, depends on the development of human resources as a priority that needs to be taken into account. Continue to reform to ensure quality human resources and professional capacity to serve the society and the labor market.
Mr. Hun Manet also pointed out that Cambodia has been recognized as a country with rapid development in recent years in terms of economy, trade and services. Cambodia is on the right track, making Cambodia grow steadily in all areas from year to year.
On that occasion, Mr. HUN Manet also said that in addition to human resource development through education, another part of human resource development is to make people healthy, these two factors must complement each other. Come on.
He added that health is an indispensable asset in the process of sustainable socio-economic development in Cambodia, especially in maintaining the stability of national economic growth, poverty reduction and Cambodia's competitiveness.
Mr. HUN Manet said that therefore, high consideration and priority to the health sector is necessary to continue to improve both now and in the long term.
He said that when people are healthy and strong, people will be able to fully participate in all social activities, especially economic activities to improve the lives of families and be able to send their children to school to gain knowledge, become human resources with skills. Real and an active force in national development.
Mr. HUN Manet stated that starting from this concept, the Royal Government has always strived to increase resources and cooperation, mobilize national assistance and international development partners to promote the development of basic infrastructure of the health system, including infrastructure construction, training. Human resources, equipments, etc. that serve the provision of health services throughout the country.
As a result, Cambodia has achieved many important achievements and progresses, in which the public health situation has been gradually improved along with the focus on improving the quality of health services at all levels. This is the additional emphasis of Mr. Hun Manet.
He added that, in fact, Cambodia has also achieved its Millennium Development Goals remarkably, of which four goals were achieved before the deadline: reducing child mortality, improving maternal health, combating HIV, AIDS, malaria, infectious diseases, and increasing global partnerships for development. Every purchase of Borey Lonni Villa in September 2019 will receive many special offers.
Statement by Minister Mam Bun Heng on the occasion of health education and distribution of mosquito nets, medicine, family hygiene packages, health education books to people in Tbong Khmum and Stung Treng provinces on September 08, 2019.
"In recent days, we have assigned officers to bring more medical equipment, including mosquito nets, to some provinces along the Mekong River, such as Stung Treng, Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum, Kratie," he said. .
In addition, in order to respond urgently to the floods that have been occurring in the provinces, the Minister of Health visited and treated the people and distributed mosquito nets, medicine, family hygiene kits and some necessary materials to the people. Victims in two provinces.
Stung Treng province in the safe area of O'Svay Secondary School, O'Svay village, O'Svay commune, Borey O'Svay Senchey district has 370 families and Srei Krasaing safe hill, Sre Krasaing village, Sre Kraing commune, Siem Bok district has 470 families and Tbong Khmum province is safe. There are 1,070 affected families from Prek Touch village, Tonle Biet Leu, Tonle Biet Krom, Chi Roth I in Tbong Khmum district.
On that occasion, Minister Mam Bunheng instructed the people to take care of their health and be careful about safety when evacuating to live in a safe place and called on the people to take care of their children and prevent them from drowning. Loss of life immediately and advised to sleep under a mosquito net day and night to prevent dengue fever and malaria.
In order to minimize the impact on the health, lives of victims and health facilities from natural disasters, especially floods, the Minister of Health reminded and called on all people to follow the following guidelines:
1: Before the flood
* Monitor the flood situation, prepare for safe places and food. Build a fence around a pond or a place where there is water, keep the environment clean, and build toilets that need to be upgraded from low to high to prevent flooding.
2: During the flood
Do not enter an old house or a dilapidated building as it may collapse and cause danger. Do not touch electrical appliances with wet hands or while in the water while traveling by boat or ferry at night, keep the lights on.
* For pregnant women, follow up and check the pregnancy according to the schedule of the health center or hospital. If the woman is about to give birth, find a place to stay near the health center or hospital nearest to you.
Get your child vaccinated as prescribed by your doctor and feed them properly.
Be careful of girls and girls when in a safe place, lest there be sexual violence.
* Help the elderly in your family or the elderly in the neighborhood and provide support to family members or children with disabilities such as crutches, wheelchairs or some of the medications they are taking on a regular basis that are essential to their needs.
Be careful to avoid drowning, prevent small children from drowning, explain to children the dangers of drowning, go to higher ground and have a caregiver use a jacket or bucket whenever children leave home. When traveling by boat or ferry, do not overcrowd if someone drowns, call for help immediately.
Be careful of the dangers of snake bites or other venomous animals by checking properly before going to safety or before working near piles, dragging and moving trees. When traveling at night or at work, wear long pants and long boots, avoid crowded places, and never touch snakes or other animals.
* In case a family member or someone is in danger due to a snake bite or a second venomous animal, or must be sent immediately to the nearest health center or hospital for examination and treatment.
Wash vegetables and fruits with clean water, properly cooked food, and cover food well to prevent flies and dust from entering, as well as clean kitchen utensils and utensils such as dishes, pots, spoons, knives. Wash your hands often with soap before and after eating and after using the toilet.
To avoid respiratory infections, it is necessary to wear a mask or coat.
Cover your mouth when coughing or sneezing with a towel or scarf, keep it at least 1 meter away from patients who cough or sneeze, and do not wear dusty masks if necessary.
When the weather changes suddenly, take care of your health, such as dressing properly and avoiding going out for long periods of time.
* Keep your body clean by taking a shower, shampooing and washing your clothes to avoid skin rashes, scabies and so on.
3: After the flood
* Continue to eat clean food, clean water and clean body to avoid various diseases.
* Sleep under a mosquito net at all times to prevent dengue fever and malaria
* Check the house to see if it collapses, causing danger. Be careful not to get the devil, snake or other poisonous animal.
Clean the environment around the house and house because when the water recedes, it leaves a lot of dirt and germs living in the water. Avoid putting water around the house and house, leading to water worms, tiger mosquitoes and nail mosquitoes that cause dengue fever Malaria
* Must restore and clean the well before use.
* As well as repairing and rebuilding toilets, always defecate in the toilet at all times.
Before, during and after the flood: If you have a health problem, seek medical advice and treatment at the nearest health center or health center or hospital nearest you.
The Minister of Tourism encourages the newly inaugurated Kampong Thom Royal Hotel to establish agro-tourism activities for guests connected to the Sambor Prei Kuk temple area
(Kampong Thom): On the occasion of the inauguration of Kampong Thom Royal Hotel on September 9, 2019, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, encouraged the owners and managers of this hotel to consider creating entertainment activities for tourists by organizing Visits to agro-tourism sites around the province connected with the Sambor Prei Kuk temple site, a potential cultural heritage destination.
Kampong Thom Royal Hotel will provide another important accommodation service in Kampong Thom, a four-star hotel, plus Kampong Thom also has a major World Heritage site, the Sambor Prei Kuk temple, Minister Thong Khon urged the hotel to seize the opportunity This is used to its full potential, although not immediately achieved.
Mr. Thong Khon said that in the area of Sambor Prei Kuk temple, in addition to cultural tourism destinations, there are also agro-tourism potentials, such as cashew plantations, rice fields, cashew nut handicrafts, silk handicrafts, handicrafts and bamboo souvenirs, which are all products. Tourism for tourists visiting Kampong Thom.
He said that some tourists used to eat rice, vegetables, fruits and grains, but have not yet seen the cultivation, harvesting, processing of all those things, and they really want to see the production process of those things. So people can show them off with a fee through tourism services.
In addition, there are vegetable gardens, flower gardens and many other plantations where the hotel can communicate with the plantation owners to arrange tours for tourists, especially to extend the stay of tourists for several days.
He also asked Kampong Thom Royal Hotel to support local products, especially community products in Kampong Thom province, both for use as decoration equipment, supply of living room equipment and supply of restaurant needs. He also requested the provincial administration and the Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Tourism to promote the collection and distribution of all local products.
The Minister added that in addition to the World Heritage Site (Sambor Prei Kuk Temple), Kampong Thom is also an important center of travel from Phnom Penh to Siem Reap-Angkor and from Phnom Penh to Preah Vihear and Preah Vihear. All of them are important heritage sites of Cambodia and in the future Kampong Thom will be connected to Kampong Chhnang as well as the western part of Tonle Sap Lake and Tonle Sap through the construction of bridges across the Tonle Sap.
At the same time, Mr. Thong Khon requested the Kampong Thom Provincial Administration to expedite the development of other potential tourist destinations as soon as possible, especially the construction of infrastructure to those destinations and the strengthening of management mechanisms, organization, sanitation and environment.
Oknha Kuy Leang Ky, owner of Kampong Thom Royal Hotel, said that his hotel has 87 rooms, including food service, health club, swimming pool, gym, steam-sauna, massage, spa, sky bar, which cost about 4 million 8 million. Hundreds of thousands of dollars. The hotel currently employs 79 people (34 females) in all departments.
