(Svay Rieng): Many police forces, both military and local authorities, led by representatives of the Svay Rieng Provincial Prosecutor's Office, this morning, September 9, 2019, executed the judgment of the Supreme Court in Romeas Hek District, Svay Rieng Province. Families living on state land.
According to the report from Svay Rieng province, a family named Thong Sam Oeun lives in Trav village, Kampong Trach commune, Romeas Hek district, Svay Rieng province.
In the second Supreme Court judgment, it was stated that the Court of Appeal upheld the civil judgment of the Svay Rieng Provincial Court by rejecting the plaintiff's claim to the disputed land. Not the former residential land, and many people who came to live in this area after 1979 have left in a row, leaving only the plaintiff.
The plaintiffs are well aware of the background of the disputed land, which was formerly an airport land, which is state land, not private land. In addition, the disputed land has already been required by the Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of Economy and Finance to register inventory, and Romeas Hek District Hall has also issued a title deed stating that the football field of Romeas Hek District is a football field. Private property of the state already.
It should be informed that the composition of the officials who participated in the discussion to find a solution this morning included: Professional officials from the Ministry of Public Works and Transport led by Mr. Lim Sidenin, Secretary of State of the Ministry, and Kandal Provincial Hall officials led by Mr. Kong Sophoan, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province. The Prek Tamak Bridge construction team is also from Shanghai.
This morning, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) wanted the sand dredging to be completely removed from the dredgers, but Kandal Provincial Hall gave various suggestions on the difficulties. If the sand is pumped out like this, Kong Sophoan wants the big ferries to pull out the attached barges. However, these two opinions do not seem to agree, so Senior Minister Sun Chanthol will come to resolve this afternoon.
It should be noted that yesterday afternoon, a sand barge opened and got stuck with the Prek Tamak Bridge (3rd pillar), causing it to get stuck on the bridge. Immediately after receiving the information, the Governor of Kandal Province, Mr. Mao Phirun, went down to intervene to find a way to pull the ferry from the bridge.
According to General Commissioner Eav Chamroeun, for this incident, the provincial governor ordered to temporarily suspend the other sand ferry crossing under the bridge, waiting for the ferry to pull out to avoid further accidents.
Prek Tamak Bridge has a total length of 1060 meters and a width of 13.5 meters with a maximum speed of 60 kilometers per hour. The construction of the bridge cost about $ 43.5 million under Chinese loan assistance and was commissioned in 2010.
