Camcontrol: More than 100,000 people die each year from asbestos-related diseases
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Phan Oun, Deputy Director General of CamControl, said that asbestos has the worst effect when a person is exposed to its concentration or they are exposed regularly for a long time. The World Health Organization estimates that more than 107,000 people die each year from asbestos-related illnesses caused by work-related injuries.
One example of workplace health concerns is exposure to asbestos, a major health hazard worldwide. It is a human carcinogen that can cause serious diseases such as cancer and lung cancer. It can also cause asbestos, a chronic obstructive pulmonary disease for which there is no cure. Symptoms of the disease can take years to develop after exposure.
