Death news! Youk Seang, a former professor of Pali-Sanskrit at the Royal University of Phnom Penh, has passed away.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Youk Seang, a former Professor of Khmer Literature majoring in Pali and Sanskrit at the Royal University of Phnom Penh, passed away at the age of 74 on September 7, 2019 at his home in front of the Southeast Asian Television Station, Sangkat O Bek Kam, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh, and the body was cremated according to tradition this morning, September 9, 2019 at Ang Ta Minh pagoda.
The death of Professor Youk Sieng was mourned by a group of alumni of the Royal University of Phnom Penh (University of Phnom Penh) and considered a significant loss of national literary human resources. He is a well-respected professor of alumni. He is an exemplary professor for Khmer literature students who have been trained at the University of Phnom Penh since the early 1990s.
On the night of August 24, 2019, a group of alumni of Phnom Penh University of the 12th generation of the Faculty of Khmer Literature invited Mr. Youk Sieng to participate in an alumni meeting at a restaurant in Sangkat Boeung Kak, Khan Toul Kork with some former professors. More.
On the night of August 24, he was in good health, happily chatting with his former students, as if he did not seem to be suffering from any illness. He spent hours chatting with professors as well as alumni before returning home at around 9pm.
Kan Kunprasong, a 12th-generation alumnus of the Faculty of Khmer Literature, who met with Youk Seang on the night of August 24 when he received the news of his death, said that it was unexpected because when When he met us, he was in good health. However, we only express our deepest condolences to the professor who dedicated his life to the cause of education in the field of national literature.
In the social network Facebook, there is a series of sharing of news and dedication to the professor. Mr. Ham Vuthy, a former student of Khmer Literature, 30th generation scholarship, considered Mr. Youk Sieng a hero who sacrificed his life in the cause of national literature.
Youk Seang, a former model professor at the Royal University of Phnom Penh, rides a bicycle to teach students without accepting gifts such as motorcycles. Many students tried to gather resources to buy a motorbike for the teacher to ride, but he did not accept the gift of a motorbike.
