Minister of Tourism and Governor of Kampong Thom Province Agree to Help Develop Cashew Nut and Handicraft Weaving in Sambo Prey Kuk
(Kampong Thom): After grasping some of the problems of the Sambor Prei Kuk tourism community, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, and Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, joined hands and vowed to promote the development of cashew handicrafts and ivory weaving. Growing to help improve the lives of the community as well.
Such a commitment in front of the community was made on the occasion of presiding over a meeting with the tourism community of Sambo Prei Kuk on the afternoon of September 8, 2019.
On that occasion, Mr. Seng An, Director of Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Tourism, said that the cashew peeling community is still active today, helping to train other communities such as Preah Vihear, Ratanakkiri and Kampong Thom.
In addition, there has been a series of investments in cashew peeling associations, most recently with cashew peeling contracts with German companies and a series of contracts with Thai companies to peel cashew nuts for a five-year plan.
The director of the department said that although it is possible to peel cashew nuts, the association still lacks the capital to buy stocks in the warehouse to process the cashew nuts. At the same time, community representatives also raised some issues related to the above handicraft process.
After listening to the report and the statement of the community, Minister Thong Khon immediately issued a solution by ordering a professional officer, including Mr. Chuk Chumnor, Director of the Department of Tourism Product Development, to facilitate the community to achieve. And the work in front of this problem is the lack of investment capital to expand more handicraft activities.
Minister Thong Khon also agreed with Mr. Sok Lou in front of the community, determined to promote the development of this cashew nut handicraft.
As for other handicrafts, Mr. Seng An said that there are still regular activities, but now the raw materials for production are less and less, making it difficult to produce. This issue also receives attention from the Minister and the Governor.
Mr. Thong Khon encouraged the community to replant more bamboo trees to be used as raw materials for the production of various weaving products.
In addition, Minister Thong Khon and Mr. Sok Lou also urged relevant officials to pay attention to palm sugar handicrafts, soy sauce, silk scarves, lodges, tour guides, food service and so on.
Mr. Thong Khon encouraged the people in the area of Sambor Prei Kuk temple to cultivate crops and raise animals as raw materials to produce food service products to serve the needs of tourists.
