Kampong Thom Provincial Governor: Authorities will build a new road around the Sambor Prei Kuk temple to sustain the heritage in this archeological site
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, said that in the future, the authorities will build a new road from the Sambor Prei Kuk temple area to maintain the World Heritage site in this ancient site so that heavy vehicles can not pass. Let the crossing affect the temple area as it is now.
Mr. Sok Lou made this statement during a meeting with the tourism community of Sambor Prei Kuk presided over by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism at the Sambor Prei Kuk temple on the afternoon of September 8, 2019.
He said that the limitation for such construction was due to the fact that under the site of Sambor Prei Kuk, there are still a lot of traces of temples and heritage after aerial reflection by national and international experts. .
Mr. Sok Loo added that in the past, there has been criticism of the current road that passes through the center of Isan Borei, blaming the authorities of Prasat Sambo district.
In response to the above criticism, the provincial governor clarified that "the construction of this road is not the responsibility of the district authority, it is the authority of the Sambor Prei Kuk National Authority, but the Prasat Sambor district authority is not indifferent to this issue. "Let's build a new detour from the Sambor Prei Kuk temple area, and this detour will allow heavy vehicles to pass."
He said that the current road into the temple area was built and used during the French colonial period for pedestrians, ox-carts, buffaloes, elephants, etc., but now this road is used for all kinds of vehicles, which is a risk. To heritage property. However, the provincial governor Sok Lou confirmed that the road construction project may take place at the end of this year or next year.
He explained, "If our country does not strive to maintain the sustainability of the Sambor Prei Kuk temple site, UNESCO will remove the temple site from the World Heritage List, so it is necessary for proper management by the Sambor Prey Kuk Authority. "Prison."
Not unlike the words of Minister Thong Khon, the management of the above work is to attract more tourists to visit, and the benefits also reach the local people first and foremost.
