Ream Monisilong is a Cambodian artist who uses kitchen waste and organic waste to make paintings and souvenirs.
He recycles many kinds of waste that Cambodians leave in the kitchen and throws it away, such as fish skin, snail shells, duck eggs, as well as organic waste such as dead leaves, papaya trees, coconut husks, palm fronds and sugar cane. Can be processed into paper and painted beautifully.
