(Phnom Penh): From Beijing, China, Her Majesty the Queen Mother Norodom Monineath Sihanouk of the Kingdom of Cambodia issued a royal message to her compatriots about the history of Preah Ang Chek-Preah Ang Cham Temple during the Sangkum Reastr Niyum era. .
In the 1960s, His Majesty the King Father of the Khmer Nation, His Majesty the King, built a small temple in front of the "Royal Palace" in Siem Reap, with a solemn ceremony, a procession of statues of King Banana - King Cham Come and live in that little church. Unfortunately, this small church was destroyed during the Khmer Rouge regime and also lost the Banana-Cham statue.
In the 1980s, the Cambodian state discovered the Banana-Cham statue and built a large temple on the same site to house the Banana-Cham statue as a sacred place of worship in the historical territory of the province. Siem Reap.
