(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment has produced and disseminated an environmental education video spot in order to increase knowledge as well as participate in correcting people's attitudes regarding the use of plastic bags and to increase the efficiency of reducing imports, production, distribution and consumption. Plastic bags are intended to ensure the protection of public health, the environment and aesthetics.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, said that the amount of urban waste generated in Cambodia is more than 10,000 tons per day, which people in the capital and major cities are estimated. That produces 1 kg of garbage per day and people living in rural areas generate about half a kilo of garbage per day.
He said that in total, the amount of waste that Cambodia generates is about 4 million tons, of which 20% is plastic bag waste. The major provinces that produce large amounts of waste include Phnom Penh, more than 3,000 tons per day, Sihanoukville, about 700 tons per day, and Siem Reap, nearly 400 tons per day.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment also said that the sub-decree on the management of plastic bags focused on four main points, including:
First, the size and thickness of the portable plastic bag is prohibited for import, domestic production, distribution and consumption (thickness 0.03 mm and bottom width 25 cm).
Second: Incentives: Import and production of plastics or packaging materials made from perishable materials or bio-plastics, which are subject to special taxes as a burden on the state. Third, the import or production of plastic bags will be subject to special tax.
