Legal Awareness: Acquisition of Khmer Nationality by Foreigners
(Phnom Penh): Nationality refers to the legal and political bonds that connect a physical person to a country. The granting of citizenship to a natural person in certain countries has different conditions according to the laws of the country that grants citizenship.
For the Law on Khmer Nationality 2018 of the Kingdom of Cambodia, the granting of citizenship to foreigners determines the conditions for obtaining Khmer citizenship in 4 (four) cases: (1) Acquisition of Khmer nationality by birth (2) Acquisition Khmer nationality by full adoption (3) Acquisition of Khmer nationality by marriage and (4) Acquisition of Khmer nationality by naturalization.
To find out more about foreigners 'acquisition of Cambodian citizenship, for this week, FRESH NEWS' Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation, brings up the topic of "Acquisition of Cambodians by Foreigners". Present to the people, students as follows:
For children born to a Cambodian father or mother, no matter where they were born, that child will automatically be entitled to Khmer citizenship by birth. Wherever the child is born, the parents do not recognize him, but if the court rules that the child was born of a Cambodian father or mother, the child will receive Cambodian citizenship.
Children of foreigners born in Cambodia must acquire Cambodian citizenship only if they are born to foreign parents born and living legally in the Kingdom of Cambodia. Children born to unknown parents and newborns selected in the Kingdom of Cambodia shall also be considered born in the Kingdom of Cambodia and shall acquire Khmer citizenship.
2: Acquisition of Khmer nationality by full adoption (Article 10)
Foreign children who have applied for full adoption by their Cambodian spouses must acquire Cambodian citizenship when the full adoption is legally established. The word spouse means a spouse or both spouses who have the status of spouse after the legal marriage registration.
3: Acquisition of Khmer nationality by marriage (Article 11)
A woman or a man who marries a Cambodian man or wife who is married can claim Khmer citizenship only if the woman or man has been living together for 3 (three) years after the marriage is registered and has stayed for at least 12 (ten) years. Two) A full month in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Minor children with a foreign father or mother are allowed to apply for Cambodian citizenship as a family.
Separately, Article 12 of the Law on Nationality also stipulates that foreigners who can apply for Khmer citizenship by marriage must meet the following conditions:
4: Acquisition of Khmer nationality by naturalization (Article 18)
Naturalization refers to the granting of Cambodian citizenship at the request of a foreigner based on the conditions of residence, investment, gifts, cash and special privileges or special hands.
This nationalization is not the right of the applicant, it is only the favor of the Kingdom of Cambodia. In either case, the application may be denied by discretion.
4.1: General foreigners must meet the following conditions:
4.4: Foreigners who have been granted special qualifications (Article 23) That can apply for Khmer nationality by naturalization if the person meets the conditions as stated in points 1, 2 and 6 of the above conditions.
In general, foreigners applying for Cambodian citizenship must comply with the procedures and procedures of the Law on Nationality of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and the granting of Cambodian citizenship to foreigners shall be decided by Royal Decree and must be sworn in before the Supreme Court.
Citizens who acquire Cambodian citizenship may not be deprived of their citizenship, deported or deported to any foreign country unless there is a mutual agreement, and those who are Cambodian citizens are at least 18 (eighteen) years old. Chhnang can apply for renunciation of Khmer nationality if the person has another nationality without coercion.
