Kampong Cham Provincial Information Director Urges Information Officers to Join Against False Information
(Kampong Cham): The director of the Kampong Cham Provincial Information Department, Mr. Chea Kroch, said, "We, the information officers, must dare to tell the truth in order to disseminate information to the people and must participate in the production of information clips against false information."
The director of the Department of Information said so at a staff meeting on the afternoon of September 6, 2019.
Mr. Chea Kroch said, "The Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has strived to maintain peace and development in all areas up to now, so all the achievements and happiness that we all "As well as the people are getting this, we have to accept the truth and write to let our people know, which means that we contribute to the development of our country through the media."
At the same time, Mr. Chea Kroch urged the competition information officer to act as a news club against fake news because the Minister of Information, Mr. Khieu Kanharith, recently organized this competition. If you make a good anti-fake news clip, the first place winner will receive 4 million riels, the second place winner will receive 3 million riels and the third place winner will receive 2 million riels.
(Phnom Penh): From now on, those who do business on social media or online must go through education, vocational training, legal knowledge and business standards, as well as related knowledge to avoid making mistakes in doing business. Meanwhile, senior officials of the National Police have already warned about the implementation of the law and punished those who violate the law online.
This was confirmed at the opening ceremony of the web marketing business training course on September 7, 2019, chaired by Mr. Ley Sopheap, President of the Federation of Medical, Pharmaceutical and Dentistry of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Network Marketers Association, Lt. Gen. Chea Bunthol, Vice President. Central Department of Judicial Police of the National Police and Mr. Ly Sinon, Director General of NSZ World.
During the ceremony, Dr. Ley Sopheap said, "Today is the first day in the history of Cambodia that network marketing business people are invited to receive information and training on the law, business standards and policies of the Royal Government from senior officials. Of the National Police, experts as well as some leaders.
He added that the establishment of this training course aims to promote small and medium enterprises to receive proper promotion and training through the Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) system of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training. And the policy of the Royal Government so that they can get the right knowledge and professional skills to avoid unknowingly making mistakes like in the past.
Of course, web marketers have not been able to do their business properly in the past, including the implementation of government laws and policies and the implementation of web marketing standards, but not. It is not anyone's fault, because no one invited them to come for training, according to Mr. Ley Sopheap.
He added that the Royal Government of Cambodia considers the private sector as an important partner in the development of the national economy, which is why his association, in cooperation with the National Police, invites business people both online and offline to provide promotion and training. Join the Royal Government in paying attention to the private sector and to make them understand the relevant issues in their business.
Not only that, the above training course also wants to encourage all business people to support the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and support the policies of the Royal Government.
Mr. Ley Sopheap declared that "Only doing business through this network marketing can help promote strong economic development, especially to provide income to those who run small and medium enterprises that the Royal Government is taking care of." .
Lt. Gen. Chea Bunthol also warned of clear enforcement and penalties at all levels for online businesses that continue to commit offenses and guarantees protection for businesses that comply with standards and professionalism, while the law for entrepreneurs. Online business is also in the hands of the Parliament and before the approval, decision and go into force to apply to businesses in the modern technology, or digitalization.
