Pailin provincial authorities open the construction site of a concrete road in the city that has not had access for many years
(Pailin): At the request of the people, on September 7, 2019, Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, accompanied by leaders, government officials, professional institutions around the province and local authorities and working groups invited to open the construction. A 200-meter concrete road is located in Sangkat Toul Lvea and Sangkat Pailin, Pailin City, Pailin Province, which has been facing difficulties for many years.
Mr. Phan Chanthul said that roads and bridges are the lifeblood of the national economy and families, so there is a road to hope, and the construction of this road really meets the needs of the people, easy to traffic in life. Daily life, in particular, has made it easier for students to travel to school.
The provincial governor confirmed that the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has made efforts to solve all the difficulties and requests of the people as well as to build the development of the country in all fields, especially the construction of physical infrastructure. Such as: roads, bridges, schools, hospitals, etc.
On that occasion, Mr. Phan Chanthul urged all people who use this road to cooperate and coordinate the impact in the construction of this road as soon as possible as planned and to help maintain. Ensures long service life.
The people who use this road expressed their happiness and deep gratitude to the provincial leaders at all levels, especially the provincial governor, who quickly decided to build this road.
Please note that one concrete road that Pailin Provincial Authority has started to open the construction site now is 200 meters long, 6 meters wide, 1 meter diameter, 7 meters long, using a provincial development budget. Minister of Agriculture Leads a Working Group to Inspect Farmers' Cultivation in Takeo and Kampot Provinces
(Takeo): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on September 7, 2019, led the mission team in Takeo province to monitor and evaluate the cultivation, implementation of technical work, leadership management. And the implementation of the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategic Policy Phase 4.
The Minister's mission lasts for 2 days from September 7 to 8 to Takeo and Kampot provinces.
On the occasion of inspecting the production of farmers in Takeo province, Mr. Veng Sakhon on September 7, 2019, advised the people to make more efforts on crop production, increase production volume, ensure quality and improve processing capacity. To compete to meet market needs and consumer preferences.
This request was made on the occasion that Mr. Veng Sakhon led the mission team in Takeo province to monitor and evaluate the production work, the implementation of technical work, the management work and the implementation of the policy of the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy. The Royal Government in each department this morning, September 7, 2019.
On the occasion of leading the mission team in Takeo province, Minister Veng Sakhon and the provincial governor expressed their happiness and congratulations for the achievements of the farmers to get crops, income, reunion and happiness in the family.
Minister Veng Sakhon stated that it is the will and desire of the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister, to see the people live in peace, well-being, prosperity and happiness.
He said that because the country has peace, social, economic and political stability, which makes it easier for people to live in harmony, engaged in farming, animal husbandry, fish farming and planting crops according to their ability to sustain family economic growth. .
He urged people to make more efforts to increase production, increase production volume, ensure quality, improve processing capacity to compete to meet market needs and consumer preferences, and especially to take care of health. Peace and stability can only lead to continuous development.
Regarding technical work, the Minister also advised farmers to pay more attention to land leveling, grass maintenance, pest management and water use to ensure increased yields, and the Department of Agriculture should help organize rice seed production communities to ensure quality. Personal consumption reduces the purchase of rice seeds without a clear source and cost. The body of a boy who was swept away by a tornado for 4 days in Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province has been found
(Preah Vihear): The body of a boy who went missing for 3 nights and 4 days in Techo Bosbov village, Sra Em commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province, was found on the afternoon of September 6, 2019 by smashing a tree 200 meters away. Meters from the scene.
It should be noted that on the evening of September 3, 2019, a 2-year-old boy was swept away by a whirlwind while riding a motorbike while his parents were riding in a taxi across a dam with high water flow.
After the incident, the district police force and the military force of Choam Ksan district military operation area and the family tried to search for the body of the victim boy and the motorcycle, but did not find it until 3 nights and 4 days before finding both the motorcycle and the body of the victim boy. Once. Election of Vice President of Kampong Cham-Mondulkiri Chamber of Commerce, Senior Officials of the Ministry of Commerce Introduce Solidarity to Prepare for Major Investors
