Ministry of Culture begins to strengthen the capacity of officials to oversee the film industry as the film industry is constantly evolving
(Phnom Penh): In order to further promote the film industry, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts has started to strengthen the capacity of film industry supervisors so that they have the full capacity to manage the film industry. Climb relentlessly.
In order to further strengthen the capacity of officials, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts organized a workshop on "Capacity Building of Film Industry Supervisors" on September 6, 2019 with the participation of Mr. Som Sokun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Culture. And Fine Arts, Mr. Pok Borak, Director of the Department of Film Arts and Cultural Promotion, and several staff officers.
Mr. Som Sokun said that the film industry has played an important role in participating in the implementation of the Royal Government's political program, especially the national policy on culture to achieve success.
He added, "The film industry has really played an important role in the implementation of the Royal Government's political program, especially the national policy on the cultural sector to achieve success, because the film industry has contributed to the protection, preservation of cultural heritage and strengthening national identity. "
Mr. Som Sokun continued that the provision of public services in the film industry has been evolving while the national economy is growing steadily. Given the growing demand for public services in the film industry, the Ministry of Culture, through the Department of Film, has made the first priority on improving work efficiency and increasing the capacity of film industry managers and public service providers. Competent enough.
Mr. Pok Borak said that this workshop was held in order to strengthen the management of the film industry in Cambodia effectively to ensure the sustainable development of credibility in providing better public services in the film industry in accordance with the principles. National policy on the field of culture, especially in response to the evolution of society.
He expressed his belief that the film industry management officers of the Ministry of Culture, especially local officials, will gain knowledge, skills and experience to be used in a targeted manner to improve the efficiency of film management and the provision of public services. The film industry to be better for the people.
According to the report of the Department of Film, in the five years from 2014-2018, the revenue collected from the provision of public services in the film industry increased significantly, while the number of viewers of cinemas increased. More than 5 million people nationwide, and movie ticket sales are more than $ 15 million a year.
