Announcing the appointment of 39 members of the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Kampot province, 5th mandate, Mr. Pen Simon is the honorary chairman while Mr. Chiao Tai is the branch president.
(Kampot): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, has appointed 39 members of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch of Kampot Branch of the 5th Mandate in the Opening Ceremony of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Kampot Province. 5th mandate (2019-2025) in the morning of September 7, 2019 at the Provincial Conference Hall.
In this 5th mandate meeting, the Cambodian Red Cross, chaired by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, appointed Dr. Pen Simon as the Honorary Chairman and Honorary Vice President of the branch, a total of 39 people.
Full members elected the 5th Mandate Branch Committee, consisting of 15 members, including Mr. Chiao Tai as Branch Committee Chairman, Ms. Leang Hay, Permanent Vice Chairman, Ms. You Sokun, Vice Chairman, Mr. Yin Bun An, Deputy Chairman, Mrs. Tith Setha, Treasurer and Mr. Nha Bunthon, Secretary of Branch Committee for Kampot Province.
On that occasion, Mr. Chiao Tai, Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee of Kampot Province, 5th mandate, strongly committed to continue to strengthen good governance, strengthen and expand the capacity to raise funds and manage accountability and transparency.
He strives to strengthen the capacity for effective disaster management, must strive to expand and develop the driving force, including: youth and volunteers involved more actively and continue to strive to develop sub-branches to be a good branch in all fields.
Ms. Pum Chantyny commended the Branch Committee of the 4th Mandate Branch Committee, as well as the members, volunteers, Red Cross Youth Advisers and the Red Cross Sub-Branch of the Municipalities and Districts for fulfilling their noble mission with courage and non-discrimination. Willingness at all times to make the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Kampot province run smoothly from one mandate to another.
