Kun Kim Inspects Impact of Mekong River Flood in Kratie Province
(Kratie): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, this morning, September 7, 2019, led officials to inspect the impact situation of people directly in the backyard.
During the inspection of the flood situation as well as the impact, Mr. Kun Kim brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross.
Mr. Kun Kim informed the people that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit were constantly monitoring the impact of the people due to the flooding of the Mekong River and reminded the relevant officials to help and solve all these problems. . In addition, the two Samdechs also expressed their condolences to the people for the impact caused by the flooding of the Mekong River.
The Senior Minister also made some recommendations to the Provincial Disaster Management Committee to be prepared and take timely and effective response measures to reduce the impact to the lowest level by focusing on high priority on human life.
The floods affected more than 3,000 hectares of rice paddies in Kratie province, affecting more than 400 hectares of mixed crops. The provincial authorities have paid close attention to rescuing and solving the problems of the people.
Mr. Vath Thorn, Provincial Governor and Chairman of the Provincial Disaster Management Committee, led the provincial team to visit and bring medical equipment, mosquito nets to distribute to flood victims and vaccinate cattle at Toul Safety, Takhin Village. Prek Kov, Bos Leav Commune, Chit Borey District. The provincial governor also visited the people in Kratie city and the 51st Hun Sen pumping station to release water from Kratie provincial town.
