The Ministry of Labor announces the results of today's meeting of the National Minimum Wage Council, where unions are proposing $ 199 and employers are proposing $ 184.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has announced an official result for the National Minimum Wage Council meeting this morning, September 6, 2019, with the union side requesting a $ 199 wage, while the employer request Provide only $ 184 per month for garment workers by 2020.
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training confirmed that: On Friday, September 8, 2019, the National Council for Minimum Wages continued its third meeting to Negotiate the minimum wage for textiles, garments and footwear for 2020 after the workers 'and employers' sides held two internal meetings.
The Ministry of Labor said that each party continued to discuss vigorously and presented its initial position to the meeting, with the workers 'side proposing the figure of 199 US dollars and the employers' side proposing the figure of 184 US dollars as the minimum wage figure. Textiles, garments and footwear for 2020. Each party agreed to continue the meeting on September 12, 2019 at 3 pm.
