(Phnom Penh): Cambodia's capital Phnom Penh has been invited by the United Nations Industrial Development Organization (UNIDO) to participate in the 4th International Smart Cities Forum, held in Vienna, Austria from March 3 to 4. This past September.
The forum was attended by city leaders from 30 countries from Asia, Europe and Africa, as well as representatives from international organizations and the private sector to discuss, exchange experiences and find good solutions. By Ly Yong, Director-General of the United Nations Industrial Development Organization (UNIDO) on "Bridges to Cities 4.0: Connecting Cities through the Industrial Revolution".
Participating in this important event from Cambodia were Mr. Phan Phalla, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Economy and Finance, Mr. Nuon Pharath, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Kong Vithanak, Deputy Governor of Sihanoukville and Ms. Khon Khema, Director of International Relations Office of Phnom Penh Administration. All are invited to serve as speakers and mayoral roundtables for their respective programs.
The forum focuses on six major issues: (1) Climate change, (2) Sustainable infrastructure, (3) Resource management, (4) Environmental development, (5) Use modern technology to manage cities and (6) consider the possibility of choosing new financing methods suitable for development in the Industrial Age 4.0 and the era of smart cities.
It should also be noted that UNIDO is a United Nations body in charge of industrial development.
