(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government and civil society work together to build a women's network for peace in order to help women escape violence and abuse at the grassroots level. The International Women's Committee for Peace has agreed to build a network of women for peace in all 25 capitals and provinces to bring peace to the community. Currently, the network has expanded to 21 networks in Preah Vihear, Kandal, Takeo, Sihanoukville and Battambang Province.
Speaking at a meeting of the International Women's Committee for Peace 2019 this morning, September 5, 2019, Ms. Hoy Sochivanny, a representative of the International Women's Committee for Peace, affirmed that the Women's Network for Peace has a very important role in society through Educating society to avoid violence, to provide methods and strategies to do good deeds in society, not to harass others, that is, to help guide people to love peace.
She said the mechanism also helps women become more courageous in making decisions in the community to contribute to local development.
At the same time, Ms. Long Phally, Undersecretary of State for the Ministry of Women's Affairs, affirmed that the Royal Government strongly supports the project to establish a network of women for peace in the community, in order to contribute to the protection of peace in Cambodia, especially the prevention of violence and abuse. Women.
It should be noted that the establishment of the International Women's Committee for Peace in Cambodia took place while women are still vulnerable to violence and abuse from society. Ministry of Tourism continues to promote many tourist destinations to Vietnamese travel agencies
(Ho Chi Minh City - Vietnam): In addition to participating in the 15th International Tourism Fair, which is being held from September 4 to 7, 2019 in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam, the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia also organized a workshop. REX Hotel on the afternoon of September 5 to promote some important tourist destinations to tour operators as well as travel agencies there.
Good hospitality and many of Cambodia's major tourist destinations such as Phnom Penh, Siem Reap-Angkor, Sihanoukville, Kampot, Battambang, Kampong Thom, Kratie, Stung Treng, Kandal, Koh Kong, the coastal region, the Northeast and some other destinations are explained in detail with screenings. Pictures and videos as well. There will also be presentations on accommodation, air transportation, catering and more.
After a presentation by officials from the Ministry of Tourism and the private sector from Cambodia, the workshop raised questions and answers, which seemed to show a strong interest in tourism destinations in Cambodia by Vietnamese travel agencies. .
The Ministry of Tourism's efforts to organize international exhibitions in Vietnam and past efforts seem to emphasize that the promotion of overseas destinations is essential for boosting international tourism.
Since the establishment of this major annual tourism event, Cambodia has been invited to participate every year, which has encouraged tourism cooperation between Cambodia, Vietnam and other countries around the world to be strengthened and expanded, especially tourism destinations. Much of Cambodia was also promoted through the event.
Due to the efforts to promote tourism both domestically and abroad, in 2018, Cambodia achieved a growth rate of about 10.7% with the arrival of more than 6.2 million international tourists and bring money. About $ 4,356 million is injected into the national economy.
At the same time, Cambodia also expressed the expectation that by 2020 will receive more than 7 million tourists and bring about 5 billion dollars, creating nearly 1 million jobs.
