The senior official made the remarks at a press conference on "Cambodia and Democracy" organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government of Cambodia at the Office of the Council of Ministers this morning, September 5, 2019.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior stated that in order to maintain economic strength and public administration, it is necessary for the participation of the Royal Government, relevant partners and the people themselves.
He claimed that in order to increase the efficiency of public administration, the Royal Government of Cambodia has made a lot of reforms to facilitate the people. The Royal Government has transferred power to sub-national administrations and organized public forums to listen to the concerns of the people and to speed up the resolution of their problems. He claimed that so far seven ministries have transferred functions to the local.
In addition, the Royal Government of Cambodia has set out five approaches to improve shortcomings and strengthen the quality of public administration. "So far we have been on the right track and just not as smooth as we would like," he said.
He stressed that decentralization and deconcentration reforms have really contributed to the strengthening of democracy at the grassroots level, the improvement of people's lives, the strengthening of local leadership, both men and women. Make improvements to local public services as well.
"Over the past 15 years, we have been able to assess governance reform through the implementation of the OWSO administrative services and the settlement of citizen office grievances, the implementation of social accountability action plans," he said. Achieve positive results and get the support and active participation of all stakeholders, especially the people who receive effective and transparent services.
He said that these are evidence that the decentralization and deconcentration reforms in Cambodia have really improved the quality and efficiency of service delivery and provide opportunities for local administrations close to the people to fulfill their roles, duties and functions. In accordance with the law, the organization aims to make the provision of administrative services more responsive to the actual needs at the local level.
