Ministry of Health warns people how to protect their health during floods
(Phnom Penh): After the floods in some provinces on September 5, 2019, the Minister of Health, Professor Mam Bun Heng, reminded the people again about the disaster caused by the floods caused by the floods. Damage to infrastructure, property, housing, especially infectious diseases affecting health that endangers life.
In addition, in order to minimize the impact on the health, lives of victims and health facilities from natural disasters, especially floods, Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, called on all people to follow the guidelines. The following:
1: Before the flood: Monitor the flood situation, prepare safe places and food. Build a fence around a pond or a place with deep water, keep the environment clean, and build toilets that need to be upgraded from low to high to prevent flooding.
Do not enter an old house or a dilapidated building during a flood because it may cause a ruined district. Do not touch electrical appliances with wet hands or standing in water while traveling by boat or ferry at night, keep the lights on.
* For pregnant women, follow up and check the pregnancy according to the schedule of the health center or hospital. If the woman is about to give birth, find a place to stay near the health center or hospital nearest to you.
Be careful of girls and girls in safe places to avoid sexual violence.
Be careful to avoid drowning, prevent small children from drowning, explain to children the dangers of drowning, take children to higher ground and have a caregiver use a jacket or plastic bag every time a child leaves the house. When traveling by boat or ferry, do not overcrowd if someone drowns, call for help immediately.
To avoid respiratory infections, it is necessary to wear a mask or a towel or scarf to cover the mouth when coughing or sneezing, and to stay away from patients who cough or sneeze for more than 1 meter and not near the premises. There is dust, if necessary wear a mask. When the weather changes suddenly, take care of your health, such as dressing properly and avoiding going out for long periods of time.
2: After the flood
* Continue to eat clean food, clean water and clean body to avoid various diseases.
* Continue to sleep under a mosquito net at all times to prevent dengue fever and malaria.
* Check the house for collapse or danger, beware of snakes or other venomous animals.
* Clean the environment around the house and inside the house because after the water recedes, leaving a lot of dirt and germs living in the water, avoid putting water around the house and inside the house, leading to water worms, tiger mosquitoes and nail mosquitoes that can cause To have dengue fever and malaria.
* Restore and clean the well before use.
* As well as repairing and rebuilding toilets, always having to defecate in the toilet at all times.
The Ministry of Health states, "Before, during and after the flood, if you have a health problem, seek immediate medical attention and treatment at a health center near a safe place or a health center or hospital near you. You most.
The Ministry of Health has instructed all Capital-Provincial Health Departments to be ready with anti-snake medicine medicine and equipment to intervene when there are snake bites, as well as to have a team of mobile doctors to help treat patients. "Have good and timely health problems in accordance with proper medical practice."
