At least 10 innocent people have been killed and 42 others injured in a suicide car bombing in the Afghan capital, Kabul. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Thursday evening, September 5, 2019.
Afghan Interior Ministry spokesman Rahimi told Xinhua that the suicide bombing took place at 10:10 a.m. Thursday (Kabul time) in front of the administration building. Of the 42 injured, 12 were seriously injured.
Shortly after the suicide bombing, Taliban militants claimed responsibility for the attack.
