MANILA: Philippine President Rodrigo Duterte has said that although he is not a fan of online gambling, he has no intention of banning trade in line with what China has called for. If so, it will have an impact on the Philippine economy. This is according to the release by Reuters, which was quoted on the evening of Thursday, September 5, 2019.
Duterte, who previously supported the regulatory action of the gambling business in late 2016 to license the online gambling business, said he would not allow "silly activities" to shut down online gambling. Not if it has been providing more jobs in the Philippines.
"We have decided to uphold my country's interests," the Filipino strongman said. "I decided we needed it (online gambling)." Even so, Duterte also warned that all gambling operators should not forget to pay taxes to the state.
