On Wednesday, Hong Kong Mayor Carroll announced that she would officially repeal the controversial extradition law, the main reason for the tumultuous protests in the autonomous city of China. It has been more than three months now.
The extradition order aims to allow Hong Kong suspects to be handed over to mainland Chinese authorities, sparking controversy that sparked massive protests across Hong Kong in recent months. Before. While in July, Ms. Lam announced that the extradition law had been abolished and that it had not yet been repealed.
The repeal of the draft law is one of the five main demands of the protesters, including the request for Lam to resign. However, some protesters said that the official cancellation seemed a bit too late.
Cambodia, Saudi Arabia continue bilateral cooperation in the field of labor
The meeting focused on cooperation in the field of labor, which Cambodia and Saudi Arabia have cooperated well in the past and are continuing to strengthen.
Minister Ith Sam Heng also briefed the Ambassador on the progress on employment and vocational training in Cambodia.
Speaking to reporters after the meeting, Minister Ith Sam Heng said that after the signing of the agreement, the two sides implemented the technical coordination and complete the procedures for training on the transmission. So far, we have 40 legal agencies working well with Saudi Arabia.
However, the number of Cambodian workers there is still small, while the number of foreign workers working in Saudi Arabia is close to 15 million.
He noted that Saudi Arabia is a large market that absorbs foreign labor from Asia, India, Pakistan, Bangladesh and many other countries.
During the meeting, the Minister informed the parties about the possibility of attracting the labor market, focusing on the issue of wages, which in the past, some countries have received workers from Cambodia to work at a reasonable price, such as the Republic of Korea and Japan. Cambodian workers have worked hard to learn and seize the opportunity, and working conditions and safety at work, as well as return, are attractive and inviting.
In addition, Saudi Arabia is a country that has a better management system and crisis management or labor challenges that Cambodia should consider.
