The Phnom Penh Municipal Authority has decided to set up a task force to study various issues related to the project to build a sidewalk from the Cambodia Post to the area in front of the Royal Palace soon to meet the needs of national and international tourists.
Speaking at the meeting of the Technical Working Group of the Capital Hall this morning, September 5, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh confirmed that the project to build a sidewalk will be a new tourist package for Phnom Penh to attract tourists to walk to breathe the air. Fresh air and beautiful views of the four rivers like no other country.
The governor instructed the team to study the time, the traffic avoidance system and the parking lot properly so that the new tour package can run smoothly without disturbing the people.
Previously, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, said that this pedestrian tour package can be made three days a week, Friday, Saturday and Sunday, and no other vehicles are allowed to pass, only for pedestrians. Only.
He stated that the Royal Government wants to create this sidewalk to show tourists from the special point of Phnom Penh is the view of the intersection of four beautiful rivers, which are very attractive.
Please note that this project to create a pedestrian tourism package will be carried out under the cooperation between the administration of Phnom Penh Capital Hall and the Ministry of Tourism under the guidance of Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Chairs a Meeting to Summarize the Results of the Public Forum of Battambang Provincial National Working Group
(Battambang): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, chaired a meeting to review the results of the Battambang Provincial National Working Group. .
This meeting was held at Stung Sangke Theater, Battambang City this morning, September 5, 2019, with the participation of members of the Royal Government, Senators, National Assembly, Chairman of the Working Group to Assist Municipalities, Districts, Communes in Provinces, Provincial Leaders, Provincial Councils. Municipalities, districts, members of the working group, government officials around many provinces as well.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated that after collecting the results of all the challenges in the first round, we have more than 1,000 challenges for Battambang province and need to solve for the local people and continue the public forum. To collect more data to solve them.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also advised that from now until the end of 2019, working groups at all levels must focus on the following important tasks:
* First, to organize the action plan of the commune, sangkat, municipal, district and provincial working groups to address the challenges and requests collected from the public forum in accordance with the principles and measures outlined above. And report on the progress of the settlement on a monthly basis.
* Second: Continue to cooperate in local work, especially in the backyard to meet with people from all walks of life to find out about the concerns, practical requests of the people's families and challenges, suggestions that the team To be able to solve, the working group must solve for the people any problems that can not be solved, report to the higher working group to review and coordinate to solve.
* Third: To strengthen and enhance the capacity of leaders, officials and units at all levels at the sub-national level to perform their duties, especially the ability and ownership to provide services and development at the local level, to address challenges, proposals Of the people to avoid complete reliance on the team.
* Fourth, continue to cooperate with the authorities, the competent forces at all levels to jointly educate people from all walks of life to participate in maintaining peace, social stability, maintaining security, order, safety in society and participation in social development in all fields.
Six suspects arrested in drug distribution and use cases in Stung Trang and Chamkar Leu districts, Kampong Cham province
(Kampong Cham): Six suspects were arrested in connection with drug distribution and use cases in Stung Trang and Chamkar Leu districts, Kampong Cham province, and some drugs were confiscated.
Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Em Kosal said that the operation took place on September 4, 2019 at Prek Bak village, Prek Bak commune, Stung Trang district and in Opei village, Choyo commune, Chamkar Leu district, Kampong Cham province.
He added that the operation was carried out in accordance with the Royal Government's fourth anti-drug campaign plan and the order of the National Police General Gen. Neth Savoeun, urging measures to crack down on drug activities.
Lt. Gen. Em Kosal said that after receiving information from the people, he commanded the Kampong Cham Provincial Anti-Drug Office with the Stung Trang District Police Inspectorate and the Chamkar Leu District Inspectorate, led by Lt. Col. Chiv Seng Ros.
As a result, 2 cases were cracked down by incitement and 6 suspects were arrested, 6 white gram powder exhibits, 7 mobile phones, 2 motorcycles, 2 swords and some packaging bags were confiscated. The suspect has now been sent to a specialized office to build a case for further action.
More than three decades of war in Cambodia have not only devastated Cambodia's economy, but also destroyed infrastructure, roads and bridges, and left no room for construction. After rescuing the country from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot in 1979, rescuing and building road and bridge infrastructure was one of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's four priority priorities, including water, roads, electricity and people.
Since Cambodia found complete peace in 1998, the construction of road and bridge infrastructure has been rapid, and to date, many roads have been upgraded and expanded.
Dr. Ky Sereyvath stated: "When people talk about the economy of a country, they always talk about infrastructure because it is called the economic artery. So when a country has its infrastructure cut off, it means that the flow of goods in the country is disrupted, so all the production in the country is meaningless. "But due to the development of infrastructure, factories have been able to share in rural areas."
Dr. Ky Sereyvath added: “When spending money in the countryside, turn a house in a rural area into a tile house, a wooden house, a stone house. So the infrastructure is to move the factory away from the city to the low-wage areas, where the costs are lower and they can easily transport all those goods to the port and help the economy grow. The distribution is equal to the meat.
Of the $ 2.865 million in infrastructure loans, the Ministry of Public Works has completed the construction of 29 roads, equivalent to 2,888 km, and the construction of eight 8-kilometer bridges at a total cost of two. , $ 513 million. At the same time, the Ministry of Public Works is also preparing to build National Road No. 71C, National Road No. 10 at a cost of 322 million US dollars and Phnom Penh Port 30 million US dollars.
Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, described China as an important contributor to the rehabilitation and construction of road and bridge infrastructure in Cambodia.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who succeeded in building relations with China after His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, saw that the presence of road and bridge infrastructure in Cambodia stemmed from good relations between China and Cambodia. . Samdech Techo Hun Sen highly valued China's assistance in the construction of Cambodia's roads and bridges.
Samdech Techo, the Prime Minister, stated, "All these points, if there is no China, ask who is really helping us, because others have only shouted and disciplined, but they have not given us anything. So, the question is, if we do not have good relations with China, can China afford to pay for our construction? "So I really understand that it is not wrong for us to pursue a partnership policy in cooperation with China."
In order to contribute to the development of Cambodia as a friendly country of steel, China not only provides low-interest loans and assistance in the construction of infrastructure, China also provides training to officials of the Ministry of Public Works, students, Cambodia. Build this too.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has given the slogan, "There are roads, there are bridges, there is hope," which is in line with the Chinese government's words, "There are roads, there is gold, there is silver." Through this slogan, it is shown that roads and bridges contribute significantly to improving the national economy and people's lives.
Dr. Ky Serivath, an economist and chairman of the Chinese Studies Center at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, sees the construction of the road as one of the most important considerations in improving the lives of people in rural areas. He said that helping people is not the distribution of gifts, but the construction of roads is to help people realistically and carefully.
After receiving this beautiful flexible national road, the people in the area expressed their happiness and excitement almost unimaginably from the changes of the area where they live. Hean Chhon, a former Khmer Rouge soldier, stated:
Although Chinese loans are seen as contributing to improving the national economy and improving people's livelihoods. But there have been some concerns about the debt, with some accusing it of being a Chinese trap.
Minister Sun Chanthol categorically denied and dismissed the allegations. The minister claimed that Cambodia had clearly managed and dealt with this debt and that China had never forced or pressured Cambodia to borrow its money.
(Preah Sihanouk): The forces of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Unity Command since this morning, September 5, 2019, have helped to dismantle the houses of the people as illegal constructions built on the sidewalk, at the point of the burning bridge on Ke Otres Road for many years. Then moved to a new location in Kbal Chhay after the Royal Government provided them with social land per family, a lot of 5 by 20 meters.
Forty-five families, equivalent to 45 houses, have been building illegal houses on the street at the site of the fire for many years, and only now has the Royal Government addressed them by providing them with a social land policy for new housing. Days.
Speaking to Fresh News, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, confirmed that after the voluntary approval of the 45 families from the Royal Government's policy, the provincial authorities, municipal authorities, law enforcement forces and people helped to dismantle their homes. He moved from the old location to the new location, along with the provision of zinc, some consumables and some money.
The provincial governor also thanked General Hing Bun Heang, Commander-in-Chief of the Bodyguard Command, for providing large and small tents for temporary construction to shelter the people from the rain until they have finished building their houses.
