Senior Agriculture Officer: There are more than 43 million livestock in Cambodia
(Tbong Khmum): This morning, September 5, 2019, at Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Agriculture, a workshop was held on strengthening the management of livestock farms to disseminate more awareness to professional officers, company owners, livestock farms and stakeholders. Tbong Khmum Province.
Mr. Seang Soklim, Director of the Animal Production Department of the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, presided over the workshop. Raising animals as a family and raising animals commercially. There are three levels of commercial animal husbandry: small, medium and large.
He stated that commercial animal husbandry requires the owner of the farm to ask for a law from the competent authorities in accordance with the content of Prakas No. 449, on the contrary, the traditional family animal husbandry to serve daily life does not require the law. No, but must be under the technical control of the competent authorities.
Mr. Seang Soklim said that animal husbandry in Cambodia has contributed significantly to the national economic growth, which contributes about 11% of the agricultural sub-sector in 2018. The total number of animals was 44.3 million, an increase of 3.6% compared to 2017.
At the same time, the director of the Department of Animal Production instructed all participants to present the goals of animal husbandry to be successful, there are two main points, including:
* First: For successful animal husbandry, three technical principles must be followed: breed, feed and care (biological cage, safety, vaccines, breeding ...) * Second: For successful animal husbandry, care must be taken. The other three important factors are to have a clear feeding plan, understand the market demand and study the economic efficiency.
