Mr. HUN Manet: Choosing the right leader makes the country prosperous, but choosing the wrong leader divides the country
(Takeo): Mr. Hun Manet said that choosing the right leader does not incite division, make the country prosperous, provide mental and physical well-being to the people, but choosing the wrong leader divides the nation.
This statement was made on the occasion that Mr. HUN Manet, Representative of Samdech Techo HUN SEN and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the Assembly Hall and achievements in Wat Thomchar (called Wat Cheung Koun) in Cheung Koun Village. Cheung Koun commune, Samrong district, Takeo province, this weekend.
Mr. Hun Manet said that the people elect their leaders to vote for themselves to provide peace, maintain peace and develop the country for the future of future generations. I would like to thank the people who voted for Samdech Techo Hun Sen to encourage and encourage him to continue to lead the country.
At the same time, Mr. HUN Manet said that many achievements in Takeo province were built for the people in Takeo province, all of which were achieved by the joint construction of the monks, the committee, the pagoda, the Buddhists, the philanthropists.
He said that if we did not have war, we would have built more, but unfortunately we have had destructive wars in all areas. We are very proud that we have ended the war and the greatest pride is the spirit of the Cambodian people, no matter how difficult it is, to work together to build achievements.
Mr. HUN Manet would like to express his gratitude and ask for the generosity of the monks, the committee, the abbot, the pagoda, the Buddhists, the people to continue to build achievements in a peaceful national environment. Build achievements for all and help each other maintain stability, happiness and respect each other.
