The LJ-I drone appeared at the International Fighter Aircraft Show in Zhukovsky, near Moscow, last week. The drone is rated by Chinese military experts as highly capable of long-range flight and is equipped with an electromagnetic weapon system.
The LJ-I drone also has similar capabilities to fourth- or fifth-generation fighter jets. But the drone demonstration comes as the United States and its allies such as South Korea, Japan and Australia step up purchases and deploy of F-35 fighter jets to curb growing Chinese military influence in the region. .
