Ministry of Commerce and Foreign Trade Organization of Japan Sign a Memorandum of Understanding to Expand Economic-Trade Relations and Attract Japanese Investors
Speaking at the Memorandum of Understanding, Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak thanked the Japanese government and people for their care and assistance to the Cambodian people.
He stressed that the MoU will further strengthen cooperation in the fields of trade promotion, investment and industrial development in order to establish a comprehensive partnership between the Ministry of Commerce and JETRO.
The Minister also noted some of the activities that JETRO has implemented in Cambodia, including business matching, study, analysis, participation in local trade fairs, facilitation of issues for Japanese companies, training of officials and the private sector, and assistance. To Cambodian companies participating in the Japan Expo.
He praised that JETRO's efforts to gather factual information from the Cambodian market have given Aeon the confidence to invest in supermarkets in Cambodia, and the establishment of Aeon Mall has brought with it good standards such as standards. Sanitation is used in the Cambodian market, which is an added value of this investment as well.
In response, Dr. Yuri Sato thanked the Minister for his appreciation.
She praised the Ministry of Commerce's cooperation and coordination on Japanese business. She also noted some of the reforms that the Royal Government of Cambodia has put in place and implemented to facilitate business and trade, which are positive signs that she will bring to the fore.
Please note that the Memorandum of Understanding signed now is an update to the Memorandum of Understanding signed by the Ministry of Commerce and JETRO on December 14, 2009. Cooperation between the two institutions has contributed to the growth of trade volume between Cambodia and Japan, which in 2009 was small and in 2018 reached about 1.6 billion US dollars.
