(Kandal): The groundbreaking ceremony of a water supply station in Svay Ampear commune, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province of the Cambodian Poverty Alleviation Pilot Project under the cooperation financing of the People's Republic of China was held this morning. This year 2019 is chaired by Mr. In Chantha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development.
Speaking at the ceremony, Mr. In Chantha stated that through the construction of this water supply station will be able to complement the rural development work on water supply for use, especially to reduce the cost of the people in Svay Ampear district. Top of Kandal province.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development requested the Department of Rural Economic Development, Department of Rural Development of Kandal Province and all relevant working groups to continue to cooperate and facilitate this work to ensure the successful construction of this water supply station.
On that occasion, Mr. In Chantha also mentioned that the Ministry of Rural Development has recently revised the five-year Strategic Plan for Rural Development, 2019-2023, to make the program of the Ministry more consistent with the program of the Royal Government in the legislature. This sixth as well. The five-year Strategic Plan for Rural Development includes:
Program 1: Institutional capacity building and human resource development Program 2: Continue to build, maintain and maintain rural infrastructure, physical public services, Program 3: Improve the health, education and living conditions of rural people 4: Job creation, entrepreneurship and rural economic development.
Through these four programs, he strongly hopes that the Ministry of Rural Development will contribute more strongly to the Royal Government of Cambodia in reducing rural poverty, especially to create socio-economic opportunities, promote economic growth and improve livelihoods. Of the people in rural areas for the better.
Tan Hui Pheng, deputy director general of the China International Poverty Alleviation Center, said the project would address the issue of water safety, which is a nuisance. The team will work hard to implement this project to build this project better to ensure the quality of construction.
He also hopes that the villagers will continue to support and support the work of the team by using and maintaining the infrastructure built to achieve the use of all types of infrastructure in a sustainable and long-lasting.
