Kan Ben Pchum Ben is an important Buddhist festival celebrated by all Cambodian Buddhists every year. This festival is held to dedicate merit to the souls of all the meritorious people who have passed away to the next world.
On the other hand, it is also an opportunity for parents, relatives and friends who live in different places to find out about their well-being and progress in their daily lives and increase their solidarity. This year, the Kan Ben Pchum Ben festival will take place from Saturday 1 Roach to Saturday 15 Roch Khep, corresponding to 14 to 28 September 2019.
In particular, the Kathina Festival is a precious festival in Buddhism, which occurs only once a year and lasts for 29 days, with a pagoda receiving only one Kathina Festival, which is a very auspicious gift for grandparents and devotees. This year, the Kathina Festival will take place from Monday, November 1 to November 11, 2019.
