Mekong River floods begin to flood people's villages, Mr. Kun Kim ordered the authorities to strengthen the spirit to help people
(Phnom Penh): Some villages of the people along the Mekong River in Stung Treng and Kratie provinces have been waiting for flooding after the water level along the Mekong River rose in recent days.
The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has announced that the water level in the Mekong River has risen sharply beyond the alarming level due to the effects of the low pressure system combined with the effects of the 14th typhoon KAJIKI and the effects of the southwest monsoon. This effect has caused heavy rains in some provinces of Cambodia and in the catchment area of the Mekong River in Vietnam, Thailand and Laos.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, said that the Mekong River floods had inundated some areas in Stung Treng and Kratie provinces. In particular, Tbong Khmum and Kampong Cham provinces have not been flooded yet.
According to Kun Kim, the level of flooding in Stung Treng is still low and has not yet reached the evacuation of people or livestock. In Kratie province, flooding in Bos Leav commune, Chit Borei district affected about 1,986 families and more than 2,000 livestock. Nearly a thousand cattle and more than 100 people have already been evacuated to safety and will continue to evacuate if the water continues to rise.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, accompanied by officials of the National Committee for Disaster Management, on September 4, 2019, visited the flooded area in Kratie province to check the actual situation and manage the rescue and then went to the province. Tbong Khmum and Kampong Cham also to check the threat of villagers from the flooding of the Mekong River.
With a visit to the flood-hit provinces along the Mekong River, Senior Minister Kun Kim urged authorities and law enforcement forces in the flood-hit provinces to pay close attention to the floods. Rescuers evacuate people as well as livestock to safety.
"By direct order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia and chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, I have traveled to all provinces affected by the Mekong River floods. Today, I went to Kratie, Tbong Khmum and Kampong Cham to check the impact and transport measures to save people to safety. Mr. Kun Kim confirmed that.
Mr. Kun Kim claimed that so far, the National Committee for Disaster Management, both national and sub-national level, has cooperated to be ready to carry out operations to help people from the floods.
Senior Minister Kun Kim also called on the authorities and law enforcement forces in the provinces threatened by the floods to increase their awareness of the need to rescue people. The Senior Minister stated that it is necessary to strictly implement the orders and spirit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, not to leave any citizen to suffer without the help of the authorities.
Phnom Penh Military sends woman to court after arrest in theft
(Phnom Penh): The specialized police force of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie this morning, September 4, 2019, sent a woman to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal punishment under arrest in connection with a theft case.
Please be informed that on August 29, 2019, the competent authorities of the Criminal Investigation Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie arrested a female suspect named Tin Sopha, 48 years old, a domestic worker, after being sued by her landlord. For stealing (hul, phamoung, rags and shirts, cut skirts) several times at 138BIS, Chrey Chisak village, Sangkat Choam Chao, Khan Por Sen Chey.
After being detained and interrogated by Phnom Penh Military Police, the suspect confessed that he and his 18-year-old daughter, Srey Nich, had come to work as housekeepers and cleaners for the landlord at the above point, earning 200 riel. Dollars a month, and every day he and his daughter clean the locker room, the bedroom every day, the owner leaves the room key to open the door and then return the keys to the owner.
After the interrogation, the competent authorities of the Criminal Investigation Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie prepared a case file and sent the above suspects to court to be punished according to the law on the morning of September 4, 2019.
