Researchers are shocked by the rapid melting of glaciers on Greenland, and they are also worried about the future of cities along the coast around the world. During 2019, Greenland lost enough ice to raise sea levels by more than a millimeter globally.
The Greenland Glacier covers about 80 percent of the island's total area of more than 2 million square kilometers, about the size of Saudi Arabia's oil-rich country and is the second largest glacier in the world. World after Antarctica and 2-3 km thick.
If all the glaciers on Greenland melt once, it could raise sea levels around the world to 7 meters. Although this will not happen for hundreds or thousands of years, rising Greenland ice sheets over the next few decades could pose a threat to the millions living in the city. Located along the coast, especially cities below sea level.
