The United States, Britain and France, as well as a number of Western countries, may be responsible for war crimes in Yemen due to a series of attacks, UN investigators said in a report released on Tuesday. Help or support the Saudi-led coalition against the Iranian-backed Houthi rebels.
In addition, according to UN experts, the parties to the conflict in Yemen are all involved in acts of violence and impunity, especially those involving airstrikes on civilians, torture and sexual abuse. And obstructing or hindering UN humanitarian assistance to the people of Yemen.
According to the United Nations, the four-year war in Yemen has killed 7,290 civilians and left 80 percent of Yemen's 24 million people in a serious humanitarian crisis. Of that, 10 million people depend on humanitarian aid.
47 Houses Donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to Veterans
(Kratie): 47 houses donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen were handed over to the families of poor veterans in Sambour Sen Chey village. Svay Chres Commune, Snoul District, Kratie Province.
The handover ceremony on the morning of September 4, 2019 was presided over by Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, with the participation of the governors of Tbong Khmum, Kampong Cham and Kratie provinces. Separately, 38 families of veterans who received this house came from Tbong Khmum province and 9 families from Kampong Cham province.
According to the report, the veterans are poor and have volunteered to live in Sambour Sen Chey village, Svay Chreah commune, Snuol district, Kratie province. So far, they have received 114 houses donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit. There are 42 in Kratie, 34 in Kampong Cham and 38 in Tbong Khmum.
In addition, Senior Minister Kun Kim also reminded all veterans to participate in the implementation of the commune safety policy by volunteering as a reporting agency to the commune administration to provide information on irregularities and crimes. Other in the local area for the authorities to effectively suppress the commune to ensure security and good order.
In addition to handing over the houses, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also recommended the installation of electricity in each house, and on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the provincial governor and the president of the three provincial Veterans Association paid the cost. Lighting and lighting bulbs for the 114 siblings to help make bathrooms for every home.
On that occasion, the 47 families of veterans also received 50 kg of rice, some food items and 100,000 Riels, as well as 124 veterans who participated in this ceremony, 50,000 Riels each and the Governor of Kampong Cham helped dig a well. Two of them were given to Mr. San Sai for the blind to facilitate living and the other for common use in the village. Separately, Tbong Khmum Veterans Association also organized a solidarity meal.
Under the guidance of Senior Minister Kun Kim, the governor of Snuol district promised to help clear the road in Choun village and instructed the three provincial veterans' associations to continue to search for those who are really difficult to respect and ask Samdech to build a house for them.
At the same time, the veterans who received the house donated by Samdech said with a smile that they were very excited when they were struggling to be given a house by Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit and sent to Minister Kun Kim. Personally, I wish both Samdech and his family good health and good luck to continue to lead the Cambodian ship.
(Preah Vihear): The low pressure system and the effects of the 14th typhoon Kazikiki are affecting Cambodia, leading to heavy rains in many areas, especially in the Dangrek mountain range, causing floods, affecting people's homes and Many infrastructure systems.
In fact, in Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province, heavy rains are flooding, causing some roads to be flooded and damaged. According to the authorities, a child, including a motorcycle, was swept away by the whirlpool and no body has been found so far.
The district governor also confirmed that the floodwaters also swept away a child and a motorbike belonging to the residents, who to date have not yet found the bodies, and the authorities and the Red Cross have donated to relatives. Victims, too.
In Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province, the floods also affected people's homes and infrastructure.
Speaking to Fresh News, Anlong Veng District Governor Hor Chin Virakyuth confirmed that heavy rains fell in Anlong Veng district last night, causing the water level to rise sharply, causing flooding in Ta Mok district. Anlong Veng increased to the point of emergency and also affected the inability to travel from the district town to Char Rohal village, Lum Tong commune in 7 places and the red gravel road was completely destroyed.
The governor of Anlong Veng district confirmed that the flood occurred this morning due to heavy rain on the mountain in Trapeang Prasat district last night, and according to the flow of the flood. Extreme levels of flood danger were announced in 2017.
