Murder! A widow was brutally murdered in Baray district, Kampong Thom province, the perpetrator and her son-in-law were arrested
(Kampong Thom): A widow was killed by an unknown assailant and then escaped. The brutal murder was found dead on the roof of his house at 6 am on September 4, 2019 in Trapeang Chrey village, Balang commune, Baray district, Kampong Thom province.
According to the local police, the victim, 51-year-old Doul Kheang, who sells noodles at the stall in front of her house, lives in the commune where the incident took place.
According to Kuy Kit, the victim's eldest daughter, her mother had four daughters, all widows, and all three of them migrated to work in Thailand. Today, the mother lives with her two young grandchildren, who are orphans, and sells noodles at the front of the house every morning.
According to the neighbors, the victim was a good person and never had any conflicts with others. Every day, he always sells noodles in front of the house, but in the morning, the victim is not seen coming down to sell noodles and see her 6-year-old granddaughter sitting crying in the doorway.
At that time, he ran to interrogate, and when he arrived at the house, he found his mother dead in a pool of blood, and immediately reported to the authorities for examination and forensic examination. After the competent experts have examined and forensically concluded that it is a case of murder.
