Mr. Toch Chao Koy added that for gas stations selling poor quality and not enough liters, professional officials made an education contract to change later. If the second check finds that "any station continues to sell less than a liter of gasoline or poor quality, we will take legal action on the management of goods and services by imposing fines in accordance with the law."
Mr. President of CamControl Pursat Branch also called on all station owners and depots to sell all liters of good quality to serve the public economy and give trust from consumers.
