(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, in collaboration with the Documentation Center of Cambodia, has been conducting scientific research for the past four years on the topic of "genocide and massacres in world history" for knowledge. More to all readers, researchers, teachers and students related to national history, regional history and world history.
The history of the massacre has had a devastating effect on the nation's development. This research work is also a research obligation conducted in response to the decision of the Royal Government of Cambodia regarding the preparation of compensation plans for Civil Parties and victims of the Khmer Rouge genocide in Case 002 of the Trial Chamber. Extraordinary hearing in the courts of Cambodia, or as we call it, the tribunal to try Khmer Rouge leaders.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has agreed to compile a document on the history of the Khmer Rouge and to include this book as part of the general education curriculum from grades 7 to 12 and at the basic level of the higher education curriculum. Decision of S.C.N. No. 1134 of the Royal Government was made on June 11, 2013.
Composing, reviewing, printing and distributing books
This book was discussed with 50 Cambodian higher education professors who participated in a three-day workshop on teaching the history of Democratic Kampuchea, held in April 2019, organized by the Documentation Center of Cambodia and Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
DC-Cam publishes this book in two languages, English and Khmer, and plans to distribute it to teachers and students in some high schools in December 2019 for use as an important reference in learning and teaching. History of Democratic Kampuchea and world history. The book in Khmer was edited and edited by Pheng Pongrasy and Sopheak Phana.
About books and book creation philosophy
