On the inside pages of this book, before entering into a discussion of the historical context of each country, there is a preface to a page by Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, describing the main and effective roles and responsibilities in the field of education. In contributing to the prevention of all elements that lead to the occurrence of genocide and massacre in society.
Similarly, in the preface of Mr. Youk Chhang, Director of the Documentation Center of Cambodia and the Founder of the Leaf Institute, written on the next page, he emphasized the power of education as a great force for future social transformation and power. The greatness of mankind in achieving peace, freedom and justice.
In addition, the director's foreword also reveals a number of tips and solutions to prevent genocide, massacre and other forms of violence. At the grassroots level, participation in global strategies to prevent those crimes is an indispensable task.
Philosophy of Book Making
The four authors of this book intend to show the world how the genocide and genocide took place, which were similar and different depending on the historical context, political situation, culture, religion, nation. Genetics and identities of people living in different environments.
Support from the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, praised this work and agreed to the educational mission to promote a deeper understanding of history through reflection and commitment. In-depth study of historical events taking place in the world.
Ros Sowacha, spokesman for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, stated that "70% of the Cambodian people living today have never been through genocide. "So the study of genocide in Cambodia and around the world will help them understand history and serve as a basis for intergenerational dialogue."
