The following is the directive of Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Samdech Picheay Sena discussed with the National Assembly Expert Committee on the draft law on the approval of the agreement between Cambodia and the Organization for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons.
Samdech Pich Sena said that Cambodia has benefited from this agreement, such as cooperation with the Organization for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons and technical assistance and capacity development.
Mr. Hun Neng stated that after Samdech Picheay Sena and his colleagues commented on the points raised by the National Assembly Expert Committee, the National Assembly Expert Committee expressed its support for the draft law and decided to send it. The draft law is submitted to the National Assembly Standing Committee for further review by the National Assembly.
The National Authority for Chemical Weapons of Cambodia has established good relations, smooth and effective cooperation with the Organization for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons in the study, analysis and purpose of each article set out in this Agreement without affecting the Basic Law. Politics and national interests.
So far, 193 countries are partners with the Organization for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons. Fifty-six countries have signed the agreement, of which 55 have signed but ratified by 41. In ASEAN, the five countries that have signed the agreement are Cambodia, Laos, the Philippines, Thailand and Vietnam.
The Draft Law on the Approval of the Agreement between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Organization for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons on the Privileges and Immunities of the Organization for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons was approved by the Council of Ministers on August 2, 2019. And sent for permission from the legislature, which consists of three articles.
