Hong Kong activists urge Taiwan to join pro-democracy protests in Hong Kong
Tens of thousands of people have taken to the streets in Hong Kong since mid-June 2019.
Hong Kong, a former British colony, returned to Chinese rule in 1997 under a "one country, two systems" formula that guaranteed its independence. China has also proposed the same formula for Taiwan, which considers Taiwan an isolated province and difficult to control.
The Chinese government has accused Taiwan's Taipei administration of backing the protests in Hong Kong. The allegations were denied by Taiwan.
Hong Kong pro-democracy lawmaker Eddie Chu has urged Taiwanese authorities to stand up with humanitarian mechanisms to protest from Taipei after hundreds of people were arrested since the protests began.
