BEIJING: Eight schoolchildren were killed in an attack outside a primary school in China on the first day of school. This is according to the Chinese police quoted by the BBC on Tuesday, September 3, 2019.
A 40-year-old man was arrested at the scene in central China's Hubei Province, police said. But at the same time, they did not specify how the victim was killed or the real motive behind the attack, only that it was known that all the students were between 6 to 13 years.
(Phnom Penh): By 2019, Cambodia has received a loan for the construction of road and bridge infrastructure from China about 2.865 million US dollars. The money was spent on the construction of 29 roads, equivalent to 2,888 km, and the construction of eight bridges with a length of 8 km.
Loans for road and bridge construction in Cambodia are not limited to China, Japan, South Korea, development partners, the World Bank, the Asian Development Bank and some other countries. But China is the largest lender for road and bridge construction.
Because China is the largest lender for the construction of roads and bridges, this raises the question of why Cambodia borrows more money from China for the construction of roads and bridges than other countries.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, asserted that Cambodia did not discriminate against loans for the construction of roads and bridges, but that the reason for Cambodia borrowing a lot from China was because Cambodia had good relations with China. Lending procedures are quick and uncomplicated.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also revealed that in some countries, the procedure for borrowing money to build roads is slow, sometimes taking up to five years. The slow procedure in lending is also slowing down Cambodia's development in the infrastructure sector.
According to Mr. Sun Chanthol, because the Chinese lending procedures are quick to meet the needs of road and bridge development in Cambodia, China has become the largest lender for road and bridge construction in Cambodia.
