Wage Discussion: Unions and employers have not yet released figures but are gathering information seeking consensus
(Phnom Penh): Regarding the second meeting of the National Minimum Wage Council held at the Ministry of Labor on September 3, the unions and employers have not yet released figures, but all parties are collecting data and Separate information to serve as a basis for discussion, find a consensus mechanism (consensus) that will be discussed this weekend.
After the meeting, Mr. Heng Sour, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, said that today's meeting was transformed into a tripartite meeting of each party from now until the 6th. She is coming and all parties will meet again to discuss and find a mechanism to reach a point that is acceptable to all parties.
Heng Sour confirmed that through this morning's meeting, although the union and employers have not yet released any figures, but all parties seem to be aware of local trends as well as some criteria.
He said that at this time, they are surveying to find an internal agreement first to present to the other side. That is why the National Minimum Wage Council decides to leave the possibility or time for each party to decide internally through pre-negotiation to make the other party acceptable.
He claimed that at today's meeting, the two sides had a positive correspondence, focusing on the figures and the impact of each rule change rather than the correspondence between the workers 'side and the employers' side.
Ministry of Tourism unveils six points of memorandum of understanding with Malaysia
(Phnom Penh): After the Minister of Tourism of Cambodia, Mr. Thong Khon, and the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Malaysia, Mr. Sai Foudin Abdullah, signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Tourism Cooperation, the Ministry of Tourism presented six points in the memorandum. This is necessary for the development of tourism.
The MoUs focus on: * Research and development. * Human resource training. * Dissemination and propaganda. * Workshops, meetings, conferences and exhibitions, tourism, trade fairs. Professional officers. * Promoting other economic activities through tourism.
The signing ceremony was held on the morning of September 3, 2019 at the Peace Palace under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Mahathir Mohamad, Prime Minister of Malaysia.
In the first six months of 2019, Cambodia received more than 3.3 million international tourists, an increase of 11.2%, of which more than 90,000 Malaysian tourists, an increase of 7%.
