Timor-Leste has been seeking ASEAN membership for many years. Cambodia, one of the ASEAN member countries, has also made great efforts to help Timor-Leste become a member of ASEAN.
Cambodian leader Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who had a difficult history when Cambodia applied for ASEAN membership, expressed his willingness to help Timor-Leste. Samdech Techo Hun Sen once said that only countries that have experienced the same difficulties understand Timor-Leste's difficulties. Samdech Techo Hun Sen has also confirmed that Cambodia has sent officials to study the situation in Timor-Leste.
Speaking in a statement after the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that in the meeting with Mahathir, the case of Timor-Leste was discussed and it was agreed that Timor-Leste should be allowed to become the 11th member of the ASEAN.
Mr. Mahathea also confirmed this case. "Timor-Leste, which has long applied for ASEAN membership, should definitely become an ASEAN member and we will try to ensure that Timor-Leste becomes a member of ASEAN," he said. At the upcoming summit in the ASEAN Leaders' Meeting.
The Association of Southeast Asian Nations was established on August 8, 1967. Initially, there were five countries: Malaysia, Indonesia, the Philippines, Singapore and Thailand. After 1984, five more countries in the region joined: Brunei, Vietnam, Laos, Myanmar and Cambodia on April 30, 1999.
Today, ASEAN is playing an important role in discussing various issues both regionally and globally. ASEAN has a total population of over 600 million.
