(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, and the Prime Minister of Malaysia, Mahathir Mohamad, consider that the superpower's sanctions on small countries are extremely unfair because they do not only affect To a country, that is, to affect a trading partner.
The same assertion between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Mahathir Mohamad was made this morning, September 3, 2019, during a working meeting at the Peace Palace on the occasion of the Prime Minister of Malaysia's visit to Cambodia. 3 days from September 2 to 4, 2019.
"This is very unfair because small countries can not impose sanctions on any country, but only superpowers can impose sanctions on them and put pressure on small countries not to be free," he said. "We are talking about human rights, about freedom. They take our rights and freedoms by putting them on this trading partner, which is very unfair."
Mahathir Mohamad stressed that the sanctions affect not only the countries directly affected but also other countries that do not have a conflict with the country but are banned from doing business with that country. Because of that punishment.
Similarly, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, also highlighted the UN Security Council sanctions on North Korea. Samdech considers that it really affects the trading partners and countries that suffer from sanctions.
