(Siem Reap): Tonle Snguot Temple is an ancient hospital built during the reign of King Jayavarman VII in the late 12th and early 13th centuries. Cut down the trees that grow on the temple and the process of removing the stones of the dry river to preserve and repair and strengthen.
According to Mr. Chea Sarith, director of the Tonle Sap Dry Rehabilitation Site and an archaeologist at the Department of Temple Preservation in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology, the temple is in a state of disrepair due to water, plants, quality of materials and age of construction. The foundation stone is crumbling and the body of the temple is very tilted. The stone wall is moving from the original position.
