According to a joint statement issued by the two countries, the two leaders expressed satisfaction over the closer friendship and cooperation between Cambodia and Malaysia in all areas, including trade and investment. "Investment, halal industry development, defense and security, tourism, agriculture and education."
The two leaders stressed the importance of continuing to strengthen and expand cooperation and cooperation within the bilateral, regional and multilateral frameworks to serve the interests of the two peoples and to contribute to peace, stability and prosperity. In the whole region. This is according to the joint statement.
For trade volume between the two countries has increased significantly in recent years. A report by the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia shows that in 2017, the two countries' trade volume was more than 411 million US dollars, Cambodia exported nearly 148 million US dollars to Malaysia and imported 464 million US dollars from Malaysia.
In 2018, the total trade volume will be more than 474 million dollars. Of that, Cambodia exported more than $ 130 million to Malaysia and imported more than $ 344 million from Malaysia. In the first six months of 2019, the trade volume was over $ 400 million, of which Cambodia exported more than $ 60 million to Malaysia and imports from Malaysia amounted to nearly $ 340 million.
