The 73 ASEAN students are SCG "Sharing Dreams" scholarship students from Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Myanmar, the Philippines, Thailand and Vietnam. They are a network of ASEAN youth who care about the environment and want to contribute to building a sustainable future.
The students raised environmental issues in ASEAN with participants in the conference, which included business leaders, government officials, intergovernmental representatives and UN representatives at the annual conference on sustainable development organized by SCG. Which is one of the leading cement companies in ASEAN.
Students from Cambodia have expressed concern about the problem of plastic waste in Cambodia and called for sustainable development. Students from Laos raised the issue of deepening water depths in the Mekong River, which they claimed was caused by deforestation. Meanwhile, students from Vietnam expressed concern over the growing hot weather in Ho Chi Minh City.
These environmental concerns were shared by ASEAN students to nearly 2,000 participants at the Sustainable Development Conference, which also marks the 10th anniversary of the event.
