The device is about the size of a bank card and about the same thickness, but it may save the lives of victims trapped under rubble after earthquakes, as Indonesia often suffers from natural disasters.
A group of three students from the University of Brawijaya have already received patents for their innovative device, which costs $ 7. But the three students stated that they wanted to develop it perfectly before considering going public, while a senior official at the Indonesian Ministry of Education was also interested in helping develop their equipment.
