Malaysian PM: Cambodia has an older culture than the United States, democracy must not follow US rules
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Malaysia, Mahathir Mohamad, said that Cambodia is a country with a culture and civilization older than the United States, so must choose the country's leadership process according to the circumstances in accordance with its culture, civilization, traditions and customs. Yes, to follow any form of democracy, command, or desire of the United States.
Mr. Mahathea's remarks in response to questions from Cambodian students during a lecture on "Balancing relations with superpowers in the ASEAN context" organized by the Royal University of Phnom Penh on the afternoon of September 2, 2019. A student asked Mahathir in the context of Cambodia, "Do we have to read American democracy?"
Answering this question, the Prime Minister of Malaysia pointed out that each country has a different culture, civilization, values, customs and ideas. He said that Cambodia is a country with a much older culture and civilization compared to the United States.
In this sense, Mahathir Mohamad encourages Cambodia to follow its own path, adapting to the circumstances, without relying on the need to follow American-style democracy or American aspirations.
In that lecture, Mr. Mahathea also reminded Cambodian students to study hard to find out what is happening and to avoid bad things such as drugs. The prime minister also warned young people who could become leaders to avoid the use of weapons and war to resolve issues, using diplomacy and dialogue to resolve issues.
Mahathir Mohamad's remarks were made in a lecture on "Balancing relations with superpowers in the ASEAN context" organized by the Royal University of Phnom Penh on the afternoon of September 2, 2019.
