A female hairdresser was injured in several incidents when her former owner, Chan Salon, used nail clippers to stab her several times when they were arguing. . The incident happened at 11:20 AM on August 28, 2019 in the "Chan Salon" beauty salon near Vin Ming Market, Trapeang Thleung 2 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao 1, Khan Por Sen Chey.
The victim was identified as 18-year-old Chantha, who suffered injuries to her abdomen, chest, throat and bleeding head. She is currently living in the village where the incident took place. A 36-year-old female was injured in one hand. After the incident, the villagers informed the police at Chaom Chao 1 police station to intervene, and the police force went to arrest the two men at the police station for questioning because there were injuries on both sides.
According to a witness, before the incident, the owner of the shop called the victim into his shop, then she entered, but after a while, the owner pushed the victim out and slapped him. As well as stabbing the victim in the head and throat. He then stabbed her in the chest, but was kicked in the leg by the victim, who then stabbed her and ran away, shouting for help.
The owner of the barber shop said that she fired her victim in the past because she was dishonest and always said she was scared and useless. As well as chatting on her phone and niece's phone and mocking everything even more can not stand.
Local police officials confirmed that the shop owner had caused violence to the victim and even sued for $ 15,000.
