(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, has decided to set up a special road inspection team to inspect the quality of roads under construction to further improve the quality of road construction.
The quality of road construction in Cambodia is an issue that people often raise and often criticize the construction that is not done well, done in front and back damaged.
Mr. Sun Chanthol explained the procedure of road construction that all road construction projects that receive assistance or loans from countries and friendly partner organizations, all the selection of construction companies and technical inspection companies are countries or organizations that provide assistance and loans. Do it yourself. Separately, the Ministry has also assigned technical officers to monitor and control the technology as well as the quality of construction.
After construction, before handing over to the Royal Government, the Ministry must check the quality again before deciding whether to accept or not. Senior Minister Sun Chanthol always inspected the road in detail, sometimes using bicycles, and when driving and checking.
The use of this means in order to ensure that the roads constructed are of the correct quality according to the techniques and agreements. Recently, Mr. Sun Chanthol decided to remove six road technical inspectors after he found that the roads they inspected were of poor quality and had been built incorrectly.
Mr. Sun Chanthol reminded both the construction company, the technical inspection company and the technical inspector: "Building and damaging the road is a waste of time." "It causes accidents and traffic jams, and hurts the people."
Mr. Sun Chanthol claimed that in order to improve the quality of road construction, he decided to set up a special road technical inspection team, a company that raided the road to inspect the quality of the road and report directly to him.
In an interview with Fresh News, while presenting measures to improve the quality of road construction, Mr. Sun Chanthol also confirmed the type of road built in Cambodia. The presentation of the types of roads built in Cambodia answers the question as well as some of the people who see that some roads are thin and some roads are thick.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also stated the reasons why Cambodia chose to build DBST level roads. Mr. Sun Chanthol pointed out that the reason why Cambodia chose to build DBST level roads is to integrate roads from the provinces with Phnom Penh. Until now, as the traffic level has become busier, Cambodia has started to decide to expand the quality of some roads to the AC level, which has thicker tires and lasts longer than DBST.
The minister claimed that if Cambodia chooses to build roads with good AC connectivity, it will not be able to connect, and in economic terms it will not be very profitable because the roads in the provinces are not busy yet. Every purchase of Borey Lonni Villa in September 2019 will receive many special offers.
Tbong Khmum Deputy Governor Asks Government Officials, Relevant Units and People Across the Province to Take Care of Forest Protection and Plant More Trees
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Peang Narith, Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, requested government officials, armed forces at all levels, relevant units and people throughout Tbong Khmum to participate in the maintenance of forest protection and replanting trees. .
This request was made on the occasion of Mr. Peang Narith presiding over the distribution of study materials to 322 students and planting 200 luxury trees at Teuk Chrov Secondary School in Khlai Village, Teuk Chrov Commune. Tbong Khmum Province under the theme "A Tree of Life" organized by the Alumni Association of Cambodia on September 1, 2019.
On that occasion, the Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum requested civil servants, armed forces at all levels, relevant units and people throughout Tbong Khmum to participate in the spirit of forest protection and replanting more trees because That:
* Forests are natural resources that are important not only for sustaining human and animal life, but also to provide greenery, beautification, and many other great benefits for business, accommodation, tourism, recreation, and coolness for humans and animals. And inheritance is also valuable for future generations.
* Forests provide the balance of the natural environment and the stability of our planet.
* Forests help prevent climate change, greatly reducing natural disasters such as droughts, floods, erosion, global warming, and global warming.
At the same time, Mr. Peang Narith continued that in order to continue the movement of planting trees and maintaining natural resources to be greener and more beautiful everywhere in Tbong Khmum province, he would like to provide some guidance as follows:
1: Local authorities, officials, units continue to mobilize the masses to participate in planting luxury trees, fruit trees, flowers for everyone everywhere, such as in pagodas, schools, communities, streets, homes, public places at least one. Get one tree a year.
2. The Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries shall arrange for a large number of all kinds of luxury nurseries to be prepared for distribution to the people or the units to plant trees in public places.
3. Take appropriate measures to prevent and suppress all deforestation, forest fires and deforestation by ensuring effective law enforcement.
4: Increase education for people through programs that show the importance of managing and protecting sustainable forest resources.
5. We should unite to prevent anarchic activities in the forestry sector, promote both technology and the spirit of the community to be strong for the benefit of the people who depend on non-timber forest products through the strict implementation of the law. Forest.
