Samdech Techo Hun Sen Welcomes Malaysian PM to Visit Cambodia
Mr. Mahathir Mohamad and his wife arrived in Cambodia at around 9:40 am on September 2, 2019 for a three-day official visit from September 2 to 4, 2019. 2019. The visit of the oldest Prime Minister in the world was made at the invitation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, during the visit, the Prime Minister of Malaysia will pay a separate courtesy call on Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Acting Head of State of Cambodia and Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly.
Mahathir Mohamad will hold a bilateral meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen to discuss various aspects of bilateral cooperation. The two Prime Ministers will also exchange views on regional and international issues of common interest. The two prime ministers will then preside over the signing ceremony of a number of documents and make a joint statement.
During his stay in Phnom Penh, the Prime Minister of Malaysia will lay a wreath at the Independence Monument and pay his last respects to His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the "King of Cambodia", the former King of Cambodia.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated that the official visit of Dr. Mahathir Mohamad to Cambodia will further contribute to strengthening and deepening the good relations and close cooperation between Cambodia and Malaysia within the framework. Bilateral, regional and international.
After arriving in Cambodia, on the afternoon of August 2, 2019, Mr. Mahathir Mohamad will give a lecture on "Balancing Relations with Great Powers in the ASEAN Context" at the Royal University of Phnom Penh.
At the same time, Huy Yaleng expressed the high expectation that there will be a lot of support from the audience, because unlike usual, now he has carefully selected to make it come out. A new story, a unique life story, education, struggle to please the audience of all ages, all walks of life.
