Clearing forest land in Vern Sai district so far has not yet had the competent authority and the authorities have taken action yet
(Ratanakkiri): Hundreds of hectares of state-owned forest reserves have been cleared in Team Krom village, Phnom Kok commune, Vern Sai district, Ratanakkiri province, a mixed forest and dense forest rich in valuable timber. There are no professional authorities and local authorities to prevent and take action.
According to the information provided by the local people, the above activities were carried out by Heng Dara Company, importing 3 machines (Abol, Escarvator) and some other means. This activity started in 3-4 months until mid-August 2019 and this activity was temporarily suspended due to heavy rain at the end of August.
Sources said that the above activities were considered by some individuals in the Vern Sai district administration, in which Mr. Heng Savoeun, Vern Sai district governor, told reporters that he informed Mr. Thong Savun, the provincial governor and Mr. Bou. Lam, a member of the Ratanakkiri constituency, is already asking for the land to be planted with cashews to supply the district administration.
According to the law, clearing hundreds of hectares of state forest land and using such heavy machinery without a permit from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, so the above activities are illegal. Separate sources have revealed that Heng Dara Company and some individuals in the Vern Sai District Administration have conspired to clear state forest land, grow cashews and resell them (to China) for $ 2,000 per hectare.
Due to these inactive reasons, the activities of land disputes and the clearing of state forests in Vern Sai district have not been cracked down on by the authorities, making the state forest lands shrink from year to year. Therefore, in the above case, there should be a working group to take timely measures to prevent clearing activities and land disputes.
