In order to facilitate the facilities for students and young people who want to study the above skills, International University (IU) and the Cambodian Economic Youth Association have confirmed that they will help facilitate all means for all who want to study.
At the Master Scholarship Awarding Ceremony for Community Health and Rural Development on August 31, 2019 at the Cambodian Economic Youth Association, Mr. Chhim Sauki stated that the good cooperation between the International University (IU) and the Ministry of Development Rural Development in Community Health and Rural Development Skills for Postgraduate Training for Cambodian Students, Civil Servants and Youth.
On that occasion, Mr. Sabo Ozano, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Rector of International University, confirmed that employees in the private sector, civil society organizations and civil servants who do not have a degree and a bachelor's degree from now on can study for a master's degree. On Community Health and Rural Development from International University (IU). By applying for this Master's Scholarship, you must contact the Cambodian Economic Youth Association.
He added that the conditions for admission to the master's degree, private sector employees, civil society organizations or government officials need to have at least 5 years of experience in the work they are currently doing and the study can choose. Yes, study from Monday to Friday from 5:30 am to 8:30 pm and study on Saturdays and Sundays full time.
Mr. Ley Sopheap, Member of the Capital Council and President of the Cambodian Economic Youth Association, said, "This is the first time that the Royal Government has given the green light to the private sector, civil society organizations and civil servants who do not have a bachelor's degree or a bachelor's degree. At least 5 years of work experience can apply for this Master's Scholarship from an international university.
