Watch the music video below: Legal Awareness: Business Registration Topics
(Phnom Penh): According to the Law on Trade Rules and Business Registration of the Ministry of Commerce of the Kingdom of Cambodia, when you want to start a business for profit, you need to register your business at the Ministry of Commerce.
Why does the Royal Government require business registration? Because of business registration, it is very important to show that a business is a legitimate business and is protected by law in the event of a dispute or any problem that may arise.
But this listing also requires a clear financial understanding of each business, or in other words, the cash flow in their business that can earn and profit.
Therefore, business registration in line with the current situation is done to ensure legitimacy, including the name of the company, the type of company as (monopoly, co-ownership, private limited liability company, public limited liability company and company Foreign, etc.…) Your company's products and services.
After the business is registered, your business will receive a certificate as well as protection if the name or product is copied.
Therefore, in order to be clearer this week, the Legal Awareness Program, which is a collaboration between Fresh News and the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation, would like to raise the topic of "Business Registration" to present to all citizens as Below:
However, if it is not possible to fill in the information and enter the requirements in the automated system by yourself, please come to the Ministry of Commerce to request the registration officer to fill in instead (Article 2 of the same Prakas).
As for the conditions for business registration, you have to fill in the file according to the form prescribed by the Ministry, and after completing it, you have to pay the fee to study the registration file.
Once the business registration is complete, you will receive a certificate of your registration. And for business registration in the Kingdom of Cambodia is divided into three:
1: Conditions for Business Registration for Individual Traders
All natural persons who are traders must register their business at the provincial / municipal Department of Commerce or other places designated by the Ministry of Commerce at the place where they do business no later than 15 (fifteen) days before opening. Its business.
In addition, the registration of the commercial register may be made by the person concerned or by his / her jurisdiction, and the juror must have a power of attorney to be kept on the clerk of the commercial court for which he / she has applied for registration.
Not only that, the trader must hand over the signature and fingerprint to the place of application for business registration in two (two) copies (Article 14, paragraph 1, 2, 3 of the Law on Commercial Rules and Commercial Registration). .
2: Conditions for business registration for legal entities
The legal entity that has established a trading company in the Kingdom of Cambodia, regardless of the form of establishment and duration, must register the business and the registration in the business register must be done by the editor or Governor of the company in the month of the establishment of the company and 15 (fifteen) days before the opening date of business operations.
The applicant for registration must submit two (two) copies of the transcript and keep the company's statute to the place of registration of business registration (Article 17, paragraph 1, 2, 3 of the Law on Commercial Rules and Commercial Registration). Karma).
3: Conditions for business registration for foreign legal entities
All foreign trading companies that have only branches or agencies in the Kingdom of Cambodia must complete the business registration form in accordance with Articles 17 and 18 of the Law on Commercial Rules and Business Registration as well as legal entities. (Article 19, paragraph 12 of the Law on Commercial Rules and Commercial Registration).
In short, for traders and companies that have registered a business on their business, they will get a legitimate business and be protected for the name and product of that company, as well as to avoid Loss of benefits caused by crooks falsifying the name or product of the company.
In this case, the business owner can also file a complaint to the Ministry of Commerce to dissolve the business of the crook, but if the actions of the person have caused serious loss of benefits, the affected business owner can file a claim for compensation. The competent court of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
