* History of Cambodia-Malaysia relations:
Cambodia and Malaysia established diplomatic relations on August 31, 1957. But in the face of the crisis of war from 1969 to 1975, the two countries maintained diplomatic ties at the level of the Chargé d'Affaires, residing in Beijing. Cambodia and Malaysia re-established diplomatic relations on December 19, 1991.
For trade volume between the two countries has increased significantly in recent years. A report from the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia shows that in 2017, the trade volume of the two countries was more than 411 million US dollars, Cambodia exported nearly 148 million US dollars to Malaysia and imported 464 million US dollars from Malaysia.
In 2018, the total trade volume will be more than 474 million dollars. Of that, Cambodia exported more than $ 130 million to Malaysia and imported more than $ 344 million from Malaysia.
In the first six months of 2019, the trade volume was over $ 400 million, of which Cambodia exported more than $ 60 million to Malaysia and imports from Malaysia amounted to nearly $ 340 million.
Cambodia's main imports: fuel, hoses and hoses, brake pads and tires, woven fabrics, beverages, and processed foods from flour. Cambodia's main exports: clothing, grain, electric motors, coconut oil and palm oil.
Malaysia ranks first among ASEAN members, importing the most Cambodian rice with a total of 40,861 tonnes in 2018.
