(Phnom Penh): This morning, August 31, 2019, BELTEI School, in collaboration with the General Department of CamControl, organized a "Training on Food Safety and Consumer Protection" program for food vendors in all 21 BELTEI schools.
The training was held at BELTEI International School 18 (Phsar Prek Eang Branch) under the chairmanship of Mr. Ly Bun Chhay, Deputy Director General of BELTEI Group and Branch Manager Mr. Sin Sideth, Head of Laboratory and Trainer Mr. Heng Maly, Branch Manager of CamControl. Phnom Penh.
Mr. Heng Maly said that the key point of food safety is to be properly prepared and segregated and to know how to look at the packaging, such as keeping a good shape, not fake, not bulging, not rusting, not leaking, not smelly and not torn. Checking production and expiration dates, understanding of food chemicals and their health effects.
He said that all vendors in the school must be highly responsible, do not hide the location of the source of food imports are not safe, and the purchase must have a clear invoice or purchase goods that know the correct source and address, easy for authorities to take legal action. .
Mr. Sin Sideth, Director of the Laboratory Department and Trainer of the General Department of CamControl, also presented the impact on food safety to the vendors in the school. At the same time, Mr. Sin Sideth also said that in order to be safe, food requires the participation of all stakeholders.
On that occasion, Mr. Ly Bun Chhay, Deputy Director General of BELTEI Group, expressed his deep gratitude to Mr. Sin Sideth and Mr. Heng Maly for taking the opportunity to explain the food safety at this time.
