Lt. Gen. Heng Vuthy: The pagoda is a repository of cultural rules that express the national identity
(Central): Lt. Gen. Heng Vuthy, Deputy Secretary General of the National Authority for Chemical Weapons, said that the pagoda is a repository of cultural rules that express the national identity.
Lt. Gen. Heng Vuthy added that, however, through Buddhist studies is the basis for: disseminating knowledge, theories, rules and regulations of Buddhism, building the resources of monks, strengthening the understanding of the traditional culture of Buddhism, etc., building morals and virtues. Buddhism.
This statement was made by Lt. Gen. Heng Vuthy on the occasion that he and Ms. Ket Rady presided over the inauguration ceremony of the Buddhist Primary School and its achievements at Wat Mony Botum in Kbal Chroy Village, Kampong Phnom Commune, Leuk Dek District, Kandal Province. August 29, 2019.
He said that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, for 40 years since 1979, which is our second birthday, we have made the country peaceful, the political situation, the people living. Harmonious progress has been made in all fields, especially Buddhism.
Lt. Gen. Heng Vuthy also stated that according to current statistics, 95% of the population is Buddhist, there are 4,985 pagodas and 70,853 monks nationwide.
He said that through Buddhism, we observe that monks have played an important role in contributing to society in the education of young people, young men, women, boys, girls, Buddhists, the general public to do only good deeds, know sin, merit, to practice virtues, morals to leave. Fornication, drunkenness, gambling, avoiding drugs, following in the footsteps of Buddhism forever.
Lt. Gen. Heng Vuthy emphasized that it is true that as a follower of Buddhism, one must constantly obey and learn the Dharma, the Vinaya, which is the precious advice of the Samma Samma Buddha, our Master.
He continued that the main purpose of the Buddha is to want the whole of humanity to live in prosperity and generosity for everyone, so that they and the society can be good, strive to do meritorious deeds, adhere to the four Brahma temples in themselves. .
Lt. Gen. Heng Vuthy and Ms. Ket Rady also donated 12,000 billion Riels for the pagoda's chief priest to organize the festival and support 200 grandparents, each of whom received a piece of white cloth and budget. 5,000 Riels and 200 incentive gifts for each student, 2 books, 2 pens, 5,000 Riels.
