The Ministry of Health issued a press release on the meeting of Minister Mam Bunheng with the Deputy Ministers of Health of China, Japan and Korea.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on August 31, 2019 issued a press release on the meeting between Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, with Deputy Minister of National Health Committee of the People's Republic of China, Deputy Minister of Health of Japan and Deputy Minister of Health. Minister of Health of the Republic of Korea
According to a press release issued on the afternoon of August 30, 2019, the two sides discussed cooperation in the fight against malaria, including strengthening the capacity of laboratories, training of human resources, and preventing the spread of malaria. Medicines and strengthening malaria surveillance system in Stung Treng province.
In addition, the two sides will continue to cooperate in the field of cardiovascular disease, especially pediatric open heart surgery, the integration of this cardiology in the construction of the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital in Preah Kosomak. Continue to support the ophthalmology surgery as well.
In particular, in the meeting with the Deputy Minister of Health of Japan, Wen focused on the training of midwives, nurses, maternal and child health care programs and the construction of health infrastructure, as currently through JICA is implementing a project to improve Battambang Provincial Hospital. This includes the construction of hospital buildings, the installation of medical equipment and facilities.
The meeting with the Deputy Minister of Health of the Republic of Korea also focused on capacity building cooperation between health officials and health facilities in Battambang, Pursat and Pailin provinces. In addition, the Korean side has provided grants such as the construction of the vision building of Ang Duong Hospital and is expanding further.
