(Preah Vihear): Brigadier General Kang Sao Kun, Commander of the Preah Vihear Provincial Gendarmerie, has ordered the Provincial Gendarmerie to continue to pay attention to the suppression of natural resource crimes and to be ready to rescue people at any time. Various disasters.
The Commander-in-Chief chaired a meeting to review the implementation of the duties and responsibilities of the Royal Gendarmerie in August and to raise the work direction for September 2019 on the afternoon of August 30, 2019 by issuing such regulations. The meeting was also attended by Deputy Commanders, Deputy Chiefs of Staff, Heads of Departments, Offices and Local Commanders in Municipalities, Districts, and many other security headquarters.
Brigadier General Kang Sao Kun said that although the crackdown on natural resource crime in Preah Vihear province has resulted in the burning of cars and bulldozers, as well as other equipment used to transport illegal timber. Despite the illegal logging business, some traders have not been able to comply with the law, instead they continue to do so in secret.
In this case, the Commander of the Preah Vihear Provincial Gendarmerie instructed all the Armed Forces to pay more attention to cracking down on natural resource crimes by cracking down on illegal traders and illegal business locations in The bases of their respective bases, in general, must be determined to strictly follow the orders of General Sao Sokha with high efficiency.
At the same time, Brigadier General Kang Sao Kun advised all forces to be highly prepared to rescue people in case of disasters. In particular, on the occasion of the upcoming Pchum Ben festival, to participate in protecting security and order at pagodas so that people can go to the candle ceremony safely and warmly.
