According to Donald Trump, although tariff plans will be implemented, US and Chinese officials are still discussing trade issues between the two countries. The Trump administration recently announced a decision to raise tariffs to 15 percent on $ 300 billion worth of Chinese goods, with half of them set to take effect on September 1 and the other half extended. December 15.
In addition, the United States will raise tariffs to 30 percent on another $ 250 billion Chinese goods, which will take effect on October 10. China has also announced a $ 75 billion tariff increase on US goods, which will be implemented in two separate packages, similar to China's $ 300 billion tariff increase.
For US goods in the first package, tariffs will be increased by 10 percent on September 1, while tariffs on US goods in the second package will be applied on December 15 at 5 percent. China, meanwhile, decided to renew its 25 percent tariff on US cars and 5 percent on spare parts on Dec. 15 after the project was suspended.
Donald Trump has confirmed his administration's new tariff plan on Chinese goods after US companies urged him to scrap the plan because it would hurt them and many experts. He warned of the consequences for Americans, especially low-income people and US importers.
