(Phnom Penh): The report shows that in recent months, the number of tourists visiting Siem Reap has decreased compared to previous years. A report by the Angkor Foundation shows that in July, nearly 150,000 visitors visited Angkor, a drop of nearly 20 percent from 2018. In the first seven months of 2019, it received nearly 1.4 million visitors, but this number decreased by more than 10 percent compared to the same period in 2018.
Mr. Phillip Kao, President of Siem Reap Tourism Club, said that the drop in tourists during the Low Season has been common for many years. But this year 2019 is different from previous years. The president of the Siem Reap Tourism Club claims that there are currently about 20,000 hotel rooms in Siem Reap, but only between two and three thousand guests per night, leaving many hotel rooms.
Mr. Phillip Kao requested the Royal Government of Cambodia and relevant ministries to help find a better mechanism to respond to the fall. Kao wants the government to waive visa fees for tourists, an approach that ASEAN members and other countries are implementing to attract visitors. He also wants to facilitate open access for guests in neighboring countries such as Thailand and Laos to drive to Siem Reap.
Phillip Kao also wants to create programs and events to attract guests.
To know more about the concerns and suggestions of the tour operators in Siem Reap during this visit, please watch the interview between Mr. Van Say and Mr. Phillip Kao, President of the Siem Reap Tourism Club: "Study of technical skills and labor market needs" as a topic. Interview with Fresh News TV's "Special Guest of the Week" broadcast on Monday, September 2nd!
