The General Department of Taxation issues a press release on the application for stamp duty on the transfer of ownership within the relatives who receive tax preferences.
At the same time, the General Department of Taxation requests all property owners to fulfill their obligation to register and file tax returns every year on two other types of taxes: property tax or land tax, which is not used properly and in a timely manner if the property That is obliged to pay taxes.
The statement said that in case the property owner fails to file the tax return in the past, the procedure for reviewing the exemption or preferential tax stamp for the transfer of ownership or possession of the property within the relatives. The above will take time to check the fulfillment of property tax obligations or unused land tax.
In addition, the property will be subject to the payment of taxes, surcharges and interest at the same time as the application for stamp duty.
Separately, for real estate owned by legal entities (companies), there are also other tax debts, and if the company has tax debts, they will be required to pay those tax debts before they can be stamped.
