ASEAN and partners agree to continue to set anti-drug goals
(Siem Reap): August 28-30, 2019, as scheduled, the 40th ASEAN Senior Officials' Meeting on Drugs, hosted and chaired by Cambodia, has concluded. The meeting was chaired by General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, with the participation of representatives from ASEAN, China, Japan, Korea, Russia, India and UNODC.
On that occasion, General Meas Virith proudly stated that as the host of the 40th ASEAN Senior Officials' Meeting on Drugs (ASOD), it went smoothly and with deep meaning. Some, as well as challenges that arise within the framework of drug control within the jurisdiction of ASEAN member states.
On that occasion, General Meas Virith also said that the meeting noted the following issues:
* First, the drug situation related to cultivation, production, and drug trafficking continued to occur, and drug prices fell sharply, while the drug market was noted that there was no such reduction in prices. At the production site.
* Third, the widespread use of methamphetamine in the form of ecstasy crystals from Europe and the increasing use of methamphetamine and new drugs.
* Fourth: Drug criminals have the support of illegal armed groups to prevent them from cultivating and producing drugs.
* Fifth, the increase in the production of ATS synthetic drugs based on the import of chemical compounds to the source of production, with the import of chemical compounds into the production area of both illegal and illegal chemical compounds. And the shift from legal trade to illegal drug production sites, leading to an increase in the price of cheap synthetic drugs.
