Anti-Counterfeiting Committee Chairman Tells Officials Not to Use Counterfeit Products
(Phnom Penh): General Miech Sophanna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Chairman of the Committee for Combating Counterfeit Products that pose a high risk to health and social safety (CPPCC) on August 30, 2019. Told all its officials that it is strictly forbidden to use counterfeit goods.
This statement was made on the occasion that General Miech Sophanna presided over the ceremony to announce the composition of the CPP, which was attended by the leaders of relevant ministries and institutions as Undersecretary of State, Deputy Director General, Director of Departments, members. This morning, August 30, 2019, the CPP and representatives of embassies in Cambodia, NGOs and the private sector.
General Miech Sophanna stated, "It is strictly forbidden for the members of the committee as well as the officials in the committee ... If we work in the committee to fight counterfeit products, we should not use counterfeit products because if we use The counterfeit goods themselves are gone, how can we crack down on counterfeits? ”
"We must use the real thing to respect intellectual property, as well as to respect those who use ingenuity, innovation, investment of time and money to launch a branded product," said the chairman of the Anti-Counterfeiting Committee.
He also pointed out that the production and circulation of counterfeit products, which are spreading from day to day almost everywhere today, is considered a crime organized by the organization and a transnational crime. Seriously affect public health and endanger humanity.
Mr. Miech Sophanna raised three important points to participate in the orientation of policies and activities against counterfeit products, including:
In this regard, he said, training, education, and dissemination of anti-counterfeiting campaigns are indispensable in order to make people better understand the impact of using counterfeit products and to provide information to the committee. Committee.
3. In the fight against counterfeit products, no institution or organization or country can successfully carry out this work alone until there is good cooperation in the country, the region and the world to be successful. And effective.
He also requested you, the Vice Chairpersons of all committee members, to continue good cooperation in all activities under all circumstances, which will enable Cambodian society to eliminate counterfeit products that pose a high risk to health and social safety. Successfully.
He praised the committee's efforts in the past, cracking down on and seizing hundreds of tons of counterfeit products, destroying them and sending the suspects to court for some prison sentences. Also.
He said that in many of the results achieved, do not forget about an important event is the celebration of the regional conference on "the fight against counterfeit and substandard drugs" at the end of 2018 in the presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen Director The Minister of Cambodia, supported and invited by international delegates and dignitaries from France, China, Myanmar, Thailand, Laos and Vietnam.
A total of 450 representatives from relevant ministries and institutions of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the private sector participated in the discussion to share experiences on the fight against counterfeit and substandard drugs encountered in their respective countries. How to find solutions to prevent and eliminate effectively.
