Ministry of Labor Continues Campaign to Prevent Child Labor in Brick Making in Kandal Province
(Central): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training continues its campaign to prevent the use of child labor in brick-making handicrafts in order to promote and prevent the use of child labor in the brick-and-mortar sector and to monitor the implementation of working conditions in the brick-and-mortar sector. At various brick handicraft sites in Kandal province.
The ministry's leaders have stated that this measure is a fierce measure for artisans who continue to use child labor in their handicrafts without exception and without understanding.
The campaign started on August 26, 2019 under the leadership of Mr. Veng Heang, Director of the Department of Child Labor of the Ministry of Labor and Mr. Thul Neang, Director of the Department of Labor of Kandal Province, accompanied by National and Provincial Labor Inspectors.
Mr. Veng Heang confirmed that the general working conditions of the 20 handicrafts in Muk Kampul district saw significant progress.
The team also interviewed employers, employees and families living in the brick kiln to monitor awareness on child labor prevention, improve education and vocational training opportunities for vulnerable children and young workers, especially the situation assessment. Debts of families involved in brick production activities.
