Mr. Phay Siphan confirmed that the draft law on construction was first drafted in 2017 by professional officials of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and with input and input from experts of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure. Transport and tourism of Japan.
This draft law was sent to the Office of the Council of Ministers on 16 July 2019 and submitted to the Technical Meeting with the Legal Council and the Economic and Cultural Council of the Office of the Council of Ministers on the 23rd, 24th and 25th. July 2019 and inter-ministerial meeting on 6 and 7 August 2019.
The Ministry of Justice has helped to revise a number of articles in the relevant chapters and provisions to ensure consistency with other applicable laws of the Kingdom of Cambodia. The draft law was also submitted to the Supreme Advisory Council on August 13, 2019.
The draft law on construction has the following objectives and benefits:
* Strengthen the management of all stakeholders and operations in the construction sector to ensure security, safety and public order, protect the interests of construction owners, consumers and the public.
* Participate in strengthening urban management by developing the city to be beautiful and good environment for sustainable living to promote public welfare
* Increase accountability and efficiency in construction and professionalism in the construction sector
* Increase investor confidence in the construction sector, promote real estate market, socio-economic efficiency.
The objectives of this draft law include:
* Quality, security, safety, construction, work, property and well-being of construction owners, construction users and the public * Aesthetics and good environment for sustainable living aimed at promoting public well-being * Accountability and efficiency in work and construction professionals * Increasing investment confidence in the construction sector and boosting the real estate market economically and socially.
Mr. Phay Siphan affirmed that the construction sector has played a role as a pillar with three other pillars that promote growth: tourism, agriculture and industry by participating in the organization and development of infrastructure in both the public and private sectors, especially industrial production, handicrafts and trade. Agriculture, services and tourism, as well as participate in the development of housing and other structures to serve the lives of people safely and comfortably.
Over the last decade, investment in the construction sector has grown steadily and continues to grow, especially in the construction of high-rise buildings such as condominiums, shopping malls, shopping malls, business centers, office buildings, hotels, multi-functional buildings, construction. Satellite city, housing, villa, educational institution, hospital, bank, factory, warehouse, gas station, etc.
