The purpose of this national conference is to share experiences on the management of genocide-related archives. The conference will allow the Tuol Sleng Museum of Genocide:
First, network with national institutions that are active in the history of the Khmer Rouge and peacebuilding initiatives, and with similar institutions around the world. Second, to change the international perspective on the ethical challenges brought about by digitalizing the archives related to the genocide / genocide.
The national conference was organized as part of the "Project on the Preservation and Integration of Tuol Sleng Museum Archives into a Computer System" funded by KOICA.
This national conference is part of a three-day international conference on "Genocide, Memory and Peace" to be held in Phnom Penh from 28 to 30 August 2019 . The conference was organized by the Tuol Sleng Genocide Museum (TSGM), Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts of Cambodia, with support from KICA and UNESCO.
