He said that in the above meeting, the Ministry of Tourism, the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, the Cambodian Chefs Association, the Cambodian Restaurant Association, the Cambodian School of Tourism, the Confucius Institute, tourism researchers and other stakeholders agreed to set up a technical committee to prepare a glossary. Which is right to improve the quality, improve the food sector in Cambodia and reduce mistakes in writing this menu and so on.
He said that once the lexicon is finalized, the Ministry of Tourism will integrate restaurants and canteens by training trainers and representatives of various business establishments to make the implementation more accurate. Air India ready to stop using plastic products during flights
According to Air India, the 200 ml plastic water bottle will be replaced immediately, offering a larger capacity of 1,500 ml and not made of plastic. Forks, spoons and knives, plastic and cakes, as well as food wrapped in plastic will be discontinued from October 2 and replaced with wooden materials, while food packaging is paper.
In mid-August, on the occasion of India's Independence Day, Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi said the elimination of the use of disposable plastic products was a major goal and he called on the people India together contributes to this goal.
According to the Indian government, India produces about 5.6 million tons of plastic waste each year. In Mumbai and New Delhi, the use of plastic products is banned, but not strictly enforced.
The private security sector is considered as an important sector in participating in maintaining security and social order.
(Phnom Penh): The General Commission of the National Police, which has the Department of Private Security Management as its secretary, considers the private security sector as an important sector that has actively contributed to maintaining security, social order, as well as protecting national interests and national development. .
This was stated by Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Department of Private Security Management, on the evening of August 29, 2019, on the occasion of the invitation of Lt. Gen. Dy Vichea, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, at the Closing Ceremony of the Private Security Agency Training Course. 20th, with about 200 participants.
The Director of the Department of Private Security Management emphasized that the protection of social security is the duty of all citizens to work together to prevent and suppress all crimes in all forms for the safety of the people as well as tourists. National and international who are also in Cambodia.
At this point, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey confirmed to all participants that private security agencies have a role not only in protecting private property or private enterprises, but also in obliging to protect public property, social security and the lives of citizens. Also, in particular, serves as an important support force to the competent authorities.
He claimed that if private security agents saw or suspected any illegal activity, whether in their standing position or where, they should immediately report it to the nearest competent authority or to the Department of Private Security Management directly. Also through the phone number provided.
