Please be informed that Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng's remarks are in response to questions from journalists who asked how the authorities will prepare after Sam Rainsy announced that he will return to Cambodia soon. This was said on November 9, 2019. 40th ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly, successfully hosted by Thai Parliament
The 40th ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly, hosted by the Thai Parliament on August 25, successfully concluded on the morning of August 29, 2019. After Thailand hosts the event next year, the 41st IPA General Assembly of Vietnam will host it again from August 25 to 30, 2020 in Halong.
The Women's Parliamentary Committee (WAIPA) has adopted two resolutions on the promotion of gender equality and women's empowerment in the ASEAN community and the gender gap in technological regulations.
The Economic Committee adopted four resolutions on the theme of promoting economic development in the ASEAN Community, improving ASEAN cooperation in the context of the Fourth Industrial Revolution, and supporting small and medium enterprises. .
The Social Affairs Commission has adopted six resolutions on improving social services for the elderly and strengthening the safety of tourism. The organizing committee discussed 17 resolutions on strengthening the activities of the AIPA Secretariat and its partners.
The 40th IPA General Assembly met with observer countries such as Australia, Canada, China, Russia, the Republic of Korea under the theme "Partnership for Good Law Enforcement".
Chhuon Ly Phay, President of the 40th AIPA Parliament and President of the Thai Parliament It is an important mechanism for implementation in each country to build solidarity, good cooperation within the ASEAN family, as well as a world of peace and sustainable development.
He stressed that in the context of the current regional and global challenges, solidarity and good cooperation are the key to finding happiness and development for the people through their representatives. He hopes that the complex issues of climate change, extremism, trade competition and the solution can be resolved through the strengthening of cooperation between IPA and ASEAN.
Please be informed that the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) is an inter-parliamentary organization representing the legislatures of the 10 member countries of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN): Brunei, Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, Myanmar, Singapore, Thailand, Vietnam and Philippines. AIPA is a gathering of the voices of the people of the ASEAN Community as ASEAN partners in promoting the achievement of the ASEAN Community.
The 40th ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly will be held in the Kingdom of Thailand from 25 to 30 August 2019 under the theme "Promoting Parliamentary Partnership for Sustainable Communities."
Thai PM tells some rich people not to 'pretend to be poor' to get social security card
(Bangkok): Thai Prime Minister Prayuth Chan-o-cha has called on some rich people in Thailand not to steal welfare cards from the poor because it is a violation of their rights. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Thursday afternoon, August 29, 2019.
According to the Prime Minister, those who have their own large houses and land or have some money in their bank account are not considered poor by the state, so they should not apply for a welfare card. "Some rich people want welfare cards like the poor, on the pretext that they have no money in the bank, as they have large villas and large plots of land that belong to them," Prayuth said. "
As many as 14.6 million low-income Thais have been granted social security cards by the Thai government, each of whom can withdraw 500 baht in cash, or about $ 16.33 a month. This and another 500 baht for next month to facilitate their living to some extent.
