Sharing the Six Important Recommendations of the Royal Government of Cambodia by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense The 14th and related meetings in Siem Reap this morning, August 29, 2019.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh said that in order to promote economic growth and social development with the direction for the future of the welfare of the ASEAN community is all healthier, Samdech would like to share some recommendations to the following ceremonies:
First, all ASEAN member countries must work together to improve and promote the implementation of activities to better harmonize the health sector in the ASEAN region as a whole by reducing the gap in the quality of health services.
Second, ASEAN must be jointly prepared to respond to public health disasters, especially outbreaks of infectious diseases in the ASEAN region, and disasters caused by climate change.
Third, ASEAN must work together to reduce the gaps in medical technology by complementing each other with shortcomings, building capacity, technology, modern technology and human resources, especially to develop knowledge and technical skills in accordance with the standards. International and modern technology to provide services to people with high efficiency and reliability.
Fourth, ASEAN must engage with all stakeholders in the health sector, share information, knowledge, experience, technology and technology on a regular basis to find the necessary methods and requirements for timely response to disasters in ASEAN countries and Local.
Fifth, ASEAN must work together to combat counterfeit and substandard medicines through cross-sectoral cooperation, further strengthening the legal framework, enhancing the capacity of technical officers to conduct ongoing research, and continuing to strengthen good governance mechanisms.
Sixth, ASEAN must work with development partners and the World Health Organization to promote the implementation of existing regional and global mechanisms and develop new mechanisms or guidelines for health sector harmonization and technical support. And funding for the prevention of counterfeit and substandard medicines.
Please be informed that this ASEAN Health Ministers' Meeting focused on four main topics: 1: Fighting against counterfeit and substandard medicines, 2: Ensuring the sustainability of financing health care services, 3: Strengthening the capacity to Implement the International Health Regulations of the World Health Organization; and 4: Innovations to strengthen health care services.
The meeting was attended by the Health Ministers of the 10 ASEAN Member States, ASEAN Plus Three (China, Japan, Korea), the ASEAN Secretary-General and about 300 accompanying delegates.
