75 families in Pak Klang commune, Koh Kong province who have not had access to clean water for more than 30 years now have access to clean water
(Koh Kong): Mr. Khlum Koki, Director of the Department of Industry and Handicraft of Koh Kong Province, on the afternoon of August 28, 2019, led his subordinates and local officials to inspect the water shortage after the people raised in the 23rd public forum. August is located in Thmey Cham Yeam village, Pak Klang commune, Mondul Seima district. The people there have not used clean water for more than 30 years.
One resident said that they had been living in Spean Yol village for more than 30 years and did not have enough clean water from year to year. All water consumption is bought from a broker at a price of 5,000 riel per cubic meter (five thousand riel) and not enough for household use.
"Seeing the difficulties of lack of clean water and electricity for many years, all 75 families have decided to raise these two issues in a public forum to ask the relevant officials to help solve them. "Because when they run out of water, they are forced to use water from wells."
Mr. Khlum Koki, Director of the Provincial Department of Industry and Handicrafts, said that he was satisfied with the people's suggestions about the lack of clean water for the 75 families at the above point, because if they did not raise it, the department would not know because it did not. There is no local authority to report to the department.
