Ministry of Water Resources: From today to September 3, Cambodia may have a lot of rain, please people beware of wind, thunder, lightning and flooding
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a notification on the weather in Cambodia from today to September 3, 2019, stating that during this period, Cambodia will have moderate to heavy rain, especially in the provinces. Next to the sea.
At the same time, the Ministry called on people to be very careful about the phenomenon of rain, wind, thunder, lightning and floods caused by heavy rain, as well as the flood of the Mekong River continues to rise.
This morning, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh opened the 14th ASEAN Health Ministers' Meeting in Siem Reap.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health of Cambodia, as the host and rotating chair of the ASEAN Health Ministers, will chair the 14th ASEAN Health Ministers' Meeting and related meetings from 26 to 30 August 2019 at Siem Reap Province. This is according to a press release from the Ministry of Health, obtained by Fresh News.
The meeting is held every two years on a rotating basis, which includes: 1: Preparatory Meeting of ASEAN Health Ministers, ASEAN Plus Three and ASEAN-China, and 2: Meeting of ASEAN Health Ministers, ASEAN Plus Three and ASEAN-China under the chairmanship. "Promoting the Health of All ASEAN People"
The meeting will focus on four main topics: 1: Fighting counterfeit and substandard medicines, 2: Ensuring the sustainability of health care financing, and 3: Strengthening the organization's capacity to implement international health regulations. Global Health and 4: Innovations to strengthen health care services.
The meeting was attended by the Health Ministers of the 10 ASEAN Member States, ASEAN Plus Three (China, Japan, Korea), the ASEAN Secretary-General and about 300 accompanying delegates. The meeting will also discuss and approve some key priority agendas.
Speaking to Fresh News tonight, Mr. Chhim Phal Varun, Secretary General of the Supreme Advisory Council, said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen's praise for Mr. Yun Min was made in a meeting with members of the Supreme Council. Consult and advise to review the one-year work of this institution to find points to improve and enhance the work efficiency of the Supreme Advisory Council.
Although he did not remember the original words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Mr. Chhim Phal Varun can only confirm that Samdech Techo Prime Minister really praised Mr. Yun Min, the former Governor of Sihanoukville, who dared to resign while The mayor of Paris did not dare to do this.
It should be informed that after the collapse of a 7-storey building at dawn on June 22, 2019, which caused dozens of deaths and injuries, Mr. Yun Min, who was the Governor of Sihanoukville at that time. Request Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to resign in order to acknowledge the mistakes that have been made.
After agreeing to allow Mr. Min to resign, Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to appoint Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, who was then the Governor of Kampong Cham, to be the Governor of Sihanoukville. Separately, Mr. Yun Min was promoted by Samdech Techo to the rank of General and has the role of Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense. Chinese Embassy in Cambodia Releases Guidelines for Chinese Tourists to Understand Cambodia's Traditional Culture and Laws
(Phnom Penh): To contribute to attracting Chinese tourists and show Chinese tourists to understand the culture, traditions, customs and traditions of the Cambodian people. The Chinese Embassy in Cambodia has issued guidelines or "compasses for Chinese people to come to Cambodia" for Chinese people visiting Cambodia.
The launch of the "Compass for Chinese People to Cambodia" is in response to the growing number of Chinese tourists coming to Cambodia, with the Chinese Embassy expecting 3 million Chinese tourists to come to Cambodia. In the coming 2020.
The Ambassador of the People's Republic of China made the remarks at a press conference on "Day of Consular Services and" Compass for Chinese Citizens Coming to Cambodia "at the International Airport on the evening of August 28. 2019. With the participation of Mr. Hor Sarun, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia.
In response to the increase in the number of tourists and the promotion of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, Mr. Hor Sarun, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Tourism, said that Cambodia welcomes and is ready to receive the growing number of Chinese tourists. Ascending. The reception for Chinese tourists has been organized by the Ministry of Tourism since 2016 to make it easier for Chinese tourists to visit Cambodia.
After being ready to receive Chinese tourists since 2016 and improving relations between Cambodia and China, Cambodia achieved an increase of about 11% with the arrival of tourists. More than 6.2 million international people and bring about 4.356 million US dollars to the national economy in 2018. Of which, more than 2 million Chinese tourists out of the total international tourists.
