Oknha Kouch Mengly Donates 90 Folding Armchairs to Koh Rok Ko Primary School, Phnom Kravanh District, Pursat Province
(Pursat): Mr. Oknha Dr. Kouch Mengly, CEO of Mengly J. Kouch Education Company through Mengly J. Foundation. Kouch provided 90 folding armchairs to Koh Rok Ko Primary School in Angkor Village, Samrong Commune, Phnom Kravanh District, Pursat Province.
The handover took place on August 27, 2019. The primary school has 3 classrooms with over 80 students.
Oknha Dr. Kouch Mengly said that this is the second time that the Mengly J Foundation. Kouch distributes charitable gifts as study materials to students in this remote area. On May 3, 2019, he donated a water pump, three blackboards and some study materials as well as student uniforms.
Every rainy season, the students of Koh Rok Ko Primary School face many difficulties, such as the road to school is far and slippery. While studying, it may rain if it rains. The school does not yet have a bathroom or a swimming pool. Not only that, there is no electricity yet.
Oknha Dr. Kouch Mengly added, "Most of us build the whole building, including the library, appliances, tables, cabinets, blackboards, bathrooms, wells, gardens, street paintings." Now there are 2 schools and 10 schools are asking me because my goal is to have one school in each province, a school that is in dire need. ”
Please note that the geographical area of Koh Rok Ko Primary School has not been divided into all the villages because it is too big, it is up to 54 kilometers from Samrong commune in Phnom Kravanh district. After placing 90 chairs in the classroom of the primary school, the team discussed the project to build a bathroom for boys and girls with the principal and the commune chief to know the budget for the construction.
