SCG Conference on Sustainable Development focuses on plastic waste in ASEAN
(Thailand): SCG, one of the leading corporations in ASEAN, has partnered with 44 partner institutions from government, public and private sectors, both in Thailand and abroad, to host regional development conferences. Sustainable, focusing on the problem of plastic waste in ASEAN.
This year's Regional Conference on Sustainable Development marks the 10th anniversary and will be held under the theme "Cooperation for Action" to build all-round cooperation that will be a driving force for the creation of a circular economy. In Thailand and to achieve sustainable development goals.
The conference was attended by more than 1,500 participants, including company presidents and senior government officials, medium and large enterprises, intellectuals, NGOs and national and international journalists. Fresh News and nine other Cambodian journalists were also invited by SCG to participate in the event.
The purpose of this conference is to find a solution to the crisis of resource scarcity through the implementation of the circular economy strategy, namely "most efficient use of resources, proper waste separation and disposal" to ensure the efficiency of resources in During the entire production and consumption cycle.
The cooperation aims to create a sustainable industry, combat pollution by plastic litter in the sea, improve community livelihoods and manage industrial waste.
"Data show that the average Thai per capita produces 1.15 kilograms of garbage, and the rate of waste generation is increasing," he said. In 2018 alone, Thailand will produce about 28 million tons of waste.
"Therefore, the concept of a circular economy is a solution to alleviate these problems, because this concept promotes the principle of production, consumption and lice," he said. "The concept also incorporates the principles of efficient use of resources, waste separation and proper disposal to conserve natural resources for future generations."
Please be informed that in recent years, SCG has established cooperation with many partners to achieve the principle of circular economy and solve the problem of waste and garbage.
These include: 1: Cooperation for a Sustainable Industry, 2: Cooperation to tackle marine litter, 3: Cooperation to improve the quality of life of people in the community, and 4 : Cooperation for industrial waste management. Dr. Mao Ha Vannal Continues Study Tour of Civil Aviation University of China
On August 28, 2019, Dr. Mao Hovannal, Minister in Charge of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, and his delegation continued their visit and discussion with Prof. Dong Chean Kan, Director of the Aviation University of China and university leaders.
This visit is to learn about the establishment of the Civil Aviation University, to gain experience in management and to explore the possibility of sending professional and young Cambodian officials to study and strengthen the capacity of this university as well.
Dr. stated that the training of human resources in the field of civil aviation is the main existence for the replacement of professional officers who will retire and meet the growing needs of the civil aviation sector in Cambodia under the leadership and guidance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Please note that China Civil Aviation University is a national university under the direct control of the Civil Aviation Administration of China. Founded in 1951, the university employs more than 3,000 professors and researchers and teaches all subjects related to civil aviation, from technical to doctoral.
Under the full cooperation from the field of civil aviation, Cambodia and China can arrange to send Cambodian students to study at the University of Civil Aviation.
