(Phnom Penh): A woman was seen getting off a plane at Phnom Penh International Airport flying from China and she was walking in an awkward position when the airport staff questioned her and found out that she had a mental disorder. It is suspected that she was abused to become such a person for cheating brokers to sell and work in China.
The woman got off the plane at 1 am on August 28, 2019 at the Phnom Penh International Airport until the morning when she reported to the Kacap 1 police to pick her up for questioning and search for relatives.
Authorities said the woman did not have a passport or identity card, only a letter sent to her by the Chinese side in some Chinese and English characters. In the letter, she is named Ton Sophoan, 32 years old, but does not know where she lives in the village, commune, district, province.
When questioned, she did not remember where she lived, but said she had cheated a broker to sell in China five months ago and had been severely abused. Police are now searching for her family to take her back home, but do not know if found or not yet. Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, August 28: More than 2,000 illegal vehicles found and more than 1,503 fined
