One year ago, the Supreme Advisory Council collected 295 issues, submitted to Samdech Techo 251 times
(Phnom Penh): In the past one year, members of the Supreme Advisory Council have led 295 meetings with the people, including 200 secretariat officials as observers, and raised those issues. Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia 251 times.
This is according to the report of the Supreme Advisory Council in the conference to present the results of the meeting of the Supreme Advisory Council on the afternoon of August 28, 2019 at the Office of the Council of Ministers.
According to the 12-month report of the Supreme Advisory Council, the Secretariat also submitted the report of the party delegation along with its summary report to Samdech Techo Hun Sen through 90 permanent Deputy Prime Ministers.
It should be informed that the Supreme Advisory Council was established by Royal Decree dated September 6, 2018 at the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen after the 6th National Election. The Supreme Advisory Council is composed of 16 of the 20 political parties that participated in the election.
