Minister Thong Khon Proposes Airlines to Establish Aviation Association to Expand Flight to Major Destinations
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, on August 28, 2019, held a meeting with representatives of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, airlines in Cambodia and the relevant private sector, requesting these stakeholders to jointly consider the establishment of "Association Aviation ”to participate in the promotion and expansion of direct flights to major tourist destinations around the world.
Mr. Thong Khon said that this is the first time that the expert team of the Ministry of Tourism, the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation and about five airlines in Cambodia have held discussions to improve the quality of tourism services of local airlines, participation, promotion and study. Consult the main tourist destination markets in the area.
During the meeting, Mr. Thong Khon requested the relevant parties to cooperate in establishing an "Aviation Association" to facilitate consultation and resolve issues related to the air travel industry smoothly.
He said that through the establishment of this association will encourage airlines to provide good services and address a number of challenges, including: the organization of local flight magazines, videos from Cambodia, announcements on the plane. Multilingual in line with passenger type, notification of delays and avoid frequent flight deletions.
At the same time, domestic airlines have also requested the relevant authorities to consider tax reductions related to landings at international airports and to intervene to some destination countries regarding flight and landing times.
Please note that Cambodia is currently connecting direct flights to Thailand, Vietnam, Laos, the Philippines, Indonesia, Singapore, Malaysia, Myanmar, ASEAN plus three Arab countries.
On that occasion, the Minister also urged airlines to study the connection of additional direct flights from Phnom Penh, Siem Reap and Sihanoukville to major tourist destinations, including Beijing and the main provinces of the People's Republic of China. With the Consulate General of Cambodia stationed there and potential tourist destinations.
Destinations in Japan include Tokyo, Osaka, Fukuoka, while destinations in India include New Delhi, Calcutta, Assam. Apart from that, there are also tourist destinations in South Korea, Sri Lanka and so on.
Minister Thong Khon requested the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, airlines in Cambodia, as well as the relevant private sector to hold regular meetings with the Ministry of Tourism.
Experts say raising tariffs on Chinese imports could endanger US children's safety
NEW YORK (Reuters) - The recent US government increase in tariffs on Chinese products will put American society at greater risk, especially children, experts say. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Wednesday afternoon, August 28, 2019.
Rising prices for baby products imported from China due to the US government will make some American parents, especially those on low incomes, unable to afford adequate beds for their children, which means that children In a dangerous situation.
Mr Shami explained that many children's furniture products would be affected by the 25 percent tariff increase, with Americans spending more to buy toys, car seats, rubber and other essentials for child safety.
Therefore, experts see that it puts the infants and children of poor families at great risk, sometimes putting their children to bed with them or using a crib. Poor quality, which can seriously affect a child's sleep.
According to a study, if children share a bed with their parents, they will face more risks, including suffocation, insomnia, insomnia and other serious risks, as many as 3,700 children. People die every year in the United States due to sleep-related causes.
