(Preah Vihear): A suspect who is the father of animals was arrested by the police force of Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province immediately after the man raped his 9-year-old daughter.
The suspect was arrested on the afternoon of August 27, 2019 in Anlong Veng village, Kantuot commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province.
This morning, August 28, 2019, Lieutenant Colonel Ou Seng, Police Inspector of Choam Ksan District, Preah Vihear Province, said that the suspect who was detained by the police was named Min Phea, male, 35 years old, farmer. The victim was a 9-year-old schoolgirl living together in the same commune.
Choam Ksan District Inspector continued that before the incident, the victim was playing in front of the house, while the stepfather who was working in the backyard shouted for the victim to help and also arrested. The rape was carried out until there was blood on the grass at the scene.
Mr. O Seng continued that because he saw that his daughter was anemic, the girl's mother was taken to the hospital with suspicion. At that time, the girl told her mother about her stepfather's actions. The girl's mother then immediately complained to the authorities and arrested the suspect.
The suspect is currently being investigated by the Choam Ksan District Police and sent to the Preah Vihear Provincial Police for legal action.
Senior Minister Kun Kim Inspects Homes for Veterans in Oddar Meanchey Province's Chong Kal District and Tells Homeless Members Can Apply
(Oddar Meanchey): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, this morning, August 28, 2019, continued to inspect the construction of houses for Cambodian veterans in Chong Kal District, Oddar Meanchey Province to prepare for the completion of about 200 houses at the end. December 2019 is coming.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, during a visit this morning, said that so far, the process of building houses for Cambodian veterans to live in Chongkal district, Oddar Meanchey province has been completed about 150 houses. Mr. Kun Kim added that among the completed houses, the association has also gradually handed over to members to stay.
The Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association confirmed that for more than 200 houses built in Chongkal district to be distributed to members of the veterans who have a difficult life, no land, no real home to live.
According to Kun Kim, 100 houses in this area will be handed over to 100 families of veterans in Phnom Penh, while the remaining 50 houses will be handed over to Oddar Meanchey province and some other provinces with homeless members. And volunteer to live in this area with subsistence farming.
In addition to providing land and houses for accommodation, the Cambodian Veterans Association, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, also handed over 2 hectares of land for a family to grow crops. This is according to Senior Minister Kun Kim.
In addition, Senior Minister Kun Kim called on members of the Veterans Association in all provinces who do not have real houses and land to apply to the Commission of the Cambodian Veterans Association for the purpose of allocating and handing over land and housing for compensation. What the veterans sacrificed for the motherland.
At the same time, the people who are the families of Cambodian veterans also expressed their excitement and deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who always pays attention. Put to their well-being and living, who build houses and provide additional land for cultivation.
It should be informed that the people who are the families of Cambodian veterans after receiving the house and land have made their daily life seem to be better as they can grow more crops on the land that the Veterans Association Cambodian fighters handed over and in addition to what the Royal Government handed over to the series. Tomorrow, NEA has 700 more job opportunities waiting for students and job seekers.
