Mr. Seng Kimlak, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, issued a second summons to Sam Rainsy, the leader of the illegal opposition group, on the morning of August 28, 2019. This order was made on August 5, 2019 and was taken to the house of Mr. Sam Rainsy in Sangkat Chak Angre, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh this morning, August 12, 2019.
In connection with this incitement case, in the past, the representative of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court has summoned Sam Rainsy, who is fleeing the district, to appear for questioning on July 31, 2019, but he did not respond. No court summons.
The lawsuit comes after prisoner Sam Rainsy posted a distorted message about Hok Lundy's death. Mr. Sam Rainsy slandered Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the killer of Mr. Hok Lundy and lied that Mr. Dy Vichea, the son of Mr. Hok Lundy, was now plotting revenge with the support of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, on July 8, 2019, confirmed that the recent filing of a lawsuit against Sam Rainsy, the leader of the extremist opposition group, in court was Samdech's first complaint in a single stage. This life.
Samdech stated that the filing of the lawsuit against Sam Rainsy is a wake-up call for some politicians to adhere to the dignity, morality and virtue of the profession, to avoid fabricating information to incite, inspire, maliciously slander and divide to fulfill. Its unjust purpose and ambition and its group.
